  ],
  "notes": "All five Section 6.1 covenants are conjoined pointwise. Thresholds are encoded as stated: Leverage <= 3.0 (violation only if greater), Interest Coverage >= 3.0 (violation only if less), debt per patient <= 35,000, net worth >= the stated floor, and capex <= 20,000,000. Debt per patient uses division by patient_count, so a zero count is reported by the evaluator as unresolved; no positivity is assumed, and QF_NRA is used for that reason. The net worth floor is computed from two cumulative inputs, the positive net income sum and the equity proceeds sum, because the source gives no state-update rules. Capex is evaluated pointwise using the fiscal-year-to-date amount at each observation. The covenant text has no explicit exceptions or applicability conditions beyond 'at any time' and the stated fiscal year scope."
