      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio as of the end of the fiscal quarter, as a plain ratio (3.00 to 1.00 is 3.0).",
      "source_quote": "Permit the Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio as of the end of any fiscal quarter of the Borrower to be less than 3.00 to 1.00"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is violated if the leverage ratio is greater than 3.50 for quarters ending before 2015-01-31, or greater than 3.00 for quarters ending on or after that date, so compliance is <= 3.5 or <= 3.0 respectively. It is also violated if the interest coverage ratio is less than 3.00, so compliance is >= 3.0. The ratios are atomic inputs because the source does not define them. The covenant applies only while Obligations remain outstanding (with the stated exceptions) and only at fiscal quarter ends. The 'on or after' case is the negation of the 'prior to' flag."
