      "meaning": "Indebtedness of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries on the test date, excluding the portion that constitutes Revolving Loans.",
      "source_quote": "Indebtedness of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries on each date listed below"
    },
    {
      "name": "avg_revolving_in_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Average amount of Revolving Loans, as the portion of Indebtedness, outstanding during the Test Period ending on the test date, with Test Period clause (ii) computed from the Closing Date.",
      "source_quote": "the portion of Indebtedness of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries which constitute Revolving Loans shall be the average amount outstanding during the Test Period ending on such date"
    },
    {
      "name": "senior_indebtedness_excl_revolving",
      "meaning": "Senior Indebtedness of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries on the test date, excluding the portion that constitutes Revolving Loans.",
      "source_quote": "Senior Indebtedness of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries on each date listed below"
    },
    {
      "name": "avg_revolving_in_senior",
      "meaning": "Average amount of Revolving Loans, as the portion of Senior Indebtedness, outstanding during the Test Period ending on the test date, with Test Period clause (ii) computed from the Closing Date.",
      "source_quote": "the portion of Senior Indebtedness of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries which constitute Revolving Loans shall be the average amount outstanding during the Test Period ending on such date"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_ebitda",
      "meaning": "Consolidated EBITDA of the Borrower for the Test Period ending on the test date.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated EBITDA of the Borrower for the Test Period ending on each date listed below"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Pointwise encoding. On each listed quarter-end date from 1998 through 2004, both the Total Leverage Ratio (a) and the Senior Leverage Ratio (b) must be at most the scheduled maximum, so the body is a conjunction of the two. Each numerator is the non-revolving amount plus the average Revolving Loans for the Test Period, per the PROVIDED clauses. The revolving averages are separate inputs for (a) and (b), so the encoding does not assume Revolving Loans are Senior Indebtedness. The schedule is encoded by year and month with ite. Division by zero EBITDA is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. Outside the listed dates the covenant is treated as not applicable at that observation."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; total_debt: Total Debt of the Borrower at the observation time (Section 6.05(a)); units are the same currency units as total_capitalization.\n; total_capitalization: Total Capitalization at the observation time (Section 6.05(a)); same currency units as total_debt.\n; is_four_quarter_period_observation: true iff this observation is one at which a period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Borrower is being tested, i.e. the period ends at this observation (Section 6.05(b)).\n; consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio: Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending at this observation, as a number x for x to 1.0; meaningful when is_four_quarter_period_observation is true.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((total_debt Real) (total_capitalization Real) (is_four_quarter_period_observation Bool) (consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (and\n    ; (a) Total Debt must not exceed 50% of Total Capitalization at any time\n    (<= total_debt (* 0.5 total_capitalization))\n    ; (b) the ratio must not be less than 3.0 to 1.0 for any four-quarter period\n    (=> is_four_quarter_period_observation (>= consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio 3.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "total_debt",
      "meaning": "Total Debt of the Borrower at the observation time, in the same currency units as total_capitalization.",
      "source_quote": "Permit Total Debt to exceed 50% of Total Capitalization at any time"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "Total Capitalization at the observation time, in the same currency units as total_debt.",
      "source_quote": "Permit Total Debt to exceed 50% of Total Capitalization at any time"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_four_quarter_period_observation",
      "meaning": "True iff this observation is the end of a period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Borrower for which the interest coverage test is evaluated.",
      "source_quote": "for any period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Borrower"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio for the four consecutive fiscal quarters ending at the observation, expressed as x for x to 1.0.",
      "source_quote": "Permit the Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio for any period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Borrower to be less than 3.0 to 1.0"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Part (a) applies at every observation (\"at any time\"). It is written as total_debt <= 0.5 * total_capitalization, which is the negation of \"exceed 50%\" and avoids a division. Part (b) is gated by a flag for observations that end a four-quarter period, and the violation condition \"less than 3.0\" becomes >= 3.0 for compliance. The ratio's definition is not supplied, so it stays an atomic Real input. The Required Lenders consent exception and the covenant's term are not modeled as inputs. The source gives no observation-level state for them, and they do not change the pointwise numeric tests."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; operating_cash_flow: Borrower's Operating Cash Flow for the measurement period ending at this observation (3, 6, 9 or 12 months ended per the schedule), on an accrual basis for the first four periods (the 1997 periods).\n; debt_service: Debt Service with respect to Borrower's Obligations for the same measurement period, on an accrual basis for the first four periods.\n; is_period_threshold_1_85: true iff this observation is the end of a scheduled period whose required amount is 1.85: Mar 31, Jun 30, Sep 30 and Dec 31, 1997 (3, 6, 9 and 12 months ended); Mar 31, Jun 30 and Sep 30, 1998; Dec 31, 1999; and Mar 31, Jun 30, Sep 30 and Dec 31 of 2000 and 2001 (twelve months ended).\n; is_period_threshold_1_80: true iff this observation is the end of a scheduled twelve-month period whose required amount is 1.80: Dec 31, 1998; Mar 31, 1999; Jun 30, 1999; or Sep 30, 1999.\n; agent_prior_written_consent: true iff Agent has given prior written consent to the ratio being below the scheduled amount for this period.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((operating_cash_flow Real) (debt_service Real) (is_period_threshold_1_85 Bool) (is_period_threshold_1_80 Bool) (agent_prior_written_consent Bool)) Bool\n  (or agent_prior_written_consent\n      (ite is_period_threshold_1_85\n           (>= (/ operating_cash_flow debt_service) 1.85)\n           (ite is_period_threshold_1_80\n                (>= (/ operating_cash_flow debt_service) 1.80)\n                true))))",
