{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; covenant_active_obligations_outstanding: true iff any Note remains unpaid, or the Loan Commitments remain in effect, or any other amount is owing by Borrower to Administrative Agent or any Bank under the Agreement or any other Loan Document, at the observation time.\n; combined_ebitda: Combined EBITDA, measured as of the most recently ended calendar quarter.\n; fixed_charges: Fixed Charges, measured as of the most recently ended calendar quarter.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((obligations_outstanding Bool) (combined_ebitda Real) (fixed_charges Real)) Bool\n  (=> obligations_outstanding (>= (/ combined_ebitda fixed_charges) 1.4)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "obligations_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True iff, at the observation time, any Note remains unpaid, or the Loan Commitments remain in effect, or any other amount is owing by Borrower to Administrative Agent or any Bank under the Agreement or any other Loan Document.",
      "source_quote": "So long as any of the Notes shall remain unpaid, or the Loan Commitments remain in effect, or any other amount is owing by Borrower to Administrative Agent or any Bank under this Agreement or under any other Loan Document"
    },
    {
      "name": "combined_ebitda",
      "meaning": "Combined EBITDA, measured as of the most recently ended calendar quarter (the numerator of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "The ratio of Combined EBITDA to Fixed Charges, each measured as of the most recently ended calendar quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "fixed_charges",
      "meaning": "Fixed Charges, measured as of the most recently ended calendar quarter (the denominator of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "The ratio of Combined EBITDA to Fixed Charges, each measured as of the most recently ended calendar quarter"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant forbids the ratio from being less than 1.40 to 1.00, so compliance requires ratio >= 1.4 (non-strict). The 'so long as' clause is encoded as the applicability condition obligations_outstanding. The ratio is computed as combined_ebitda / fixed_charges, so a zero fixed_charges is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the division is by a variable. Both inputs are taken as already measured as of the most recently ended calendar quarter, so no separate calendar flag is needed."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; ebit_ltm: EBIT of the Borrower for the most recently ended four fiscal quarter period, as of this observation.\n; interest_expense_ltm: Interest Expense of the Borrower for that same four fiscal quarter period.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (ebit_ltm Real) (interest_expense_ltm Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (>= (/ ebit_ltm interest_expense_ltm) 2.2)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.",
      "source_quote": "as of the end of each fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "ebit_ltm",
      "meaning": "EBIT of the Borrower for the most recently ended four fiscal quarter period, as of this observation.",
      "source_quote": "EBIT for the most recently ended four fiscal quarter period"
    },
    {
      "name": "interest_expense_ltm",
      "meaning": "Interest Expense of the Borrower for the same four fiscal quarter period as ebit_ltm.",
      "source_quote": "Interest Expense for such four fiscal quarter period"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is applied pointwise: at each fiscal quarter-end observation, EBIT divided by Interest Expense must be at least 2.2 (the 2.2 to 1.0 ratio, non-strict). The ratio is kept as a division, as the source defines it, so a zero Interest Expense is reported by the evaluator as unresolved. No positivity assumptions are added. Division by a variable is nonlinear, so the logic is QF_NRA. The introductory clause about Loan Documents remaining in effect is treated as the general duration of the covenant, which the evaluation history covers, and is not encoded as a parameter."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; obligation_outstanding: true iff at the observation time any Advance remains unpaid or any Lender has any Commitment under the agreement (the condition under which Section 5.03 applies).\n; consolidated_ebitda_ltm: Consolidated EBITDA of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries for the period of the four fiscal quarters most recently ended, as of the observation.\n; consolidated_interest_expense_ltm: Consolidated interest expense of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries for that same four-fiscal-quarter period, as reported on the Consolidated statements of income (or comparable statement).\n; consolidated_covenant_debt: Consolidated Covenant Debt of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries as of the observation (as of fiscal quarter end when is_fiscal_quarter_end is true).\n; net_worth: Net Worth of the Borrower as of the observation (as of fiscal quarter end when is_fiscal_quarter_end is true).\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((obligation_outstanding Bool) (consolidated_ebitda_ltm Real) (consolidated_interest_expense_ltm Real) (consolidated_covenant_debt Real) (net_worth Real) (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool)) Bool\n  (=> obligation_outstanding\n      (and\n        ; (a) Interest Coverage Ratio not less than 3.50 : 1.00\n        (>= (/ consolidated_ebitda_ltm consolidated_interest_expense_ltm) 3.5)\n        ; (b) Covenant Debt to Capital not greater than 0.50 : 1.00, measured at each fiscal quarter end\n        (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n            (<= (/ consolidated_covenant_debt (+ consolidated_covenant_debt net_worth)) 0.5)))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "obligation_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True iff at the observation time any Advance remains unpaid or any Lender has any Commitment under the agreement.",
      "source_quote": "So long as any Advance shall remain unpaid or any Lender shall have any Commitment hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_ebitda_ltm",
      "meaning": "Consolidated EBITDA of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries for the four fiscal quarters most recently ended.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated EBITDA of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries for the period of four fiscal quarters most recently ended"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_expense_ltm",
      "meaning": "Consolidated interest expense of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries for the same four-fiscal-quarter period, as reported on the Consolidated statements of income (or comparable statement).",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated interest expense of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries for that period as reported on the Consolidated statements of income (or comparable statement)"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_covenant_debt",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Covenant Debt as of the observation date (the fiscal quarter end when the Debt to Capital test applies).",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Covenant Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_worth",
      "meaning": "Net Worth as of the observation date (the fiscal quarter end when the Debt to Capital test applies).",
      "source_quote": "Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter.",
      "source_quote": "measured as of the end of each fiscal quarter"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Both covenants apply only while an Advance is unpaid or a Commitment exists. The interest coverage test (a) is stated without a quarter-end restriction, so it is applied at every observation. The debt to capital test (b) applies only at fiscal quarter ends. Ratios are written as divisions, so a zero denominator is reported as unresolved by the evaluator. Because of that division by variables, the logic is QF_NRA. No sign or positivity assumptions are added. The definitions of Consolidated EBITDA, Consolidated Covenant Debt and Net Worth were not supplied, so each is an atomic Real input."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; pre_tax_income_four_quarters: Pre-Tax Income from Continuing Operations of the Company for the four fiscal quarters ended on the observation date (currency units).\n; consolidated_interest_expense_four_quarters: Consolidated Interest Expense for the same four fiscal quarters (currency units); denominator of the ratio.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter.\n; any_advance_unpaid: true iff any Advance remains unpaid at the observation time.\n; any_lender_commitment: true iff any Lender has any Commitment under the agreement at the observation time.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((pre_tax_income_four_quarters Real) (consolidated_interest_expense_four_quarters Real) (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (any_advance_unpaid Bool) (any_lender_commitment Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end (or any_advance_unpaid any_lender_commitment))\n      (>= (/ pre_tax_income_four_quarters consolidated_interest_expense_four_quarters) 2.0)))",
  "symbols": [
