{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; covenant_obligations_outstanding: true at this observation if the Company may still borrow hereunder, or the Loans (including any Discretionary Revolving Loan) are not paid in full, or any Letter of Credit has not expired or terminated, or any LC Disbursement has not been reimbursed (Article VIII lead-in period).\n; is_prior_to_dec_31_2005: true if the observation date is strictly before December 31, 2005; false if on or after December 31, 2005.\n; leverage_ratio: the Leverage Ratio at the observation, expressed as a number X meaning X to 1.0.\n; consolidated_operating_cash_flow: Consolidated Operating Cash Flow at the observation, the numerator of the cash-flow-to-interest ratio.\n; consolidated_interest_expense: Consolidated Interest Expense at the observation, the denominator of the cash-flow-to-interest ratio.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((covenant_obligations_outstanding Bool) (is_prior_to_dec_31_2005 Bool) (leverage_ratio Real) (consolidated_operating_cash_flow Real) (consolidated_interest_expense Real)) Bool\n  (=> covenant_obligations_outstanding\n      (and\n        (ite is_prior_to_dec_31_2005\n             (<= leverage_ratio 5.5)\n             (<= leverage_ratio 5.0))\n        (>= (/ consolidated_operating_cash_flow consolidated_interest_expense) 2.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "covenant_obligations_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True at the observation if the Company may still borrow hereunder, or the Loans (including any Discretionary Revolving Loan) are not paid in full, or any Letter of Credit has not expired or terminated, or any LC Disbursement has not been reimbursed.",
      "source_quote": "so long as the Company may borrow hereunder and until payment in full of the Loans"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_prior_to_dec_31_2005",
      "meaning": "True if the observation date is strictly before December 31, 2005; false if it is on or after December 31, 2005.",
      "source_quote": "prior to December 31, 2005"
    },
    {
      "name": "leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Leverage Ratio at the observation, expressed as X for X to 1.0. It is an atomic input because its definition is not supplied.",
      "source_quote": "a Leverage Ratio of not more than"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_operating_cash_flow",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Operating Cash Flow at the observation, the numerator of the cash-flow-to-interest-expense ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Operating Cash Flow"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Expense at the observation, the denominator of the cash-flow-to-interest-expense ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Interest Expense"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Pointwise translation of 'Maintain at all times'. The covenant applies when covenant_obligations_outstanding is true. The leverage cap is 5.5 before December 31, 2005 and 5.0 on or after that date. The coverage ratio is computed as Consolidated Operating Cash Flow divided by Consolidated Interest Expense and must be at least 2.0. A zero denominator is reported as unresolved by the evaluator. QF_NRA is used because the division is by a variable."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; consolidated_leverage_ratio: Consolidated Leverage Ratio of the Company as at the observation date (last day of the fiscal quarter), expressed as a Real X where the ratio is X to 1.0.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: True iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Company.\n; in_initial_period: True iff the fiscal quarter ends during the period from the Closing Date to the day prior to the date that is six months after the Closing Date.\n; in_later_period: True iff the fiscal quarter ends during the period from the date that is six months after the Closing Date and until the Maturity Date.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((consolidated_leverage_ratio Real) (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (in_initial_period Bool) (in_later_period Bool)) Bool\n  (and\n    (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end in_initial_period) (<= consolidated_leverage_ratio 5.5))\n    (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end in_later_period) (<= consolidated_leverage_ratio 4.5))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "consolidated_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Leverage Ratio of the Company as at the observation date (last day of the fiscal quarter), as a Real X meaning X to 1.0. Atomic input because the definition is not supplied.",
      "source_quote": "the Consolidated Leverage Ratio as at the last day of any fiscal quarter of the Company"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Company.",
      "source_quote": "as at the last day of any fiscal quarter of the Company"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_initial_period",
      "meaning": "True iff the fiscal quarter ends during the period from the Closing Date to the day prior to the date that is six months after the Closing Date.",
      "source_quote": "for any fiscal quarter ending during the period from the Closing Date to the day prior to the date that is six months after the Closing Date, 5.5 to 1.0"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_later_period",
      "meaning": "True iff the fiscal quarter ends during the period from the date that is six months after the Closing Date and until the Maturity Date.",
      "source_quote": "for any fiscal quarter ending during the period from the date that is six months after the Closing Date and until the Maturity Date, 4.5 to 1.0"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant forbids permitting a ratio greater than the cap, so compliance means ratio <= 5.5 in the initial period and ratio <= 4.5 in the later period, tested only at fiscal quarter ends. The period flags are supplied as separate inputs, so the six-month boundary and Maturity Date are evaluator-supplied rather than computed. The 'for so long as any Loan or other Obligation remain unpaid' condition is treated as the covenant's general duration and is not encoded as a separate input. The Subsidiary-permission language is not separately modeled; the ratio is the tested quantity."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; commitments_or_amounts_outstanding: True when the Banks hold any Revolving Credit, Term Loan or Convertible Loan Commitment, or any amount payable under the agreement or any Note remains unpaid, so the Article V covenants apply.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: True when the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter.\n; in_period_closing_to_june_30_1995: True when the Fiscal Quarter ends from the Closing Date through June 30, 1995.\n; in_period_july_1_1995_to_june_30_1996: True when the Fiscal Quarter ends from July 1, 1995 through June 30, 1996.\n; in_period_july_1_1996_and_thereafter: True when the Fiscal Quarter ends on or after July 1, 1996.\n; consolidated_debt: Consolidated Debt as of the observation day (last day of the Fiscal Quarter).\n; cash_flow_four_quarters: Cash Flow for the four Fiscal Quarters ending on the observation day.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((commitments_or_amounts_outstanding Bool)\n                            (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool)\n                            (in_period_closing_to_june_30_1995 Bool)\n                            (in_period_july_1_1995_to_june_30_1996 Bool)\n                            (in_period_july_1_1996_and_thereafter Bool)\n                            (consolidated_debt Real)\n                            (cash_flow_four_quarters Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and commitments_or_amounts_outstanding is_fiscal_quarter_end)\n      (and\n        (=> in_period_closing_to_june_30_1995\n            (<= (/ consolidated_debt cash_flow_four_quarters) 6.5))\n        (=> in_period_july_1_1995_to_june_30_1996\n            (<= (/ consolidated_debt cash_flow_four_quarters) 6.0))\n        (=> in_period_july_1_1996_and_thereafter\n            (<= (/ consolidated_debt cash_flow_four_quarters) 5.5)))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "commitments_or_amounts_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True when any Bank has any Revolving Credit, Term Loan or Convertible Loan Commitment, or any amount payable hereunder or under any Note remains unpaid, so the covenant is in force.",
      "source_quote": "so long as any Bank has any Revolving Credit Commitment, Term Loan Commitment or Convertible Loan Commitment hereunder or any amount payable hereunder or under any Note remains unpaid"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True when the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter.",
      "source_quote": "As of the last day of each Fiscal Quarter ending during each period set forth below"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_period_closing_to_june_30_1995",
      "meaning": "True when the Fiscal Quarter ends within the period from the Closing Date through June 30, 1995 (ratio limit 6.50 to 1.00).",
      "source_quote": "Closing Date through June 30, 1995"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_period_july_1_1995_to_june_30_1996",
      "meaning": "True when the Fiscal Quarter ends within the period from July 1, 1995 through June 30, 1996 (ratio limit 6.00 to 1.00).",
      "source_quote": "July 1, 1995 through June 30, 1996"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_period_july_1_1996_and_thereafter",
      "meaning": "True when the Fiscal Quarter ends on or after July 1, 1996 (ratio limit 5.50 to 1.00).",
      "source_quote": "July 1, 1996 and thereafter"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_debt",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Debt of the Borrower as of the last day of the Fiscal Quarter (the numerator of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Debt as of such day"
    },
    {
      "name": "cash_flow_four_quarters",
      "meaning": "Cash Flow for the four Fiscal Quarters ending on the observation day (the denominator of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "Cash Flow for the four Fiscal Quarters ending on such day"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio is Consolidated Debt divided by four-quarter Cash Flow and must be not greater than (<=) the applicable limit: 6.50, 6.00 or 5.50. The division is kept as written, so a zero Cash Flow is reported as unresolved by the evaluator. QF_NRA is used because the denominator is a variable. Period flags are supplied by the evaluator; the formula does not enforce that exactly one is true. The formula is vacuously true when the covenant is not in force or the date is not a fiscal quarter end."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; note_unpaid: true at this observation time if the Note remains unpaid (the covenant applies only while this holds).\n; tier1_capital: Borrower's Tier I Capital on a consolidated basis at the observation time (numerator of the 8% ratio).\n; tier1_plus_tier2_capital: Borrower's Tier 1 plus Tier 2 Capital on a consolidated basis at the observation time (numerator of the 11% ratio).\n; risk_weighted_assets: Borrower's Risk-Weighted Assets on a consolidated basis at the observation time (common denominator of both ratios).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((note_unpaid Bool) (tier1_capital Real) (tier1_plus_tier2_capital Real) (risk_weighted_assets Real)) Bool\n  (=> note_unpaid\n      (and (>= (/ tier1_capital risk_weighted_assets) 0.08)\n           (>= (/ tier1_plus_tier2_capital risk_weighted_assets) 0.11))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "note_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True at the observation time if the Note remains unpaid; the covenant applies only while this holds.",
      "source_quote": "So long as the Note shall remain unpaid"
    },
    {
      "name": "tier1_capital",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Tier I Capital on a consolidated basis at the observation time (numerator of the 8% minimum ratio).",
      "source_quote": "minimum Tier I Capital to Risk-Weighted Assets ratio of 8%"
    },
    {
      "name": "tier1_plus_tier2_capital",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Tier 1 plus Tier 2 Capital on a consolidated basis at the observation time (numerator of the 11% minimum ratio).",
      "source_quote": "Tier 1 plus Tier 2 Capital to RiskWeighted Assets ratio of 11%"
    },
    {
      "name": "risk_weighted_assets",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Risk-Weighted Assets on a consolidated basis at the observation time (denominator of both ratios).",
      "source_quote": "The Borrower will maintain on a consolidated basis"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Both ratios are computed as capital divided by risk-weighted assets, with minimums of 8% (0.08) and 11% (0.11). 'Minimum' is encoded as non-strict (>=). The two ratio requirements are conjoined (AND). The covenant is conditioned on the Note being unpaid. A zero risk_weighted_assets value is reported as unresolved by the evaluator, and no positivity assumption is made. QF_NRA is used because the division is by a variable. The source does not define Tier 1, Tier 2 or Risk-Weighted Assets, so they are atomic inputs."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_quarter_end: true iff the observation is the end of a quarterly fiscal period of the Borrower (the measurement date)\n; liabilities_base: Borrower's Liabilities at the observation date, excluding any amounts added under the second sentence of 5.12 (third-party indebtedness in excess of $25,000)\n; third_party_obligations_aggregate: aggregate amount in USD of indebtedness of any other person or entity that the Borrower has assumed, guaranteed, endorsed or otherwise become liable for, excluding endorsements of negotiable instruments for deposit or collection in the ordinary course of business\n; third_party_excess_classified_liabilities: USD amount of such third-party obligations in excess of $25,000 that is reasonably classified, in light of the facts and circumstances, as actual or matured liabilities under GAAP\n; tangible_net_worth: Borrower's Tangible Net Worth in USD at the observation date\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_quarter_end Bool)\n                            (liabilities_base Real)\n                            (third_party_obligations_aggregate Real)\n                            (third_party_excess_classified_liabilities Real)\n                            (tangible_net_worth Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_quarter_end\n      (<= (/ (+ liabilities_base\n                (ite (> third_party_obligations_aggregate 25000.0)\n                     third_party_excess_classified_liabilities\n                     0.0))\n             tangible_net_worth)\n          0.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation is the end of a quarterly fiscal period of the Borrower, when the ratio is measured.",
      "source_quote": "measured at the end of each quarterly fiscal period"
    },
    {
      "name": "liabilities_base",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Liabilities at the observation date, excluding amounts added under the second sentence of 5.12 for third-party indebtedness in excess of $25,000.",
      "source_quote": "a ratio of its Liabilities to Tangible Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "third_party_obligations_aggregate",
      "meaning": "Aggregate USD amount of indebtedness of any other person or entity that the Borrower has assumed, guaranteed, endorsed or otherwise become liable for, excluding endorsements of negotiable instruments for deposit or collection in the ordinary course of business.",
      "source_quote": "assume, guarantee, endorse or otherwise become liable in connection with the indebtedness of any other person or entity in an aggregate amount exceeding $25,000, except for endorsements of negotiable instruments for deposit or collection in the ordinary course of business"
    },
    {
      "name": "third_party_excess_classified_liabilities",
      "meaning": "USD amount of such third-party obligations in excess of $25,000 that is reasonably classified, in light of the facts and circumstances, as actual or matured liabilities under GAAP, and so is included in Liabilities.",
      "source_quote": "all such amounts in excess of $25,000 and reasonably classified, in light of the facts and circumstances existing at such time, as actual or matured liabilities determined in accordance with GAAP, shall be included within the term \"Liabilities\""
    },
    {
      "name": "tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Tangible Net Worth in USD at the observation date, the denominator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "a ratio of its Liabilities to Tangible Net Worth"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is applied pointwise at quarter-end observations. The ratio is total Liabilities divided by Tangible Net Worth, which must be at most 0.5 (.50 to 1.0). Division by a zero Tangible Net Worth is left to the evaluator as unresolved, and no sign assumption is made, so the ratio is not rewritten as a multiplication. The third-party addition applies only when the aggregate exceeds $25,000. The classified excess is an externally supplied input, and the caller must not already have counted it in liabilities_base. The lead-in waiver and the condition on outstanding amounts or commitments are not modeled as inputs, so the formula covers only the 5.12 test itself. QF_NRA is used because the denominator is a variable."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; commitments_in_effect: true if any of the Commitments are in effect at the observation time.\n; all_obligations_paid_in_full: true if the Loans, all interest thereon and all other amounts payable by the Borrower under the agreement have been paid in full at the observation time.\n; majority_lender_prior_written_consent: true if the Majority Lenders have given prior written consent covering the leverage ratio exceeding 60% at the observation time.\n; consolidated_debt: Consolidated Debt of the Borrower at the observation time (Real, currency units).\n; stockholders_equity: Stockholders' Equity of the Borrower at the observation time (Real, currency units).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((commitments_in_effect Bool) (all_obligations_paid_in_full Bool) (majority_lender_prior_written_consent Bool) (consolidated_debt Real) (stockholders_equity Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and (or commitments_in_effect (not all_obligations_paid_in_full))\n           (not majority_lender_prior_written_consent))\n      (<= (/ consolidated_debt (+ consolidated_debt stockholders_equity)) 0.6)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "commitments_in_effect",
      "meaning": "True if any of the Commitments are in effect at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "so long as any of the Commitments are in effect"
    },
    {
      "name": "all_obligations_paid_in_full",
      "meaning": "True if the Loans, all interest thereon and all other amounts payable by the Borrower under the agreement have been paid in full at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "until payment in full of Loans hereunder, all interest thereon and all other amounts payable by the Borrower hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "majority_lender_prior_written_consent",
      "meaning": "True if the Majority Lenders have given prior written consent covering the leverage ratio exceeding 60% at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "without the prior written consent of the Majority Lenders"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_debt",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Debt of the Borrower at the observation time (currency units).",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "stockholders_equity",
      "meaning": "Stockholders' Equity of the Borrower at the observation time (currency units); no sign assumption is made.",
      "source_quote": "Stockholders' Equity"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio is Consolidated Debt / (Consolidated Debt + Stockholders' Equity), and the formula requires it to be <= 0.6 (60%). Exceeding 60% is the breach, so exactly 60% complies. The covenant is evaluated pointwise at each observation for 'at any time'. It applies while Commitments are in effect or the obligations remain unpaid. Reading 'and until payment in full' as continuing until both conditions end is an interpretive choice. The prior-written-consent exception is modeled as an input that disables the restriction. A zero denominator is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the division has a variable denominator."
}

