{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; net_leverage_ratio: Net Leverage Ratio as of the observation date (the definition is not supplied, so it is an atomic Real; the ratio X to 1.00 is encoded as X).\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter.\n; in_period_1: true iff the observation date falls in the period March 30, 2001, to June 29, 2001.\n; in_period_2: true iff the observation date falls in the period beginning June 30, 2001 and ending June 29, 2002 (the source's 'and' is read as a range).\n; in_period_3: true iff the observation date is on or after June 30, 2002 ('and thereafter').\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((net_leverage_ratio Real) (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (in_period_1 Bool) (in_period_2 Bool) (in_period_3 Bool)) Bool\n  (and\n    (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end in_period_1) (<= net_leverage_ratio 2.0))\n    (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end in_period_2) (<= net_leverage_ratio 1.75))\n    (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end in_period_3) (<= net_leverage_ratio 1.5))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "net_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Net Leverage Ratio as of the observation date, as an atomic Real because its definition is not supplied. A ratio of X to 1.00 is encoded as X.",
      "source_quote": "Net Leverage Ratio"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter.",
      "source_quote": "as of the end of any fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_period_1",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date falls in the period March 30, 2001, to June 29, 2001.",
      "source_quote": "March 30, 2001, to June 29, 2001"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_period_2",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date falls in the period from June 30, 2001 through June 29, 2002. The source's 'and' is read as a range.",
      "source_quote": "June 30, 2001 and June 29, 2002"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_period_3",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is on or after June 30, 2002.",
      "source_quote": "June 30, 2002 and thereafter"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The Net Leverage Ratio is tested only at fiscal quarter ends. The maximum is 2.00 in period 1, 1.75 in period 2 and 1.50 in period 3, and each limit is non-strict (<=) because the Borrowers may not permit the ratio 'to exceed' it. The source text for period 2 reads 'June 30, 2001 and June 29, 2002'. The table structure shows this is a range from June 30, 2001 to June 29, 2002, and in_period_2 is defined that way. The period flags are evaluator-supplied calendar inputs. The Borrowers are the obligors, and the commitment-termination preamble is not modelled because it is a duration condition on the whole covenant, not an observation input."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; obligations_outstanding: True at the observation time if the Obligations of Borrower to Lender have not yet been paid in full (the covenant runs only until payment in full).\n; lender_written_consent: True at the observation time if Lender has consented in writing to the Borrower permitting an interest coverage ratio below 3.5 to 1.0.\n; ebitda_prev_four_quarters: Borrower's EBITDA for the previous four consecutive fiscal quarters ending at the observation time, in currency units.\n; interest_expense_prev_four_quarters: Borrower's Interest Expense payable during the same four consecutive fiscal quarters, in currency units.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((obligations_outstanding Bool) (lender_written_consent Bool) (ebitda_prev_four_quarters Real) (interest_expense_prev_four_quarters Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and obligations_outstanding (not lender_written_consent))\n      (>= (/ ebitda_prev_four_quarters interest_expense_prev_four_quarters) 3.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "obligations_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True at the observation time if the Obligations of Borrower to Lender have not yet been paid in full.",
      "source_quote": "Until payment in full of all Obligations of Borrower to Lender"
    },
    {
      "name": "lender_written_consent",
      "meaning": "True at the observation time if Lender has consented in writing to the Borrower permitting an interest coverage ratio below 3.5 to 1.0.",
      "source_quote": "unless Lender consents in writing"
    },
    {
      "name": "ebitda_prev_four_quarters",
      "meaning": "Borrower's EBITDA for the previous four consecutive fiscal quarters ending at the observation time, in currency units.",
      "source_quote": "EBITDA for the previous four consecutive fiscal quarters of Borrower"
    },
    {
      "name": "interest_expense_prev_four_quarters",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Interest Expense payable during the same four consecutive fiscal quarters, in currency units.",
      "source_quote": "Interest Expense payable during such four consecutive fiscal quarters"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant prohibits permitting the ratio to be less than 3.5 to 1.0, so compliance requires ratio >= 3.5 (non-strict). It applies at any time, so the function is evaluated pointwise at each observation with no calendar flag. The ratio is computed as EBITDA / Interest Expense. Division by zero is left unresolved by the evaluator, with no positivity assumption. QF_NRA is used because the division has a variable denominator. The covenant applies only while Obligations remain outstanding and Lender has not consented in writing, so both conditions are explicit Boolean inputs. EBITDA and Interest Expense are not defined in the source, so they are kept as atomic Real inputs."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; in_covenant_period: true iff the observation time is within the period before the later of the date the Obligations are repaid in full and the date the Borrowers no longer have a right to borrow or have Letters of Credit issued.\n; required_lenders_written_consent: true iff the Required Lenders have given prior written consent otherwise (waiver) covering this observation.\n; availability: Availability in US dollars at the observation time.\n; aggregate_revolving_loan_commitments: Aggregate Revolving Loan Commitments in US dollars at the observation time.\n; fixed_charge_coverage_ratio: consolidated Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio of the Credit Parties and their Subsidiaries, as of the end of the most recent fiscal month for which the Administrative Agent has received financial statements, for the preceding twelve months (as a ratio, 1.10 means 1.10:1.00).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((in_covenant_period Bool) (required_lenders_written_consent Bool) (availability Real) (aggregate_revolving_loan_commitments Real) (fixed_charge_coverage_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and in_covenant_period\n           (not required_lenders_written_consent)\n           (< availability\n              (ite (>= 10000000.0 (* 0.15 aggregate_revolving_loan_commitments))\n                   10000000.0\n                   (* 0.15 aggregate_revolving_loan_commitments))))\n      (>= fixed_charge_coverage_ratio 1.10)))",
