  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is a ratio test, so the body is the ratio (earnings / fixed charges) compared with 2.00. The Borrower must not permit the ratio to be less than 2.00, so compliance is ratio >= 2.0 (non-strict). The test applies only at quarter-end observations, so it is guarded by is_quarter_end. A zero denominator is reported as unresolved by the evaluator. No positivity assumption is made, and the ratio is not rewritten as a cross-multiplication, which would change the meaning when fixed_charges is negative. QF_NRA is used because the division is by a variable. The definitions of the two Consolidated terms are not supplied, so they remain atomic Real inputs."
