  "symbols": [],
  "notes": "Section 5.21 is an incorporation-by-reference and automatic-amendment clause. It sets no numeric threshold or ratio of its own. What it requires depends on the Financial Covenants (levels, ratios, definitions) in the Note Purchase Agreement, and no source context supplies that text. The only freestanding obligation is that Borrowers 'promptly execute and deliver' an amendment. 'Promptly' has no stated time limit, and a Boolean for that obligation would be borrower-compliance QA, not a translation of a financial covenant. The clause also gives no state-update rules for the 30-day Required Lender objection window beyond what an evaluator would have to supply as opaque flags. A faithful SMT encoding of the incorporated covenants therefore needs the Note Purchase Agreement's Financial Covenant terms, or a decision on whether to formalize only the amendment-delivery obligation."
