{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; consolidated_indebtedness: Consolidated Indebtedness of the Company, the numerator of the ratio, at the observation time, in the same currency units as consolidated_tangible_net_worth. The source supplies no further definition.\n; consolidated_tangible_net_worth: Consolidated Tangible Net Worth of the Company, the denominator of the ratio, at the observation time, in the same currency units as consolidated_indebtedness. The source supplies no further definition.\n; is_last_day_of_fiscal_year: true iff the observation time is the last day of a fiscal year of the Company (\"on and as of the last day of any fiscal year\"); false at any other time.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((consolidated_indebtedness Real) (consolidated_tangible_net_worth Real) (is_last_day_of_fiscal_year Bool)) Bool\n  ; The ratio is Consolidated Indebtedness / Consolidated Tangible Net Worth, with 600% = 6.0 and 650% = 6.5.\n  ; The covenant forbids exceeding the limit, so the ratio must be <= the limit.\n  (ite is_last_day_of_fiscal_year\n       (<= (/ consolidated_indebtedness consolidated_tangible_net_worth) 6.0)\n       (<= (/ consolidated_indebtedness consolidated_tangible_net_worth) 6.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "consolidated_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Indebtedness of the Company at the observation time, the numerator of the ratio, in the same currency units as consolidated_tangible_net_worth. The source supplies no further definition.",
      "source_quote": "ratio of Consolidated Indebtedness to Consolidated Tangible Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Tangible Net Worth of the Company at the observation time, the denominator of the ratio, in the same currency units as consolidated_indebtedness. The source supplies no further definition.",
      "source_quote": "ratio of Consolidated Indebtedness to Consolidated Tangible Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_last_day_of_fiscal_year",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation time is the last day of a fiscal year of the Company; false at any other time.",
      "source_quote": "on and as of the last day of any fiscal year"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Pointwise translation. On the last day of a fiscal year the ratio must be at most 600% (6.0). At any other time it must be at most 650% (6.5). 'Exceed' makes the bounds non-strict (<=). The ratio is computed as an explicit division. A zero Consolidated Tangible Net Worth is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved, and no sign or positivity assumptions are made. QF_NRA is used because the division has a non-constant denominator. The Required Banks' written-consent exception is not modeled. It is a waiver mechanism, and the source gives no observable state to encode it."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; net_earnings_before_interest_expense: consolidated net earnings before interest expense for the measurement period, excluding gain or loss from nonrecurring items and sales of assets (USD).\n; non_cash_expenses: consolidated non-cash expenses for the measurement period (USD).\n; development_interest_expense: consolidated interest expense on development projects for the measurement period (USD), before applying the $375,000 cap.\n; funded_debt_interest: consolidated interest on Funded Debt for the measurement period (USD).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (net_earnings_before_interest_expense Real) (non_cash_expenses Real) (development_interest_expense Real) (funded_debt_interest Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n      (>= (/ (+ net_earnings_before_interest_expense\n                non_cash_expenses\n                (ite (<= development_interest_expense 375000.0) development_interest_expense 375000.0))\n             funded_debt_interest)\n          2.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower, the date as of which the ratio is measured.",
      "source_quote": "measured as of the end of each fiscal quarter on a consolidated basis"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_earnings_before_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Consolidated net earnings before interest expense for the measurement period (USD), excluding gain or loss from nonrecurring items and sales of assets.",
      "source_quote": "net earnings before interest expense"
    },
    {
      "name": "non_cash_expenses",
      "meaning": "Consolidated non-cash expenses for the measurement period (USD), added to the numerator.",
      "source_quote": "non-cash expenses"
    },
    {
      "name": "development_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Consolidated interest expense on development projects for the measurement period (USD), before the $375,000 cap. The formula adds min(this value, 375000) to the numerator.",
      "source_quote": "up to $375,000 in interest expense on development projects"
    },
    {
      "name": "funded_debt_interest",
      "meaning": "Consolidated interest on Funded Debt for the measurement period (USD). It is the denominator of the coverage ratio.",
      "source_quote": "interest on Funded Debt"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is applied only at fiscal quarter-end observations. The numerator is net earnings before interest expense (already excluding nonrecurring gains or losses and asset-sale gains or losses, as the input meaning states), plus non-cash expenses, plus development-project interest expense capped at 375000. The requirement is numerator / funded_debt_interest >= 2.5 ('not less than 2.5 to 1'), so exactly 2.5 complies. Division is kept explicit, so a zero denominator is reported by the evaluator as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because division by a variable is nonlinear. The 'unless Agent ... shall otherwise consent' lead-in is a waiver and is not modeled. The preamble's duration of the covenant is handled by the pointwise convention."
}

