{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true exactly when this observation is as of the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; leverage_ratio: the Leverage Ratio as of this observation, expressed as a fraction (65% = 0.65). Atomic input; its definition is not supplied.\n; interest_coverage_ratio: the Interest Coverage Ratio as of this observation, expressed as the first number of an \"X to 1\" ratio (1.8 to 1 = 1.8). Atomic input; its definition is not supplied.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (leverage_ratio Real) (interest_coverage_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (and\n    (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (<= leverage_ratio 0.65))\n    (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (>= interest_coverage_ratio 1.8))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation is as of the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.",
      "source_quote": "as of the end of any fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Leverage Ratio as of the observation, expressed as a fraction (65% = 0.65). Atomic input because its definition is not supplied.",
      "source_quote": "the Leverage Ratio to be greater than sixty-five percent (65%)"
    },
    {
      "name": "interest_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Interest Coverage Ratio as of the observation, expressed as the first number of an 'X to 1' ratio (1.8 to 1 = 1.8). Atomic input because its definition is not supplied.",
      "source_quote": "the Interest Coverage Ratio to be less than 1.8 to 1"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Both covenants in Section 6.1 apply only as of fiscal quarter end. (a) The Leverage Ratio must not be greater than 65%, so compliance is leverage_ratio <= 0.65, with equality compliant. (b) The Interest Coverage Ratio must not be less than 1.8 to 1, so compliance is interest_coverage_ratio >= 1.8, with equality compliant. The two conditions are conjoined. The ratios are atomic because the source gives no arithmetic definitions, so no division appears. The percentage is encoded as a fraction (0.65), and the evaluator must supply leverage_ratio in that unit. The surrounding lead-in (Commitments in effect, Notes outstanding, etc.) is the period during which the covenant applies. It is not encoded as a separate input, so the evaluator should supply observations only from that period."
