    {
      "name": "sum_quarterly_net_income_excluding_loss_quarters",
      "meaning": "Dollar sum, over each fiscal quarter commencing with the quarter ended December 31, 1997 through the latest completed quarter at the observation, of Borrower's consolidated net income for that quarter, with any quarter that has a net loss counted as zero. The formula applies the 40% factor to this sum.",
      "source_quote": "40% of consolidated net income of Borrower for each fiscal quarter, commencing with the fiscal quarter ended December 31, 1997"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Each of the three financial covenants is checked at every observation, which is the pointwise reading of 'at any time' and 'at all times'. The covenants apply only while in_covenant_period is true and lender_prior_written_consent is false. The current ratio must be at least 3.0 (a shortfall is a breach) and the debt to equity ratio must be at most 1.25 (exceeding it is a breach). The two ratios are written as explicit divisions, so a zero denominator is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved, as the definedness policy requires. The tangible net worth floor is 15,000,000 plus 0.4 times the supplied cumulative quarterly sum. The sum over an unbounded number of quarters cannot be written as a fixed quantifier-free expression, so it is an input. Its meaning carries the proviso that quarters with a net loss contribute zero. The 40% factor and the $15,000,000 base stay in the formula. The reading that the 40% additions accumulate across quarters is an interpretation of 'for each fiscal quarter'. The source does not state it explicitly. QF_NRA is used because the ratios divide by variables."
