{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower and its Restricted Subsidiaries.\n; combined_funded_debt: Combined Funded Debt of the Borrower and its Restricted Subsidiaries as of the observation date (currency units).\n; combined_total_capitalization: Combined Total Capitalization of the Borrower and its Restricted Subsidiaries as of the observation date (same currency units).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (combined_funded_debt Real) (combined_total_capitalization Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n      (<= (* 100 (/ combined_funded_debt combined_total_capitalization)) 52)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower and its Restricted Subsidiaries.",
      "source_quote": "as of the end of each fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "combined_funded_debt",
      "meaning": "Combined Funded Debt of the Borrower and its Restricted Subsidiaries as of the observation date (currency units).",
      "source_quote": "Combined Funded Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "combined_total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "Combined Total Capitalization of the Borrower and its Restricted Subsidiaries as of the observation date (same currency units).",
      "source_quote": "Combined Total Capitalization"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio is expressed as a percentage, so it is 100 * Combined Funded Debt / Combined Total Capitalization. The threshold is non-strict (equal to or less than 52). The covenant applies only at fiscal quarter end, so the body is an implication on the quarter-end flag. The definitions of Combined Funded Debt and Combined Total Capitalization are not supplied, so each is an atomic Real input. Division by a variable makes the formula nonlinear, hence QF_NRA. A zero capitalization is reported by the evaluator as unresolved, and no positivity is assumed. The preamble condition (Notes unpaid, commitments outstanding, and so on) is not modeled as a parameter, since the covenant is evaluated at observations where it is in force."
}

{
