{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is a fiscal quarter end\n; total_debt: Total Debt of the Borrowers and their Subsidiaries on a Consolidated basis on the observation date\n; total_capitalization: Total Capitalization of the Borrowers and their Subsidiaries on a Consolidated basis on the observation date\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (total_debt Real) (total_capitalization Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (<= (/ total_debt total_capitalization) 0.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is a fiscal quarter end, i.e. the date as of which the ratio test applies.",
      "source_quote": "As of any fiscal quarter end"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_debt",
      "meaning": "Total Debt on the observation date, measured on a Consolidated basis for the Borrowers and their Subsidiaries. This is the numerator of the ratio. The source supplies no further definition, so it is an atomic Real.",
      "source_quote": "Total Debt on such date"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "Total Capitalization on the observation date, measured on a Consolidated basis for the Borrowers and their Subsidiaries. This is the denominator of the ratio. The source supplies no further definition, so it is an atomic Real.",
      "source_quote": "Total Capitalization on such date"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant prohibits permitting the ratio to be greater than 0.50 to 1.00, so compliance at a fiscal quarter end is total_debt / total_capitalization <= 0.5. On dates that are not fiscal quarter ends the covenant is not applicable, so the result is true. Division by zero is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved, and no positivity assumption is added. The covenant's preamble (Obligations outstanding, no consent obtained under Section 13.11) is the standing condition for the covenant to apply, and it is not modeled as an input. QF_NRA is used because the denominator is a variable."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; advance_unpaid: true iff any Advance remains unpaid at the observation date.\n; lender_has_commitment: true iff any Lender has any Commitment under the agreement at the observation date.\n; letter_of_credit_outstanding: true iff any Letter of Credit is outstanding at the observation date.\n; consolidated_debt_for_borrowed_money: Consolidated Debt for Borrowed Money of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries as of the observation date.\n; consolidated_cash_flow_4q: Consolidated Cash Flow of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries for the four fiscal quarters ended on or immediately prior to the observation date.\n; interest_and_discount_amortization_4q: sum of interest payable on, and amortization of debt discount in respect of, all Consolidated Debt for Borrowed Money of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries during that same four-quarter period.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((advance_unpaid Bool) (lender_has_commitment Bool) (letter_of_credit_outstanding Bool) (consolidated_debt_for_borrowed_money Real) (consolidated_cash_flow_4q Real) (interest_and_discount_amortization_4q Real)) Bool\n  (=> (or advance_unpaid lender_has_commitment letter_of_credit_outstanding)\n      (and\n        ; (a) Leverage Ratio: debt / cash flow not greater than 4.00 to 1.00\n        (<= (/ consolidated_debt_for_borrowed_money consolidated_cash_flow_4q) 4.0)\n        ; (b) Interest Coverage Ratio: cash flow / interest and discount amortization not less than 5.00 to 1.00\n        (>= (/ consolidated_cash_flow_4q interest_and_discount_amortization_4q) 5.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "advance_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True iff any Advance remains unpaid at the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "any Advance shall remain unpaid"
    },
    {
      "name": "lender_has_commitment",
      "meaning": "True iff any Lender has any Commitment under the agreement at the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "any Lender shall have any Commitment hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "letter_of_credit_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True iff any Letter of Credit is outstanding at the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "any Letter of Credit shall be outstanding"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_debt_for_borrowed_money",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Debt for Borrowed Money of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries as of the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Debt for Borrowed Money of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries as of such date"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_cash_flow_4q",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Cash Flow of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries for the four fiscal quarters ended on or immediately prior to the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Cash Flow of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries for the period of four fiscal quarters ended on or immediately prior to such date"
    },
    {
      "name": "interest_and_discount_amortization_4q",
      "meaning": "Sum of interest payable on, and amortization of debt discount in respect of, all Consolidated Debt for Borrowed Money of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries during the same four-quarter period.",
      "source_quote": "the sum of interest payable on, and amortization of debt discount in respect of, all Consolidated Debt for Borrowed Money of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries during such period"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenants apply 'as of any date' while any Advance is unpaid, any Lender has a Commitment, or any Letter of Credit is outstanding, so the three conditions are joined by OR as the applicability antecedent. Both ratio tests are conjoined. The Leverage Ratio is debt divided by cash flow, with '<= 4.0' because the source says 'not greater than'. The Interest Coverage Ratio is cash flow divided by interest and discount amortization, with '>= 5.0' because the source says 'not less than'. Division is kept as written, so QF_NRA is used, and a zero denominator is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. No positivity assumptions are added."
}

{
