{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; covenant_period_in_effect: true iff the observation time is on or after the Effective Date and the Section 7 covenant period has not ended, i.e. the Agreement is still in effect and it is not yet the case that the Total Commitment has terminated, no Notes are outstanding, and the Loans, Competitive Bid Loans, interest, Fees and all other Obligations are paid in full.\n; total_indebtedness: Borrower's Total Indebtedness at the observation time, as defined in the Agreement (numerator of the leverage ratio).\n; total_capitalization: Borrower's Total Capitalization at the observation time, as defined in the Agreement (denominator of the leverage ratio).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((covenant_period_in_effect Bool) (total_indebtedness Real) (total_capitalization Real)) Bool\n  (=> covenant_period_in_effect\n      (<= (/ total_indebtedness total_capitalization) 0.45)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "covenant_period_in_effect",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation time is on or after the Effective Date and the covenant period has not ended: the Agreement is in effect and it is not yet the case that the Total Commitment has terminated, no Notes are outstanding, and the Loans, Competitive Bid Loans, interest, Fees and all other Obligations are paid in full.",
      "source_quote": "on the Effective Date and thereafter, for so long as this Agreement is in effect and until such time as the Total Commitment has terminated"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Total Indebtedness at the observation time, as defined in the Agreement; numerator (i) of the leverage ratio.",
      "source_quote": "(i) Total Indebtedness"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Total Capitalization at the observation time, as defined in the Agreement; denominator (ii) of the leverage ratio.",
      "source_quote": "(ii) Total Capitalization"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Pointwise translation of 'at any time': at each observation, when the covenant period applies, Total Indebtedness / Total Capitalization must be <= 0.45 (the 'not exceed 0.45 to 1.0' limit is non-strict). The ratio is computed by direct division, so a zero Total Capitalization is reported by the evaluator as unresolved; no positivity assumption is made. QF_NRA is used because the division has a variable denominator. Definitions of Total Indebtedness and Total Capitalization were not supplied, so each is an atomic Real input."
}

{
