{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; tier1_capital: Tier 1 Capital of one Bank Subsidiary at the observation time (numerator of the Tier 1 Leverage Ratio). The evaluator calls the function once per Bank Subsidiary per observation.\n; total_assets: Total assets of that same Bank Subsidiary at the observation time (denominator of the Tier 1 Leverage Ratio).\n; is_fiscal_year_end: True exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal year of the Borrower during the term of the Agreement.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((tier1_capital Real) (total_assets Real) (is_fiscal_year_end Bool)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_year_end (>= (/ tier1_capital total_assets) 0.07)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "tier1_capital",
      "meaning": "Tier 1 Capital of one Bank Subsidiary at the observation time, the numerator of the Tier 1 Leverage Ratio. The evaluator supplies one call per Bank Subsidiary per observation.",
      "source_quote": "ratio of Tier 1 Capital to total assets"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_assets",
      "meaning": "Total assets of the same Bank Subsidiary at the observation time, the denominator of the Tier 1 Leverage Ratio.",
      "source_quote": "ratio of Tier 1 Capital to total assets"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_year_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal year during the term of the Agreement.",
      "source_quote": "as of the end of any fiscal year during the term of this Agreement"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant requires the ratio not to be less than 7.0%, so the check is >= 0.07. The ratio is Tier 1 Capital divided by total assets, as the source defines it, and a zero total_assets is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. 'Any of the Bank Subsidiaries' is handled by universal instantiation: each subsidiary's figures are supplied as a separate call and the results are conjoined. QF_NRA is used because the division has a variable denominator. The lender-consent exception is not modeled, because consent is not stated as a measurable condition."
}

{
