{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Company.\n; consolidated_leverage_ratio: Consolidated Leverage Ratio as at the observation date, as a decimal fraction (35% = 0.35).\n; consolidated_tangible_net_worth: Consolidated Tangible Net Worth as at the observation date, in US dollars.\n; consolidated_net_income_since_2005: Consolidated Net Income during the period from January 1, 2005 to and including the observation date, in US dollars.\n; net_cash_proceeds_stock_since_2005: aggregate Net Cash Proceeds of all issuances by the Company of shares of its Capital Stock during the period from January 1, 2005 to and including the observation date, in US dollars.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (consolidated_leverage_ratio Real) (consolidated_tangible_net_worth Real) (consolidated_net_income_since_2005 Real) (net_cash_proceeds_stock_since_2005 Real)) Bool\n  (and\n    (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (<= consolidated_leverage_ratio 0.35))\n    (>= consolidated_tangible_net_worth\n        (+ 1106175000\n           (* 0.5 consolidated_net_income_since_2005)\n           (* 0.5 net_cash_proceeds_stock_since_2005)))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Company; the leverage test applies only then.",
      "source_quote": "last day of any fiscal quarter of the Company"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Leverage Ratio as at the observation date, as a decimal fraction (35% = 0.35). It is an atomic input because no definition is supplied.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Leverage Ratio"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Tangible Net Worth as at the observation date, in US dollars.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Tangible Net Worth as at any date"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_net_income_since_2005",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Net Income during the period from January 1, 2005 to and including the observation date, in US dollars.",
      "source_quote": "50% of Consolidated Net Income during the period from January 1, 2005 to and including such date"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_cash_proceeds_stock_since_2005",
      "meaning": "Aggregate Net Cash Proceeds of all issuances by the Company of shares of its Capital Stock during the period from January 1, 2005 to and including the observation date, in US dollars.",
      "source_quote": "50% of the aggregate Net Cash Proceeds of all issuances by the Company of shares of its Capital Stock during the period from January 1, 2005 to and including such date"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Section 7.1 has two prohibitions, (a) and (b), and the function requires both to hold at the observation. (a) applies only when is_fiscal_quarter_end is true. The prohibition on permitting the ratio to exceed 35% becomes ratio <= 0.35. (b) applies at any date. The prohibition on net worth being less than the sum becomes net worth >= 1,106,175,000 + 0.5*net income + 0.5*stock proceeds. Net income is not assumed nonnegative. The leading 'so long as the Commitments remain in effect...' condition is not modeled as a separate input; the evaluator is assumed to supply observations only while the covenant is in force. There is no division, so no unresolved-denominator case arises."
}

