{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; commitments_expired_or_terminated: True iff the Commitments have expired or terminated at this observation.\n; loans_and_fees_paid_in_full: True iff the principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees payable under the agreement have been paid in full at this observation.\n; test_period_ends_prior_to_maturity: True iff the observed period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ends prior to the Maturity Date.\n; consolidated_ebitda: Consolidated EBITDA of the Borrower for that period of four consecutive fiscal quarters (currency units).\n; consolidated_cash_interest_expense: Consolidated Cash Interest Expense for the same period of four consecutive fiscal quarters (currency units).\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n  (commitments_expired_or_terminated Bool)\n  (loans_and_fees_paid_in_full Bool)\n  (test_period_ends_prior_to_maturity Bool)\n  (consolidated_ebitda Real)\n  (consolidated_cash_interest_expense Real)\n) Bool\n  (=> (and (not (and commitments_expired_or_terminated loans_and_fees_paid_in_full))\n           test_period_ends_prior_to_maturity)\n      (>= (/ consolidated_ebitda consolidated_cash_interest_expense) 4.0)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "commitments_expired_or_terminated",
      "meaning": "True iff the Commitments have expired or terminated at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "Until the Commitments have expired or terminated"
    },
    {
      "name": "loans_and_fees_paid_in_full",
      "meaning": "True iff the principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees payable under the agreement have been paid in full at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "the principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees payable hereunder have been paid in full"
    },
    {
      "name": "test_period_ends_prior_to_maturity",
      "meaning": "True iff the observed period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ends prior to the Maturity Date.",
      "source_quote": "for any period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending prior to the Maturity Date"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_ebitda",
      "meaning": "Consolidated EBITDA for the observed period of four consecutive fiscal quarters (currency units).",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated EBITDA"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_cash_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Cash Interest Expense for the same period of four consecutive fiscal quarters (currency units).",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Cash Interest Expense"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies while the Commitments have not both expired or terminated and the loans and fees have not all been paid in full. The article lead-in says the covenant lasts until both conditions are met, so applicability is the negation of their conjunction. The ratio must not be less than 4.0 to 1, so the test is EBITDA / cash interest expense >= 4.0. The ratio is computed by division, so a zero interest expense is reported by the evaluator as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the divisor is a variable. Consolidated EBITDA and Consolidated Cash Interest Expense are atomic inputs because no definitions were supplied."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; cp_maintenance_ratio: CP Maintenance Ratio as of the observation date, expressed as x in x:1.00.\n; is_last_business_day_of_calendar_week: true iff the observation date is the last Business Day of a calendar week.\n; gross_asset_coverage_ratio: Gross Asset Coverage Ratio as of the observation date, expressed as x in x:1.00.\n; is_gross_calculation_date: true iff the observation date is a Calculation Date for the Gross Asset Coverage Ratio test.\n; is_gross_proviso_business_day: true iff the observation date is a Business Day after a Calculation Date on which the Gross Asset Coverage Ratio was less than 4.10:1.00, and the ratio has not yet been greater than 4.10:1.00 (the proviso period).\n; gross_statement_delivered_on_time: true iff the Investment Advisor gave the Administrative Agent, by telephone or facsimile, a reasonably detailed statement of the Gross Asset Coverage Ratio for the observation Business Day by not later than the following Business Day.\n; net_asset_coverage_ratio: Net Asset Coverage Ratio as of the observation date, expressed as x in x:1.00.\n; is_net_calculation_date: true iff the observation date is a Calculation Date for the Net Asset Coverage Ratio test.\n; is_net_proviso_business_day: true iff the observation date is a Business Day after a Calculation Date on which the Net Asset Coverage Ratio was less than 4.10:1.00, and the ratio has not yet been greater than 4.10:1.00 (the proviso period).\n; net_statement_delivered_on_time: true iff the Investment Advisor gave the Administrative Agent, by telephone or facsimile, a reasonably detailed statement of the Net Asset Coverage Ratio for the observation Business Day by not later than the following Business Day.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((cp_maintenance_ratio Real)\n                            (is_last_business_day_of_calendar_week Bool)\n                            (gross_asset_coverage_ratio Real)\n                            (is_gross_calculation_date Bool)\n                            (is_gross_proviso_business_day Bool)\n                            (gross_statement_delivered_on_time Bool)\n                            (net_asset_coverage_ratio Real)\n                            (is_net_calculation_date Bool)\n                            (is_net_proviso_business_day Bool)\n                            (net_statement_delivered_on_time Bool)) Bool\n  (and\n    ; (a) CP Maintenance Ratio must not be less than 4.05 on the last Business Day of a calendar week\n    (=> is_last_business_day_of_calendar_week (>= cp_maintenance_ratio 4.05))\n    ; (b) Gross Asset Coverage Ratio must not be less than 4.00 on Calculation Dates and proviso Business Days\n    (=> (or is_gross_calculation_date is_gross_proviso_business_day)\n        (>= gross_asset_coverage_ratio 4.00))\n    ; (b) proviso: a statement is due for each Business Day in the proviso period\n    (=> is_gross_proviso_business_day gross_statement_delivered_on_time)\n    ; (c) Net Asset Coverage Ratio must not be less than 4.00 on Calculation Dates and proviso Business Days\n    (=> (or is_net_calculation_date is_net_proviso_business_day)\n        (>= net_asset_coverage_ratio 4.00))\n    ; (c) proviso: a statement is due for each Business Day in the proviso period\n    (=> is_net_proviso_business_day net_statement_delivered_on_time)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "cp_maintenance_ratio",
      "meaning": "CP Maintenance Ratio as of the observation date, expressed as x in x:1.00.",
      "source_quote": "The Borrower will not permit the CP Maintenance Ratio as of the last Business Day of any calendar week to be less than 4.05:1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_last_business_day_of_calendar_week",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last Business Day of a calendar week.",
      "source_quote": "the last Business Day of any calendar week"
    },
    {
      "name": "gross_asset_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Gross Asset Coverage Ratio as of the observation date, expressed as x in x:1.00.",
      "source_quote": "The Borrower will not permit the Gross Asset Coverage Ratio as of any Calculation Date to be less than 4.00:1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_gross_calculation_date",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is a Calculation Date for the Gross Asset Coverage Ratio test.",
      "source_quote": "The Borrower will not permit the Gross Asset Coverage Ratio as of any Calculation Date to be less than 4.00:1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_gross_proviso_business_day",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is a Business Day after a Calculation Date on which the Gross Asset Coverage Ratio was less than 4.10:1.00, and the ratio has not yet been greater than 4.10:1.00.",
      "source_quote": "such ratio shall be calculated as of the close of business on each Business Day thereafter until such ratio is greater than 4.10:1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "gross_statement_delivered_on_time",
      "meaning": "True iff the Investment Advisor gave the Administrative Agent, by telephone or facsimile, a reasonably detailed statement of the Gross Asset Coverage Ratio for the observation Business Day by not later than the following Business Day.",
      "source_quote": "a reasonably detailed statement of the Gross Asset Coverage Ratio for each Business Day during the period described in this proviso by not later than the following Business Day"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_asset_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Net Asset Coverage Ratio as of the observation date, expressed as x in x:1.00.",
      "source_quote": "The Borrower will not permit the Net Asset Coverage Ratio as of any Calculation Date to be less than 4.00:1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_net_calculation_date",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is a Calculation Date for the Net Asset Coverage Ratio test.",
      "source_quote": "The Borrower will not permit the Net Asset Coverage Ratio as of any Calculation Date to be less than 4.00:1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_net_proviso_business_day",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is a Business Day after a Calculation Date on which the Net Asset Coverage Ratio was less than 4.10:1.00, and the ratio has not yet been greater than 4.10:1.00.",
      "source_quote": "such ratio shall be calculated as of the close of business on each Business Day thereafter until such ratio is greater than 4.10:1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_statement_delivered_on_time",
      "meaning": "True iff the Investment Advisor gave the Administrative Agent, by telephone or facsimile, a reasonably detailed statement of the Net Asset Coverage Ratio for the observation Business Day by not later than the following Business Day.",
      "source_quote": "a reasonably detailed statement of the Net Asset Coverage Ratio for each Business Day during the period described in this proviso by not later than the following Business Day"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Ratios are x:1.00 and are compared as the number x. The 4.05 and 4.00 minimums are non-strict (>=) because the covenant prohibits a ratio 'less than' the threshold. The Article 7 preamble (until the Termination Date and payment in full) is treated as the evaluation window rather than a parameter, so the evaluator should only supply observations within it. 'Calculation Date' is not defined in the supplied text, so it is a Boolean input. The proviso extends calculation to each following Business Day, so those days are treated as additional days on which the 4.00 minimum is tested. The proviso-period flags are supplied by the evaluator, since the pointwise function cannot derive them from history. The reporting duty is encoded as an outcome Boolean for each proviso Business Day. The 4.10 trigger is carried by the proviso-period flags rather than as a separate numeric test, because the 4.10 threshold only sets the monitoring period and is not itself a compliance floor."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; consolidated_fixed_charge_coverage_ratio: Borrower's Consolidated Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio as at the observation date (end of a fiscal quarter), supplied as an atomic Real (e.g. 1.5 for 1.50:1.0); its definition is not supplied.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: True iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; in_period_closing_to_q4_fy2002: True iff the observation date is on or after the Closing Date and before the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2002.\n; in_period_q4_fy2002_to_q4_fy2003: True iff the observation date is on or after the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2002 and before the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2003.\n; in_period_from_q4_fy2003: True iff the observation date is on or after the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2003.\n; required_lenders_consent_in_writing: True iff the Required Lenders have otherwise consented in writing so that this covenant does not apply at this observation.\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n  (consolidated_fixed_charge_coverage_ratio Real)\n  (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool)\n  (in_period_closing_to_q4_fy2002 Bool)\n  (in_period_q4_fy2002_to_q4_fy2003 Bool)\n  (in_period_from_q4_fy2003 Bool)\n  (required_lenders_consent_in_writing Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end (not required_lenders_consent_in_writing))\n      (and\n        (=> in_period_closing_to_q4_fy2002 (>= consolidated_fixed_charge_coverage_ratio 1.5))\n        (=> in_period_q4_fy2002_to_q4_fy2003 (>= consolidated_fixed_charge_coverage_ratio 1.55))\n        (=> in_period_from_q4_fy2003 (>= consolidated_fixed_charge_coverage_ratio 1.6)))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "consolidated_fixed_charge_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Consolidated Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio as at the observation date (end of a fiscal quarter), as an atomic Real (1.50:1.0 = 1.5); its definition is not supplied.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.",
      "source_quote": "as at the end of each of its fiscal quarters"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_period_closing_to_q4_fy2002",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is on or after the Closing Date and before the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2002.",
      "source_quote": "From the Closing Date up to but not including the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2002"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_period_q4_fy2002_to_q4_fy2003",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is on or after the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2002 and before the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2003.",
      "source_quote": "From and including the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2002 up to but not including the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2003"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_period_from_q4_fy2003",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is on or after the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2003.",
      "source_quote": "From and including the last day of the fourth quarter of fiscal 2003"
    },
    {
      "name": "required_lenders_consent_in_writing",
      "meaning": "True iff the Required Lenders have otherwise consented in writing so that the covenant does not apply at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "unless the Required Lenders shall otherwise consent in writing"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Pointwise translation: the covenant applies only at fiscal quarter ends and when no written Required Lenders consent is in effect. The minimum ratio then depends on the period: 1.50 before the last day of Q4 fiscal 2002, 1.55 from that day until the last day of Q4 fiscal 2003, and 1.60 from that day onward. The ratio is compared directly with >= ('not less than'), with no division. The period flags are evaluator-supplied calendar inputs and are expected to be mutually exclusive."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; covenant_in_force: true when the Commitments remain in effect, any Note remains outstanding and unpaid, or any other amount is owing to the Agent or any Lender.\n; total_senior_funded_debt: Total Senior Funded Debt at the date of determination.\n; consolidated_adjusted_ebitda: Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA for the four consecutive fiscal quarters preceding the date of determination.\n; date_through_1998_12_31: true when the date of determination is on or before December 31, 1998.\n; date_1999_01_01_to_1999_06_30: true when the date of determination is from and including January 1, 1999 through June 30, 1999.\n; date_1999_07_01_to_1999_12_31: true when the date of determination is from and including July 1, 1999 through December 31, 1999.\n; period_ends_on_or_after_2000_01_01: true when the period ends on or after January 1, 2000.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((covenant_in_force Bool)\n                            (total_senior_funded_debt Real)\n                            (consolidated_adjusted_ebitda Real)\n                            (date_through_1998_12_31 Bool)\n                            (date_1999_01_01_to_1999_06_30 Bool)\n                            (date_1999_07_01_to_1999_12_31 Bool)\n                            (period_ends_on_or_after_2000_01_01 Bool)) Bool\n  (=> covenant_in_force\n      (and\n        (=> date_through_1998_12_31\n            (<= (/ total_senior_funded_debt consolidated_adjusted_ebitda) 4.5))\n        (=> date_1999_01_01_to_1999_06_30\n            (<= (/ total_senior_funded_debt consolidated_adjusted_ebitda) 4.25))\n        (=> date_1999_07_01_to_1999_12_31\n            (<= (/ total_senior_funded_debt consolidated_adjusted_ebitda) 4.0))\n        (=> period_ends_on_or_after_2000_01_01\n            (<= (/ total_senior_funded_debt consolidated_adjusted_ebitda) 3.75)))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "covenant_in_force",
      "meaning": "True when the Commitments remain in effect, any Note remains outstanding and unpaid, or any other amount is owing to the Agent or any Lender.",
      "source_quote": "so long as the Commitments remain in effect, any Note remains outstanding and unpaid or any other amount is owing to the Agent or any Lender hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_senior_funded_debt",
      "meaning": "Total Senior Funded Debt at the date of determination (numerator of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "Total Senior Funded Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_adjusted_ebitda",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA for the four consecutive fiscal quarters preceding the date of determination (denominator of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters preceding any date of determination"
    },
    {
      "name": "date_through_1998_12_31",
      "meaning": "True when the date of determination is on or before December 31, 1998. The 4.5 to 1 limit applies.",
      "source_quote": "4.5 to 1 through December 31, 1998"
    },
    {
      "name": "date_1999_01_01_to_1999_06_30",
      "meaning": "True when the date of determination is from and including January 1, 1999 through June 30, 1999. The 4.25 to 1.00 limit applies.",
      "source_quote": "4.25 to 1.00 for the period from and including January 1, 1999 through June 30, 1999"
    },
    {
      "name": "date_1999_07_01_to_1999_12_31",
      "meaning": "True when the date of determination is from and including July 1, 1999 through December 31, 1999. The 4.00 to 1.00 limit applies.",
      "source_quote": "4.00 to 1.00 for the period from and including July 1, 1999 through December 31, 1999"
    },
    {
      "name": "period_ends_on_or_after_2000_01_01",
      "meaning": "True when the period ends on or after January 1, 2000. The 3.75 to 1.0 limit applies.",
      "source_quote": "3.75 to 1.0 for periods ending on or after January 1, 2000"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio is Total Senior Funded Debt divided by Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA. A violation is a ratio greater than the limit, so compliance is ratio <= limit. QF_NRA is used because the division has a variable denominator. Division by zero is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. The Subsidiary Borrowers carve-out limits who is bound, not the test, so it is not encoded. The date-range flags are separate inputs supplied by the evaluator."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; commitment_or_obligation_outstanding: true iff any Lender has a Commitment or any Obligation remains unpaid or outstanding at the observation.\n; is_test_period_end_on_or_after_2014_09_30: true iff the observation is the last day of a Test Period, and that Test Period ends on or after September 30, 2014.\n; leverage_ratio: Borrower's Leverage Ratio as of the last day of the Test Period, as a ratio X in X:1.00.\n; acquisition_consideration_six_month: aggregate consideration paid in USD for all Permitted Acquisitions or other permitted Acquisitions consummated during the relevant six consecutive month period.\n; election_notice_given: true iff the Borrower elected the increase by written notice to the Administrative Agent, with the reasonably detailed description of the acquisitions and consideration paid.\n; in_increase_window: true iff the Fiscal Quarter of this Test Period is the Fiscal Quarter of the election or one of the immediately following three Fiscal Quarters.\n; increase_times_including_this: number of times the Maximum Leverage Threshold has been increased under the proviso during the term, counting the election being relied on.\n; increased_quarters_including_this: number of Fiscal Quarters in which the Maximum Leverage Threshold has been increased during the term, counting those covered by the election being relied on.\n; has_unincreased_quarter_in_last_four: true iff in the most recently ended four consecutive Fiscal Quarter period there is at least one Fiscal Quarter in respect of which the Maximum Leverage Threshold has not been increased.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((commitment_or_obligation_outstanding Bool)\n                            (is_test_period_end_on_or_after_2014_09_30 Bool)\n                            (leverage_ratio Real)\n                            (acquisition_consideration_six_month Real)\n                            (election_notice_given Bool)\n                            (in_increase_window Bool)\n                            (increase_times_including_this Real)\n                            (increased_quarters_including_this Real)\n                            (has_unincreased_quarter_in_last_four Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and commitment_or_obligation_outstanding\n           is_test_period_end_on_or_after_2014_09_30)\n      (<= leverage_ratio\n          (ite (and (> acquisition_consideration_six_month 50000000.0)\n                    election_notice_given\n                    in_increase_window\n                    (<= increase_times_including_this 4.0)\n                    (<= increased_quarters_including_this 12.0)\n                    has_unincreased_quarter_in_last_four)\n               3.0\n               2.75))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "commitment_or_obligation_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True iff any Lender has a Commitment or any Obligation remains unpaid or outstanding at the observation.",
      "source_quote": "so long as any Lender has a Commitment hereunder or any Obligation remains unpaid or outstanding"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_test_period_end_on_or_after_2014_09_30",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation is the last day of a Test Period, and that Test Period ends on or after September 30, 2014.",
      "source_quote": "as of the last day of each Test Period, commencing with the Test Period ending on September 30, 2014"
    },
    {
      "name": "leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Leverage Ratio as of the last day of the Test Period, expressed as X for X:1.00.",
      "source_quote": "a Leverage Ratio of not greater than 2.75:1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "acquisition_consideration_six_month",
      "meaning": "Aggregate consideration paid in USD for all Permitted Acquisitions or other permitted Acquisitions consummated during the relevant six consecutive month period.",
      "source_quote": "the aggregate consideration paid in connection with all Permitted Acquisitions or other Acquisitions permitted hereunder consummated during any six (6) consecutive month period exceeds $50,000,000"
    },
    {
      "name": "election_notice_given",
      "meaning": "True iff the Borrower elected the increase by written notice to the Administrative Agent, with the reasonably detailed description of the acquisitions and consideration paid.",
      "source_quote": "at the election of the Borrower by written notice to the Administrative Agent"
    },
    {
      "name": "in_increase_window",
      "meaning": "True iff the Fiscal Quarter of this Test Period is the Fiscal Quarter of the election or one of the immediately following three Fiscal Quarters.",
      "source_quote": "for the current Fiscal Quarter and the immediately following three Fiscal Quarters"
    },
    {
      "name": "increase_times_including_this",
      "meaning": "Number of times the Maximum Leverage Threshold has been increased under the proviso during the term of the Agreement, counting the election being relied on.",
      "source_quote": "more than four times"
    },
    {
      "name": "increased_quarters_including_this",
      "meaning": "Number of Fiscal Quarters in which the Maximum Leverage Threshold has been increased during the term, counting the quarters covered by the election being relied on.",
      "source_quote": "with respect to more than twelve Fiscal Quarters"
    },
    {
      "name": "has_unincreased_quarter_in_last_four",
      "meaning": "True iff in the most recently ended four consecutive Fiscal Quarter period there is at least one Fiscal Quarter in respect of which the Maximum Leverage Threshold has not been increased.",
      "source_quote": "unless in the most recently ended four consecutive Fiscal Quarter period there shall be at least one Fiscal Quarter in respect of which the Maximum Leverage Threshold has not been increased"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The threshold is 2.75 by default and 3.00 only if all increase conditions hold: consideration above $50,000,000, election by notice, within the election quarter plus the next three, at most four increases and twelve increased quarters, and at least one unincreased quarter in the last four. The source states four times and twelve quarters as parenthetical alternatives, so I required both limits, which is the conservative reading. The covenant applies only while a Commitment or Obligation is outstanding. There is no division, so no unresolved-denominator issue arises."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; covenant_period_active: true iff the observation time is on or after the Effective Date and the covenant has not yet ended, i.e. the Total Commitment has not been terminated, Notes remain outstanding, or the Loans, interest, Fees and other Obligations are not yet paid in full.\n; consolidated_indebtedness: Borrower's Consolidated Indebtedness at the observation time (Real, currency units, numerator of the ratio).\n; consolidated_net_worth: Borrower's Consolidated Net Worth at the observation time (Real, same currency units, denominator of the ratio).\n; before_first_anniversary: true iff the observation time is prior to the first anniversary of the Initial Borrowing Date.\n; before_second_anniversary: true iff the observation time is prior to the second anniversary of the Initial Borrowing Date.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((covenant_period_active Bool) (consolidated_indebtedness Real) (consolidated_net_worth Real) (before_first_anniversary Bool) (before_second_anniversary Bool)) Bool\n  (=> covenant_period_active\n      (<= (/ consolidated_indebtedness consolidated_net_worth)\n          (ite before_first_anniversary 2.5\n               (ite before_second_anniversary 2.25 2.0)))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "covenant_period_active",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation time is on or after the Effective Date and the covenant has not yet ended: the Total Commitment has not been terminated, Notes remain outstanding, or the Loans, interest, Fees and other Obligations are not yet paid in full.",
      "source_quote": "on the Effective Date and thereafter for so long as this Agreement is in effect and until such time as the Total Commitment has been terminated, no Notes remain outstanding and the Loans, together with interest, Fees and all other Obligations incurred hereunder are paid in full"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Consolidated Indebtedness at the observation time (Real, currency units); numerator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "the ratio of (i) Consolidated Indebtedness to (ii) Consolidated Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Consolidated Net Worth at the observation time (Real, same currency units); denominator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "the ratio of (i) Consolidated Indebtedness to (ii) Consolidated Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "before_first_anniversary",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation time is prior to the first anniversary of the Initial Borrowing Date.",
      "source_quote": "at any time prior to the first anniversary of the Initial Borrowing Date"
    },
    {
      "name": "before_second_anniversary",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation time is prior to the second anniversary of the Initial Borrowing Date.",
      "source_quote": "prior to the second anniversary of the Initial Borrowing Date"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio is Consolidated Indebtedness / Consolidated Net Worth, which must be at most 2.5 before the first anniversary, at most 2.25 from the first anniversary until before the second, and at most 2.0 from the second anniversary onward. 'Not greater than' is encoded as <=. The tier is chosen with nested ite, where before_first_anniversary takes precedence. Division by a zero net worth is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the denominator is a variable."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation is as of the end of a fiscal quarter, the date at which Section 4.9(a)-(d) ratios are tested.\n; is_on_or_after_first_test_period: true iff the observed fiscal-quarter period ends on or after March 31, 1997, the first period for which compliance is determined.\n; total_current_assets: Investors' total current assets (GAAP, consistently applied) at the quarter-end observation.\n; total_current_liabilities: Investors' total current liabilities (GAAP, consistently applied) at the quarter-end observation.\n; ebitda_ttm_prior_quarter: EBITDA for the twelve-month period ending on the last day of the immediately preceding fiscal quarter.\n; interest_expense_ttm_prior_quarter: total interest expense deducted in determining net income for the twelve-month period ending on the last day of the immediately preceding fiscal quarter.\n; current_maturities_principal_prior_quarter: all current maturities of principal on all unsubordinated long-term indebtedness of Borrowers, excluding any amount outstanding under the Line of Credit, as of the last day of the immediately preceding fiscal quarter.\n; senior_funded_debt: Senior Funded Debt, i.e. total funded unsubordinated indebtedness of Borrowers per GAAP, including capital leases.\n; term_loan_made: true iff the Term Loan has been made as of the observation (true = from and after the making of the Term Loan; false = prior to it).\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n    (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool)\n    (is_on_or_after_first_test_period Bool)\n    (total_current_assets Real)\n    (total_current_liabilities Real)\n    (ebitda_ttm_prior_quarter Real)\n    (interest_expense_ttm_prior_quarter Real)\n    (current_maturities_principal_prior_quarter Real)\n    (senior_funded_debt Real)\n    (term_loan_made Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end is_on_or_after_first_test_period)\n      (and\n        ; (a) Current Ratio >= 1.20\n        (>= (/ total_current_assets total_current_liabilities) 1.2)\n        ; (b) Debt Service Coverage Ratio >= 1.5\n        (>= (/ ebitda_ttm_prior_quarter\n               (+ interest_expense_ttm_prior_quarter current_maturities_principal_prior_quarter))\n            1.5)\n        ; (c) before Term Loan: Senior Funded Debt / EBITDA <= 5.0; (d) from and after Term Loan: <= 3.5\n        (ite term_loan_made\n             (<= (/ senior_funded_debt ebitda_ttm_prior_quarter) 3.5)\n             (<= (/ senior_funded_debt ebitda_ttm_prior_quarter) 5.0)))))",
