  "notes": "Section 6.12(a) is tested only at fiscal month ends once the $80,000,000 Liquidity trigger has occurred, and requires FCCR >= 1.1. Section 6.12(b) requires Liquidity >= $50,000,000 at every observation. The covenant is the conjunction of both parts. The trigger is modeled as a persistent Boolean input, following the 'beginning on the fiscal month end immediately prior' language, which implies testing continues after the trigger."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; notes_unpaid: True if any of the Notes remain unpaid at the observation time.\n; lender_has_commitment: True if any Lender has any Commitment under this Agreement at the observation time.\n; letter_of_credit_outstanding: True if any Letter of Credit remains outstanding at the observation time.\n; consolidated_funded_debt: Consolidated Funded Debt of the Company at the observation time, as a Real amount in the agreement currency.\n; ebitda: EBITDA of the Company as used in the Section 9.13 ratio at the observation time, as a Real amount in the agreement currency.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((notes_unpaid Bool) (lender_has_commitment Bool) (letter_of_credit_outstanding Bool) (consolidated_funded_debt Real) (ebitda Real)) Bool\n  (=> (or notes_unpaid lender_has_commitment letter_of_credit_outstanding)\n      (not (> (/ consolidated_funded_debt ebitda) 3.5))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "notes_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True if any of the Notes remain unpaid at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "So long as any of the Notes shall remain unpaid"
    },
    {
      "name": "lender_has_commitment",
      "meaning": "True if any Lender has any Commitment under this Agreement at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "any Lender shall have any Commitment under this Agreement"
    },
    {
      "name": "letter_of_credit_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True if any Letter of Credit remains outstanding at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "any Letter of Credit shall remain outstanding"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_funded_debt",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Funded Debt of the Company at the observation time, as a Real amount in the agreement currency (numerator of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "the ratio of Consolidated Funded Debt to EBITDA"
    },
    {
      "name": "ebitda",
      "meaning": "EBITDA of the Company used in the Section 9.13 ratio at the observation time, as a Real amount in the agreement currency (denominator of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "the ratio of Consolidated Funded Debt to EBITDA"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is a negative covenant: the Company shall not permit the ratio to be greater than 3.50 to 1.00. Compliance is therefore ratio <= 3.5, encoded as the negation of ratio > 3.5, with a non-strict boundary. The covenant applies while any one of three conditions holds (Notes unpaid, Commitment outstanding, or Letter of Credit outstanding), so the three flags are joined with OR. 'At any time' is translated pointwise at each observation. The ratio is computed by direct division, so a zero EBITDA is reported by the evaluator as unresolved, and no positivity of EBITDA is assumed. QF_NRA is used because the division is by a variable. The definitions of Consolidated Funded Debt and EBITDA were not supplied, so each is an atomic Real input."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; consolidated_indebtedness: Consolidated Indebtedness of the Company at the observation time (numerator of the ratio), as defined in the agreement, in the same currency units as consolidated_tangible_net_worth.\n; consolidated_tangible_net_worth: Consolidated Tangible Net Worth of the Company at the observation time (denominator of the ratio), as defined in the agreement, in the same currency units as consolidated_indebtedness.\n; is_last_day_of_fiscal_year: true iff the observation time is the last day of a fiscal year of the Company; false at any other time.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((consolidated_indebtedness Real) (consolidated_tangible_net_worth Real) (is_last_day_of_fiscal_year Bool)) Bool\n  (ite is_last_day_of_fiscal_year\n       (<= (/ consolidated_indebtedness consolidated_tangible_net_worth) 6.0)\n       (<= (/ consolidated_indebtedness consolidated_tangible_net_worth) 6.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "consolidated_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Indebtedness of the Company at the observation time (numerator of the ratio), as defined in the agreement, in the same currency units as consolidated_tangible_net_worth.",
      "source_quote": "ratio of Consolidated Indebtedness to Consolidated Tangible Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Tangible Net Worth of the Company at the observation time (denominator of the ratio), as defined in the agreement, in the same currency units as consolidated_indebtedness.",
      "source_quote": "ratio of Consolidated Indebtedness to Consolidated Tangible Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_last_day_of_fiscal_year",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation time is the last day of a fiscal year of the Company; false at any other time.",
      "source_quote": "on and as of the last day of any fiscal year"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio is computed as Consolidated Indebtedness divided by Consolidated Tangible Net Worth. 600% is encoded as 6.0 and 650% as 6.5. The 'exceed' wording makes the limits non-strict, so the ratio must be <= the limit. The 600% limit applies when is_last_day_of_fiscal_year is true, and 650% applies 'at any other time'. A zero denominator is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. No sign or positivity assumptions are made. The lender-consent exception ('unless at any time the Required Banks shall otherwise expressly consent in writing') is not modeled, because no consent-state input is needed to express the numeric test at an observation."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; funded_debt_to_cap_ratio: Consolidated Funded Debt to Capitalization Ratio as of the observation date (atomic ratio, to 1.0).\n; consolidated_leverage_ratio: Consolidated Leverage Ratio as of the observation date (atomic ratio, to 1.0).\n; investment_grade_date_occurred: true iff the observation date is on or after the Investment Grade Date.\n; consolidated_funded_debt: Consolidated Funded Debt at the observation date.\n; consolidated_ebitda_midstream_ltm: Consolidated EBITDA-Midstream for the four fiscal quarters ending on the observation date, or ending on the last day of the most recently ended fiscal quarter if the date is not a quarter end.\n; present_value: the Present Value amount at the observation date, as used in Section 7.11(c)(2).\n; debt_ratings_trigger_period_active: true iff the observation date falls within a Debt Ratings Trigger Period.\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n    (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool)\n    (funded_debt_to_cap_ratio Real)\n    (consolidated_leverage_ratio Real)\n    (investment_grade_date_occurred Bool)\n    (consolidated_funded_debt Real)\n    (consolidated_ebitda_midstream_ltm Real)\n    (present_value Real)\n    (debt_ratings_trigger_period_active Bool)) Bool\n  (and\n    ; 7.11(a): at each fiscal quarter end, ratio must not exceed 0.6\n    (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (<= funded_debt_to_cap_ratio 0.6))\n    ; 7.11(b): at each fiscal quarter end, leverage ratio must not exceed 3.5, ceasing from the Investment Grade Date\n    (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end (not investment_grade_date_occurred))\n        (<= consolidated_leverage_ratio 3.5))\n    ; 7.11(c): only during a Debt Ratings Trigger Period, debt <= 3.5 * EBITDA-Midstream + Present Value / 1.50\n    (=> debt_ratings_trigger_period_active\n        (<= consolidated_funded_debt\n            (+ (* 3.5 consolidated_ebitda_midstream_ltm) (/ present_value 1.50))))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.",
      "source_quote": "As of the last day of each fiscal quarter of the Borrower"
    },
    {
