    },
    {
      "name": "lease_interest_factor",
      "meaning": "Estimate of the portion of minimum rents under operating leases representing the interest factor, for the same four-quarter period, consolidated.",
      "source_quote": "estimate of that portion of minimum rents under operating leases representing the interest factor"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Pointwise at each fiscal quarter end: Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio = Cash Flow / Fixed Charges, where Cash Flow includes Fixed Charges as an addend and Fixed Charges = Interest Expense + lease interest factor. 'Not ... less than 1.30 to 1' is encoded as ratio >= 1.30. Division by zero when Fixed Charges is 0 is left to the evaluator as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the divisor is a non-constant term."
