{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n  (commitment_outstanding Bool) ; True if any Bank has any Commitment outstanding hereunder at the observation time\n  (obligation_unpaid_or_unsatisfied Bool) ; True if any Loan or other Obligation remains unpaid or unsatisfied at the observation time\n  (majority_banks_written_waiver Bool) ; True if the Majority Banks have waived compliance with Section 7.15 in writing at the observation time\n  (total_debt Real) ; St. Jude's Total Debt at the observation time, as defined in the agreement (definition not supplied; atomic input)\n  (total_capitalization Real) ; St. Jude's Total Capitalization at the observation time, as defined in the agreement (definition not supplied; atomic input)\n  ) Bool\n  (=> (and (or commitment_outstanding obligation_unpaid_or_unsatisfied)\n           (not majority_banks_written_waiver))\n      (<= (/ total_debt total_capitalization) 0.55)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "commitment_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True if any Bank has any Commitment outstanding hereunder at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "any Bank shall have any Commitment hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "obligation_unpaid_or_unsatisfied",
      "meaning": "True if any Loan or other Obligation remains unpaid or unsatisfied at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "any Loan or other Obligation shall remain unpaid or unsatisfied"
    },
    {
      "name": "majority_banks_written_waiver",
      "meaning": "True if the Majority Banks have waived compliance with Section 7.15 in writing at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "unless the Majority Banks waive compliance in writing"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_debt",
      "meaning": "St. Jude's Total Debt at the observation time, as defined in the agreement; definition not supplied, so it is an atomic Real input.",
      "source_quote": "Total Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "St. Jude's Total Capitalization at the observation time, as defined in the agreement; definition not supplied, so it is an atomic Real input.",
      "source_quote": "Total Capitalization"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies while any Commitment is outstanding OR any Loan/Obligation is unpaid or unsatisfied, and only if the Majority Banks have not waived compliance in writing. When it applies, the ratio of Total Debt to Total Capitalization must not be greater than 55%, so the constraint is non-strict: ratio <= 0.55. 'At any time' is translated pointwise. Division is kept as a division, so a zero Total Capitalization is reported as unresolved by the evaluator. The logic is QF_NRA because the ratio divides one variable by another."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; covenant_termination_conditions_not_yet_satisfied: true iff the Article VI covenant period is still running, i.e. NOT all of the following hold: Commitments expired or terminated; principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees, expenses and other amounts payable under any Loan Document (other than contingent amounts not yet due) paid in full; all Letters of Credit expired or terminated (or cash collateralized at 103% of the aggregate undrawn amount of all outstanding Letters of Credit); all LC Disbursements reimbursed.\n; is_last_date_of_fiscal_quarter: true iff the observation date is the last date of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; is_on_or_after_september_30_2006: true iff the observation date is on or after September 30, 2006 (the first test period ends September 30, 2006).\n; consolidated_ebitda: Consolidated EBITDA for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Borrower ending on the observation date.\n; consolidated_cash_interest_expense: Consolidated Cash Interest Expense for the same four-consecutive-fiscal-quarter period ending on the observation date.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((covenant_termination_conditions_not_yet_satisfied Bool) (is_last_date_of_fiscal_quarter Bool) (is_on_or_after_september_30_2006 Bool) (consolidated_ebitda Real) (consolidated_cash_interest_expense Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and covenant_termination_conditions_not_yet_satisfied\n           is_last_date_of_fiscal_quarter\n           is_on_or_after_september_30_2006)\n      (>= (/ consolidated_ebitda consolidated_cash_interest_expense) 2.0)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "covenant_termination_conditions_not_yet_satisfied",
      "meaning": "True iff the Article VI covenant period is still running, i.e. NOT all of the following hold: Commitments expired or terminated; principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees, expenses and other amounts payable under any Loan Document (other than contingent amounts not yet due) paid in full; all Letters of Credit expired or terminated (or cash collateralized at 103% of the aggregate undrawn amount of all outstanding Letters of Credit); all LC Disbursements reimbursed.",
      "source_quote": "Until the Commitments have expired or been terminated and the principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees, expenses and other amounts payable (other than contingent amounts not yet due) under any Loan Document have been paid in full and all Letters of Credit have expired or been terminated (or cash collateralized in an amount equal to 103% of the aggregate undrawn amount of all outstanding Letters of Credit) and all LC Disbursements shall have been reimbursed"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_last_date_of_fiscal_quarter",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last date of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.",
      "source_quote": "as of the last date of any fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_on_or_after_september_30_2006",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is on or after September 30, 2006, the end of the first test period.",
      "source_quote": "beginning with the period ending September 30, 2006"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_ebitda",
      "meaning": "Consolidated EBITDA for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Borrower ending on the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated EBITDA"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_cash_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Cash Interest Expense for the same period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Cash Interest Expense"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is violated if EBITDA / Cash Interest Expense is less than 2.00 to 1.00, so compliance is ratio >= 2.0 (non-strict). The test applies only at fiscal quarter-end dates on or after September 30, 2006, while the Article VI covenant period is running. The ratio is computed by division, so a zero cash interest expense is reported by the evaluator as unresolved, and no positivity is assumed. Logic is QF_NRA because the division is by a variable. Consolidated EBITDA and Consolidated Cash Interest Expense are atomic inputs because their definitions were not supplied."
}

{
