{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_year_end: True exactly when this observation is the last day of a fiscal year, so the Section 7.11 ratio test applies for that fiscal year.\n; net_premiums_written: Net Premiums Written of all Subsidiaries of FCIG which are Regulated Insurance Companies (combined basis) for the fiscal year ending at this observation.\n; policyholder_surplus: Policyholder Surplus of all Subsidiaries of FCIG which are Regulated Insurance Companies (combined basis) on the last day of that fiscal year.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_year_end Bool) (net_premiums_written Real) (policyholder_surplus Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_year_end (<= (/ net_premiums_written policyholder_surplus) 3.0)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_year_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when this observation is the last day of a fiscal year, so the Section 7.11 ratio test applies for that fiscal year.",
      "source_quote": "on the last day of such fiscal year"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_premiums_written",
      "meaning": "Net Premiums Written of all Subsidiaries of FCIG which are Regulated Insurance Companies (combined basis) for the fiscal year ending at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "Net Premiums Written of all Subsidiaries of FCIG which are Regulated Insurance Companies (determined on a combined basis) for any fiscal year"
    },
    {
      "name": "policyholder_surplus",
      "meaning": "Policyholder Surplus of all Subsidiaries of FCIG which are Regulated Insurance Companies (combined basis) on the last day of that fiscal year.",
      "source_quote": "Policyholder Surplus of all Subsidiaries of FCIG which are Regulated Insurance Companies (determined on a combined basis) on the last day of such fiscal year"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant caps the ratio of Net Premiums Written to Policyholder Surplus at 3.0:1.0, so the test is non-strict (<= 3.0). The test is applied only on fiscal-year-end observations, because the ratio is defined per fiscal year with surplus taken on its last day. The ratio is kept as a division, not cross-multiplied, so a negative surplus is not misjudged. A zero surplus is reported by the evaluator as unresolved. The logic is QF_NRA because the division is by a variable. The general lead-in about the Borrower's obligations continuing until the Total Commitment terminates and the Loans are repaid is a duration condition. It is treated as given for observations in the supplied history and is not modeled."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; bank_has_obligation_to_lend: true iff Bank has an obligation to lend at the observation time.\n; outstanding_obligations_exist: true iff there are outstanding Obligations at the observation time.\n; quick_assets: Borrower's Quick Assets at the observation time (numerator, item (A)).\n; current_liabilities: Borrower's Current Liabilities at the observation time.\n; other_obligations_owing_to_bank_not_in_current_liabilities: Obligations of Borrower owing to Bank at the observation time, only to the extent not already categorized as Current Liabilities of Borrower.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((bank_has_obligation_to_lend Bool) (outstanding_obligations_exist Bool) (quick_assets Real) (current_liabilities Real) (other_obligations_owing_to_bank_not_in_current_liabilities Real)) Bool\n  (=> (or bank_has_obligation_to_lend outstanding_obligations_exist)\n      (>= (/ quick_assets (+ current_liabilities other_obligations_owing_to_bank_not_in_current_liabilities)) 1.25)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "bank_has_obligation_to_lend",
      "meaning": "True iff Bank has an obligation to lend at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "for so long as Bank has an obligation to lend"
    },
    {
      "name": "outstanding_obligations_exist",
      "meaning": "True iff there are outstanding Obligations at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "or there are outstanding Obligations"
    },
    {
      "name": "quick_assets",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Quick Assets at the observation time (numerator, item (A)).",
      "source_quote": "Quick Assets"
    },
    {
      "name": "current_liabilities",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Current Liabilities at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "Current Liabilities"
    },
    {
      "name": "other_obligations_owing_to_bank_not_in_current_liabilities",
      "meaning": "Obligations of Borrower owing to Bank at the observation time, only to the extent not already categorized as Current Liabilities of Borrower.",
      "source_quote": "any other Obligations of Borrower owing to Bank to the extent they are not otherwise categorized as Current Liabilities of Borrower"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies while Bank has an obligation to lend OR there are outstanding Obligations, so the two Boolean inputs are joined with OR in the antecedent. The requirement is (A) / (B) >= 1.25, where B = Current Liabilities + other Obligations owing to Bank not already counted as Current Liabilities. Division is kept literally, so the evaluator reports a zero denominator as unresolved, and the logic is QF_NRA because the denominator is a variable. The source says 'at all times and tested as of the last day of each month'. I translated it pointwise at every observation and did not add a month-end flag, because that would limit the check to month-ends and drop the at-all-times requirement. Month-end observations are still covered, since the check applies at every observation."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_last_day_of_calendar_month: true exactly when the observation date is the last day of a calendar month (the date as of which the ratio must be maintained).\n; total_liabilities: Borrower's Total Liabilities as of the observation date, in currency units, before deducting Subordinated Debt.\n; subordinated_debt: Borrower's Subordinated Debt as of the observation date, in currency units.\n; tangible_net_worth: Borrower's Tangible Net Worth as of the observation date, in currency units, before adding Subordinated Debt.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_last_day_of_calendar_month Bool) (total_liabilities Real) (subordinated_debt Real) (tangible_net_worth Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_last_day_of_calendar_month\n      (<= (/ (- total_liabilities subordinated_debt) (+ tangible_net_worth subordinated_debt)) 1.45)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_last_day_of_calendar_month",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation date is the last day of a calendar month (the date as of which the ratio must be maintained).",
      "source_quote": "as of the last day of each calendar month"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_liabilities",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Total Liabilities as of the observation date, in currency units, before deducting Subordinated Debt.",
      "source_quote": "Total Liabilities"
    },
    {
      "name": "subordinated_debt",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Subordinated Debt as of the observation date, in currency units.",
      "source_quote": "Subordinated Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Tangible Net Worth as of the observation date, in currency units, before adding Subordinated Debt.",
      "source_quote": "Tangible Net Worth"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio (Total Liabilities less Subordinated Debt) / (Tangible Net Worth plus Subordinated Debt) must be at most 1.45 (\"not more than 1.45 to 1.00\", a non-strict bound) on month-end observations. The division is kept literally, so a zero denominator is reported by the evaluator as unresolved. No sign or positivity assumptions are added. QF_NRA is used because the division is by a variable expression. The until-payment-in-full and commitment-period preamble is treated as the general duration of the covenant and is not modeled as a separate input, since it is handled by the pointwise observation set."
}

{"status":"formalized","smt2":"(set-logic QF_LRA)
(define-fun covenant_holds (
  (is_covenant_compliance_date Bool) ; true iff the observation date is a Covenant Compliance Date, as of which the Borrower Leverage Ratio is determined
  (borrower_leverage_ratio Real) ; Borrower Leverage Ratio of the Borrower determined as of the observation date, expressed as a number (0.65 means 0.65 to 1)
) Bool
  (=> is_covenant_compliance_date (<= borrower_leverage_ratio 0.65)))","symbols":[{"name":"is_covenant_compliance_date","meaning":"True iff the observation date is a Covenant Compliance Date, the date as of which the Borrower Leverage Ratio is determined.","source_quote":"determined as of any Covenant Compliance Date"},{"name":"borrower_leverage_ratio","meaning":"Borrower Leverage Ratio determined as of the observation date, as a real number (0.65 corresponds to 0.65 to 1).","source_quote":"the Borrower Leverage Ratio, determined as of any Covenant Compliance Date, to be greater than 0.65 to 1"}],"notes":"The covenant prohibits the ratio from being greater than 0.65 to 1, so compliance is ratio <= 0.65 (non-strict) on Covenant Compliance Dates. The Borrower Leverage Ratio is kept atomic because no definition is supplied. The 'so long as Commitments remain outstanding or any Note remains unpaid' and Required Lender consent conditions are not modeled as inputs; the evaluator is expected to supply observations only in that period, and no consent state is encoded."}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true exactly when the observation is at the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; total_indebtedness: the Borrower's Total Indebtedness at the observation date (numerator of the ratio; definition not supplied).\n; adjusted_tangible_capital: the Borrower's Adjusted Tangible Capital at the observation date (denominator of the ratio; definition not supplied).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (total_indebtedness Real) (adjusted_tangible_capital Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (<= (/ total_indebtedness adjusted_tangible_capital) 2.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation is at the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.",
      "source_quote": "measured at the end of each fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "The Borrower's Total Indebtedness at the observation date (numerator of the ratio; definition not supplied).",
      "source_quote": "ratio of its Total Indebtedness to Adjusted Tangible Capital"
    },
    {
      "name": "adjusted_tangible_capital",
      "meaning": "The Borrower's Adjusted Tangible Capital at the observation date (denominator of the ratio; definition not supplied).",
      "source_quote": "Total Indebtedness to Adjusted Tangible Capital"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Section 6.12 prohibits the ratio from being more than 2.50 to 1.00, so the compliant condition is ratio <= 2.5, a non-strict bound. The covenant applies only when is_fiscal_quarter_end is true. The ratio is computed as Total Indebtedness divided by Adjusted Tangible Capital, and a zero denominator is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the division is by a variable. The lead-in preamble (consent in writing, Subsidiaries) is not modeled because it supplies no numeric condition. No positivity assumptions are made."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; consolidated_indebtedness: Consolidated Indebtedness of the Company at the observation time (numerator of the ratio; currency units, same as the denominator).\n; consolidated_tangible_net_worth: Consolidated Tangible Net Worth of the Company at the observation time (denominator of the ratio; same currency units).\n; is_last_day_of_fiscal_year: true iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal year of the Company (the 600% limit applies); false at any other time (the 650% limit applies).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((consolidated_indebtedness Real) (consolidated_tangible_net_worth Real) (is_last_day_of_fiscal_year Bool)) Bool\n  (ite is_last_day_of_fiscal_year\n       (<= (/ consolidated_indebtedness consolidated_tangible_net_worth) 6.0)\n       (<= (/ consolidated_indebtedness consolidated_tangible_net_worth) 6.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "consolidated_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Indebtedness of the Company at the observation time; numerator of the ratio, in currency units.",
      "source_quote": "ratio of Consolidated Indebtedness to Consolidated Tangible Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Tangible Net Worth of the Company at the observation time; denominator of the ratio, in the same currency units.",
      "source_quote": "ratio of Consolidated Indebtedness to Consolidated Tangible Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_last_day_of_fiscal_year",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal year, so the 600% limit applies; false at any other time, when the 650% limit applies.",
      "source_quote": "on and as of the last day of any fiscal year"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio is computed as Consolidated Indebtedness divided by Consolidated Tangible Net Worth. Percentages are converted to decimals (600% = 6.0, 650% = 6.5). The covenant says the ratio must not exceed the limit, so the comparison is non-strict (<=). A zero denominator is reported by the evaluator as unresolved, and no positivity of tangible net worth is assumed. The underlying definitions of Consolidated Indebtedness and Consolidated Tangible Net Worth are not supplied, so each is an atomic Real input. QF_NRA is used because the division is by a variable."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; is_test_period_end: true iff the observation date is the last day of a period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Company (or, if less, the number of full fiscal quarters since the Closing Date) ending with any fiscal quarter.\n; consolidated_leverage_ratio: Consolidated Leverage Ratio as at the observation date, as a decimal fraction (30% = 0.30).\n; consolidated_tangible_net_worth: Consolidated Tangible Net Worth at the observation time, in US dollars.\n; net_cash_proceeds_post_closing_equity: cumulative Net Cash Proceeds, in US dollars, of all issuances by the Company of shares of its Capital Stock consummated after the Closing Date, as of the observation time.\n; company_solvency_ratio: Solvency Ratio of the Company as at the observation date, as a decimal fraction (135% = 1.35).\n; has_material_insurance_subsidiary: true iff at the observation date there is at least one Insurance Subsidiary that is a Material Subsidiary.\n; max_material_insurance_subsidiary_solvency_ratio: highest Solvency Ratio, as a decimal fraction, among Insurance Subsidiaries that are Material Subsidiaries as at the observation date. It is only used when has_material_insurance_subsidiary is true.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_test_period_end Bool)\n                            (consolidated_leverage_ratio Real)\n                            (consolidated_tangible_net_worth Real)\n                            (net_cash_proceeds_post_closing_equity Real)\n                            (company_solvency_ratio Real)\n                            (has_material_insurance_subsidiary Bool)\n                            (max_material_insurance_subsidiary_solvency_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (and\n    ; 6.1(a): the ratio must not exceed 30% at a test period end\n    (=> is_test_period_end (<= consolidated_leverage_ratio 0.3))\n    ; 6.1(b): at any time CTNW >= 700M + 100% of first 200M of proceeds + 50% of the remainder\n    (>= consolidated_tangible_net_worth\n        (+ 700000000.0\n           (ite (<= net_cash_proceeds_post_closing_equity 200000000.0)\n                net_cash_proceeds_post_closing_equity\n                (+ 200000000.0 (* 0.5 (- net_cash_proceeds_post_closing_equity 200000000.0))))))\n    ; 6.1(c)(i): the Company's Solvency Ratio must not be more than 135% at a test period end\n    (=> is_test_period_end (<= company_solvency_ratio 1.35))\n    ; 6.1(c)(ii): same limit for Material Subsidiaries that are Insurance Subsidiaries\n    (=> (and is_test_period_end has_material_insurance_subsidiary)\n        (<= max_material_insurance_subsidiary_solvency_ratio 1.35))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_test_period_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Company (or, if less, the number of full fiscal quarters since the Closing Date) ending with any fiscal quarter.",
      "source_quote": "last day of any period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Company"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Leverage Ratio as at the observation date, as a decimal fraction (30% = 0.30).",
      "source_quote": "Permit the Consolidated Leverage Ratio as at the last day of any period"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Tangible Net Worth at the observation time, in US dollars.",
      "source_quote": "Permit Consolidated Tangible Net Worth at any time to be less than"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_cash_proceeds_post_closing_equity",
      "meaning": "Cumulative Net Cash Proceeds, in US dollars, of all issuances by the Company of shares of its Capital Stock consummated after the Closing Date, as of the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "Net Cash Proceeds of all other issuances by the Company of shares of its Capital Stock consummated after the Closing Date"
    },
    {
      "name": "company_solvency_ratio",
      "meaning": "Solvency Ratio of the Company as at the observation date, as a decimal fraction (135% = 1.35).",
      "source_quote": "Permit the Solvency Ratio of (i) the Company"
    },
    {
      "name": "has_material_insurance_subsidiary",
      "meaning": "True iff at the observation date there is at least one Insurance Subsidiary that is a Material Subsidiary.",
      "source_quote": "any Insurance Subsidiary which is a Material Subsidiary"
    },
    {
      "name": "max_material_insurance_subsidiary_solvency_ratio",
      "meaning": "Highest Solvency Ratio, as a decimal fraction, among Insurance Subsidiaries that are Material Subsidiaries as at the observation date. It is only used when has_material_insurance_subsidiary is true.",
      "source_quote": "any Insurance Subsidiary which is a Material Subsidiary"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The percentages are encoded as decimal fractions (30% = 0.3, 135% = 1.35). The tangible net worth floor is 700,000,000 plus 100% of the first 200,000,000 of cumulative post-closing equity Net Cash Proceeds plus 50% of the remainder. It is encoded with ite and assumes no nonnegativity. The 'any Insurance Subsidiary' limit is checked through the maximum ratio across Material Subsidiaries that are Insurance Subsidiaries, supplied by the evaluator. The clause (c) test-period condition is read as the same four-quarter period-end test as clause (a). The source's literal ordering of '(i)' and '(ii)' in (c) is garbled, but the meaning is clear."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; consolidated_indebtedness: aggregate outstanding principal amount of all Consolidated Indebtedness, in currency units, as of the observation date.\n; total_capitalization: Total Capitalization, in currency units, as of the observation date (atomic input; no definition supplied).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (consolidated_indebtedness Real) (total_capitalization Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (<= consolidated_indebtedness (* 0.65 total_capitalization))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.",
      "source_quote": "as of the end of any fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Aggregate outstanding principal amount of all Consolidated Indebtedness, in currency units, as of the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "the aggregate outstanding principal amount of all Consolidated Indebtedness"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "Total Capitalization, in currency units, as of the observation date. It is an atomic input because no definition is supplied.",
      "source_quote": "Total Capitalization"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant forbids Consolidated Indebtedness from exceeding 65% of Total Capitalization, so compliance is indebtedness <= 0.65 * Total Capitalization (non-strict). It applies only as of fiscal quarter-end observations. The ratio is written as a multiplication, so no division occurs. The 'so long as any Commitment/Obligations are outstanding' lead-in and the Required Lenders consent exception are not modeled, since the supplied observations cover periods when the covenant is in force and the source gives no consent-state input. No positivity assumptions are made on the inputs."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio: Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio as of the observation date (atomic Real, definition not supplied), expressed as x in x:1.00.\n; consolidated_total_leverage_ratio: Consolidated Total Leverage Ratio as of the observation date (atomic Real, definition not supplied), expressed as x in x:1.00.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: True iff the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_ending_on_or_after_2016_06_30: True iff the Fiscal Quarter ending on the observation date ends on or after June 30, 2016.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_ending_2016_06_30_to_2016_12_31: True iff the Fiscal Quarter ending on the observation date ends within the period from June 30, 2016 to and including December 31, 2016.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_ending_on_or_after_2017_03_31: True iff the Fiscal Quarter ending on the observation date ends on or after March 31, 2017.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio Real)\n                            (consolidated_total_leverage_ratio Real)\n                            (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool)\n                            (is_fiscal_quarter_ending_on_or_after_2016_06_30 Bool)\n                            (is_fiscal_quarter_ending_2016_06_30_to_2016_12_31 Bool)\n                            (is_fiscal_quarter_ending_on_or_after_2017_03_31 Bool)) Bool\n  (and\n    ; (a) interest coverage must not be less than 3.00:1.00\n    (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end is_fiscal_quarter_ending_on_or_after_2016_06_30)\n        (>= consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio 3.0))\n    ; (b)(i) leverage must not be greater than 4.00:1.00 for quarters ending 6/30/2016 through 12/31/2016\n    (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end is_fiscal_quarter_ending_2016_06_30_to_2016_12_31)\n        (<= consolidated_total_leverage_ratio 4.0))\n    ; (b)(ii) leverage must not be greater than 3.75:1.00 for quarters ending on and after 3/31/2017\n    (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end is_fiscal_quarter_ending_on_or_after_2017_03_31)\n        (<= consolidated_total_leverage_ratio 3.75))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio as of the observation date (atomic Real, definition not supplied), expressed as x in x:1.00.",
      "source_quote": "Permit the Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio as of the last day of any Fiscal Quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_total_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Total Leverage Ratio as of the observation date (atomic Real, definition not supplied), expressed as x in x:1.00.",
      "source_quote": "Permit the Consolidated Total Leverage Ratio as of the last day of any Fiscal Quarter of the Borrower"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter.",
      "source_quote": "as of the last day of any Fiscal Quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_ending_on_or_after_2016_06_30",
      "meaning": "True iff the Fiscal Quarter ending on the observation date ends on or after June 30, 2016.",
      "source_quote": "beginning with the Fiscal Quarter ending June 30, 2016"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_ending_2016_06_30_to_2016_12_31",
      "meaning": "True iff the Fiscal Quarter ending on the observation date ends within the period from June 30, 2016 to and including December 31, 2016.",
      "source_quote": "for any Fiscal Quarter ending during the period from June 30, 2016 to and including December 31, 2016"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_ending_on_or_after_2017_03_31",
      "meaning": "True iff the Fiscal Quarter ending on the observation date ends on or after March 31, 2017.",
      "source_quote": "for any Fiscal Quarter ending on and after March 31, 2017"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Interest coverage uses >= 3.00 (a breach is strictly less than 3.00). Leverage uses <= 4.00 and <= 3.75 (a breach is strictly greater). Ratios are atomic inputs because their definitions are not supplied. Calendar applicability is supplied as Boolean flags. The leverage covenant has no stated threshold before June 30, 2016, so no constraint applies there. The Article VII lead-in (until the Facility Termination Date) is handled by pointwise evaluation over the supplied observations."
