  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies until both the Commitments have ended and all Loans and fees are paid in full, so it is active whenever not both of those conditions hold. When active, the ratio of Consolidated EBITDA to Consolidated Interest Expense must be at least 4.0 (violated only if strictly less than 4.0). The ratio is kept as a division, so a zero interest expense is reported by the evaluator as unresolved; no sign or positivity assumptions are made. QF_NRA is used because the divisor is a variable. The 'any period of four consecutive fiscal quarters' language is handled pointwise: each observation supplies the trailing four-quarter figures."
}

{
