  "notes": "Encoded the two objectively quantifiable AIRCOA covenants in 8.09(a): (iv) the fiscal-year fee cap of 4% of Gross Revenues (non-strict, since the text prohibits exceeding it), and (v) the ban on paying management fees while not in compliance with Section 8.10. The cap is evaluated pointwise using the fiscal-year figures supplied at each observation. The remaining clauses are omitted because they are qualitative or consent-based and use undefined terms such as 'promptly', 'material', 'reasonable efforts', 'unreasonably withheld' and 'prevailing market rate'. That covers 8.09(a)(i)-(iii) and 8.09(b). Section 8.10's own test is not restated, so its compliance is an input Boolean."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n  (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) ; true iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Company\n  (any_advance_unpaid Bool) ; true iff any Advance remains unpaid at the observation time\n  (any_lender_has_commitment Bool) ; true iff any Lender has any Commitment under the agreement at the observation time\n  (pre_tax_income_continuing_ops_4q Real) ; Pre-Tax Income from Continuing Operations for the four fiscal quarters then ended\n  (consolidated_interest_expense_4q Real) ; Consolidated Interest Expense for the same four fiscal quarters then ended\n) Bool\n  (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end (or any_advance_unpaid any_lender_has_commitment))\n      (>= (/ pre_tax_income_continuing_ops_4q consolidated_interest_expense_4q) 2.0)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Company.",
      "source_quote": "as of the end of each fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "any_advance_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True iff any Advance remains unpaid at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "So long as any Advance shall remain unpaid"
    },
    {
      "name": "any_lender_has_commitment",
      "meaning": "True iff any Lender has any Commitment under the agreement at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "any Lender shall have any Commitment hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "pre_tax_income_continuing_ops_4q",
      "meaning": "Pre-Tax Income from Continuing Operations for the four fiscal quarters ended at the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "Pre-Tax Income from Continuing Operations for the four fiscal quarters then ended"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_expense_4q",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Expense for the same four fiscal quarters ended at the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Interest Expense for such four fiscal quarters"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies when it is a fiscal quarter end and either an Advance is unpaid or a Lender has a Commitment (the 'or' in 'any Advance ... or any Lender'). Compliance requires the ratio of pre-tax income to interest expense to be at least 2.0 (non-strict, 'not less than 2.0 to 1.0'). The ratio is kept as a division, so a zero interest expense is reported by the evaluator as unresolved. No positivity assumptions are added. QF_NRA is used because the division has a variable denominator."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true exactly when the observation date is a fiscal quarter end of the Borrower, the date at which the Total Leverage Ratio is measured.\n; total_leverage_ratio: Total Leverage Ratio of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries, calculated on a consolidated basis, as a real number x for x:1.0, at this observation.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (total_leverage_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (<= total_leverage_ratio 4.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation date is a fiscal quarter end of the Borrower, the date at which the Total Leverage Ratio is measured.",
      "source_quote": "measured at each fiscal quarter end"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Total Leverage Ratio of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries, calculated on a consolidated basis, as a real number x for x:1.0, at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "Total Leverage Ratio less than or equal to 4.5:1.0"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The pointwise reading is: if the observation is a fiscal quarter end, the Total Leverage Ratio must be <= 4.5 (non-strict, 4.5:1.0). The source says 'at all times, measured at each fiscal quarter end', so the test applies only at quarter-end observations. The Total Leverage Ratio definition is not supplied, so it is an atomic Real input. The consolidated-basis requirement is recorded in its parameter meaning. The proviso on additional or more restrictive covenants given to other Indebtedness holders is not encoded. It is a conditional amendment whose content depends on other agreements and has no fixed numeric terms, so it cannot be expressed as a threshold here. The encoded constraint is the stated 4.5:1.0 maximum."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n  (covenant_term_in_effect Bool) ; True when the observation falls within the Section 6.09 covenant term: on or after the Closing Date, and not yet after the point where the Commitments have expired or terminated, principal and interest on each Loan and all fees payable have been paid in full, all Letters of Credit have expired, terminated or been cash collateralized on terms satisfactory to the Issuing Bank, and all L/C Disbursements have been reimbursed.\n  (icr_test_period_ends_after_closing Bool) ; True when the observed Test Period ends after the Closing Date, so Section 6.09(a) applies at this observation.\n  (consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio Real) ; Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio for the observed Test Period, as a ratio to 1.0 (for example 2.50 means 2.50 to 1.0).\n  (leverage_test_date_is_last_day_of_test_period_ending_after_closing Bool) ; True when the observation date is the last day of a Test Period ending after the Closing Date, so Section 6.09(b) applies at this observation.\n  (consolidated_net_leverage_ratio Real) ; Consolidated Net Leverage Ratio as of the last day of the observed Test Period, as a ratio to 1.0 (for example 5.50 means 5.50 to 1.0).\n) Bool\n  (=> covenant_term_in_effect\n      (and\n        ; 6.09(a): the ratio must not be less than 2.50 to 1.0\n        (=> icr_test_period_ends_after_closing\n            (>= consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio 2.5))\n        ; 6.09(b): the ratio must not be greater than 5.50 to 1.0\n        (=> leverage_test_date_is_last_day_of_test_period_ending_after_closing\n            (<= consolidated_net_leverage_ratio 5.5)))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "covenant_term_in_effect",
      "meaning": "True when the observation falls within the Section 6.09 covenant term: on or after the Closing Date, and not yet after the point where the Commitments have expired or terminated, principal and interest on each Loan and all fees payable have been paid in full, all Letters of Credit have expired, terminated or been cash collateralized on terms satisfactory to the Issuing Bank, and all L/C Disbursements have been reimbursed.",
      "source_quote": "From the Closing Date until the Commitments have expired or terminated and the principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees payable hereunder have been paid in full and all Letters of Credit have expired or terminated or been cash collateralized on terms satisfactory to the Issuing Bank and all L/C Disbursements shall have been reimbursed"
