{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; consolidated_fixed_charge_coverage_ratio: Consolidated Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio of Holdings and its Subsidiaries as of the observation date, as a plain ratio (1.00 to 1.00 = 1.0). It is determined for the most recently ended four consecutive Fiscal Quarters for which Administrative Agent has received financial statements. Before the first day of the Fiscal Quarter after the end of the full four-Fiscal-Quarter period commencing after the Closing Date, it is determined for the period from the Closing Date to the most recent Fiscal Quarter end for which Administrative Agent has received financial statements. Treated as an atomic input because its arithmetic definition is not supplied.\n; is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter: true iff the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter.\n; covenant_trigger_event_occurring_and_continuing: true iff a Covenant Trigger Event has occurred and is continuing at the observation date.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((consolidated_fixed_charge_coverage_ratio Real) (is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter Bool) (covenant_trigger_event_occurring_and_continuing Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter covenant_trigger_event_occurring_and_continuing)\n      (not (< consolidated_fixed_charge_coverage_ratio 1.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "consolidated_fixed_charge_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio of Holdings and its Subsidiaries as of the observation date, as a plain ratio (1.00 to 1.00 = 1.0). It is determined for the most recently ended four consecutive Fiscal Quarters for which Administrative Agent has received financial statements. Before the first day of the Fiscal Quarter after the end of the full four-Fiscal-Quarter period commencing after the Closing Date, it is determined for the period from the Closing Date to the most recent Fiscal Quarter end for which Administrative Agent has received financial statements. Atomic input because its arithmetic definition is not supplied.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter.",
      "source_quote": "as of the last day of each Fiscal Quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "covenant_trigger_event_occurring_and_continuing",
      "meaning": "True iff a Covenant Trigger Event has occurred and is continuing at the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "upon the occurrence and during the continuance of a Covenant Trigger Event"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant prohibits permitting the ratio to be less than 1.00 to 1.00, so compliance is ratio >= 1.0, written as (not (< ratio 1.0)). The covenant applies only when the observation is a Fiscal Quarter end and a Covenant Trigger Event is occurring and continuing, which gives the implication. The look-back period rule (four quarters, or the Closing Date stub period) is carried in the ratio input's meaning because the ratio's definition is not supplied. The source context was empty, so the definition of Covenant Trigger Event is left as a Boolean input."
