      "source_quote": "Maintain a Consolidated Leverage Ratio"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio as determined as of the last day of the Fiscal Period, expressed as X in X:1.00. Kept atomic because its definition is not supplied.",
      "source_quote": "Maintain a Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Section 7.14(a) and (b) are both conjoined, and each applies on the last day of each Fiscal Period. The leverage test is non-strict, \"not greater than 3:00 to 1.00\" gives <= 3.0. The coverage test is non-strict, \"not less than 3.00 to 1.00\" gives >= 3.0. The ratios are atomic inputs, so no division occurs in the formula. The Article VII lead-in (until the Obligations are paid in full and the Revolving Credit Commitments terminate) is not modeled as a separate input. The evaluator supplies observations only while the covenant is in force."
