{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true exactly when the observation date is a fiscal quarter end (Section 9.1 applies only as of a fiscal quarter end).\n; total_indebtedness: Consolidated Total Indebtedness of the Credit Parties and their Subsidiaries on the observation date (the numerator of the ratio).\n; ebitda_ttm: Consolidated EBITDA for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on or immediately prior to the observation date (the denominator of the ratio).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (total_indebtedness Real) (ebitda_ttm Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (<= (/ total_indebtedness ebitda_ttm) 3.0)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation date is a fiscal quarter end; Section 9.1 applies only as of such a date.",
      "source_quote": "As of any fiscal quarter end"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Total Indebtedness of the Credit Parties and their Subsidiaries on a Consolidated basis on the observation date (numerator of the leverage ratio).",
      "source_quote": "Total Indebtedness on such date"
    },
    {
      "name": "ebitda_ttm",
      "meaning": "Consolidated EBITDA for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on or immediately prior to the observation date (denominator of the leverage ratio).",
      "source_quote": "EBITDA for the period of four (4) consecutive fiscal quarters ending on or immediately prior to such date"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant prohibits the ratio from being greater than 3.00 to 1.0, so compliance is ratio <= 3.0 (non-strict). The ratio is computed as an explicit division, so QF_NRA is used. If EBITDA is zero, the evaluator reports the result as unresolved, per the stated policy. No sign assumptions are made about either input. The consent and termination preamble (Section 13.2, payment in full) is not modeled as an input. The covenant is checked pointwise at each supplied observation."
