{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the end of one of the Company's fiscal quarters (the covenant tests ratios 'as of the end of each of its fiscal quarters').\n; consolidated_ebit: Consolidated EBIT of the Company for the then most-recently ended four fiscal quarters, as of the observation date.\n; consolidated_interest_expense: Consolidated Interest Expense of the Company for the then most-recently ended four fiscal quarters, as of the observation date.\n; consolidated_total_indebtedness: Consolidated Total Indebtedness of the Company as of the observation date (end of the fiscal quarter).\n; consolidated_ebitda: Consolidated EBITDA of the Company for the then most-recently ended four fiscal quarters, as of the observation date.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (consolidated_ebit Real) (consolidated_interest_expense Real) (consolidated_total_indebtedness Real) (consolidated_ebitda Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n      (and (>= (/ consolidated_ebit consolidated_interest_expense) 2.5)\n           (<= (/ consolidated_total_indebtedness consolidated_ebitda) 3.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the end of one of the Company's fiscal quarters, when both ratios are tested.",
      "source_quote": "determined as of the end of each of its fiscal quarters"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_ebit",
      "meaning": "Consolidated EBIT for the then most-recently ended four fiscal quarters, as of the observation date; numerator of the Interest Coverage Ratio.",
      "source_quote": "of (i) Consolidated EBIT to (ii) Consolidated Interest Expense"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Expense for the then most-recently ended four fiscal quarters, as of the observation date; denominator of the Interest Coverage Ratio.",
      "source_quote": "for the then most-recently ended four fiscal quarters, of (i) Consolidated EBIT to (ii) Consolidated Interest Expense"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_total_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Total Indebtedness as of the end of the fiscal quarter at the observation date; numerator of the Leverage Ratio.",
      "source_quote": "of (i) Consolidated Total Indebtedness to (ii) Consolidated EBITDA"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_ebitda",
      "meaning": "Consolidated EBITDA for the then most-recently ended four fiscal quarters, as of the observation date; denominator of the Leverage Ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated EBITDA for the then most-recently ended four fiscal quarters"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Both tests apply at each fiscal quarter end. Interest coverage requires EBIT/Interest >= 2.5, since the covenant forbids a ratio 'less than 2.5 to 1.0'. Leverage requires Debt/EBITDA <= 3.0, since it forbids a ratio 'greater than 3.0 to 1.0'. The ratios are computed with real division, so a zero denominator is reported as unresolved by the evaluator rather than assumed away. QF_NRA is used because division by a variable is nonlinear. The Required Lenders' written-consent waiver is not modeled; the pointwise check covers the unwaived covenant."
}

