{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; commitments_or_obligations_outstanding: true if any Lender has any Commitment, or any Loan or other obligation remains outstanding, unpaid or unsatisfied, before full payment of all amounts due to the Lenders\n; required_lenders_waived_in_writing: true if the Required Lenders have waived compliance with Section 7.1 in writing at this observation\n; is_month_end: true if the observation date is a month-end date at which a Net Capital Ratio is measured\n; broker_ncr_current: Net Capital Ratio of the Broker Subsidiary at the current month-end, as a decimal fraction (7% = 0.07)\n; broker_ncr_prior: Net Capital Ratio of the Broker Subsidiary at the immediately preceding month-end, as a decimal fraction\n; scm_ncr_current: Net Capital Ratio of SCM at the current month-end, as a decimal fraction (7% = 0.07)\n; scm_ncr_prior: Net Capital Ratio of SCM at the immediately preceding month-end, as a decimal fraction\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((commitments_or_obligations_outstanding Bool) (required_lenders_waived_in_writing Bool) (is_month_end Bool) (broker_ncr_current Real) (broker_ncr_prior Real) (scm_ncr_current Real) (scm_ncr_prior Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and commitments_or_obligations_outstanding (not required_lenders_waived_in_writing) is_month_end)\n      (and (>= (/ (+ broker_ncr_current broker_ncr_prior) 2.0) 0.07)\n           (>= broker_ncr_current 0.05)\n           (>= (/ (+ scm_ncr_current scm_ncr_prior) 2.0) 0.07)\n           (>= scm_ncr_current 0.05))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "commitments_or_obligations_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True if any Lender has any Commitment, or any Loan or other obligation remains outstanding, unpaid or unsatisfied, before full payment of all amounts due to the Lenders",
      "source_quote": "so long as any Lender shall have any Commitment hereunder, or any Loan or other obligation, shall remain outstanding, unpaid or unsatisfied and until full payment of all amounts due to the Lenders hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "required_lenders_waived_in_writing",
      "meaning": "True if the Required Lenders have waived compliance with Section 7.1 in writing at this observation",
      "source_quote": "unless and to the extent the Required Lenders waive compliance in writing"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_month_end",
      "meaning": "True if the observation date is a month-end date at which a Net Capital Ratio is measured",
      "source_quote": "any month-end Net Capital Ratio"
    },
    {
      "name": "broker_ncr_current",
      "meaning": "Net Capital Ratio of the Broker Subsidiary at the current month-end, as a decimal fraction (7% = 0.07)",
      "source_quote": "The Borrower will not permit the Broker Subsidiary to allow (a) the average of two consecutive month-end Net Capital Ratios to be less than 7%"
    },
    {
      "name": "broker_ncr_prior",
      "meaning": "Net Capital Ratio of the Broker Subsidiary at the immediately preceding month-end, as a decimal fraction",
      "source_quote": "the average of two consecutive month-end Net Capital Ratios"
    },
    {
      "name": "scm_ncr_current",
      "meaning": "Net Capital Ratio of SCM at the current month-end, as a decimal fraction (7% = 0.07)",
      "source_quote": "The Borrower similarly will not permit SCM to allow (i) the average of two consecutive month-end Net Capital Ratios to be less than 7%"
    },
    {
      "name": "scm_ncr_prior",
      "meaning": "Net Capital Ratio of SCM at the immediately preceding month-end, as a decimal fraction",
      "source_quote": "the average of two consecutive month-end Net Capital Ratios"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Pointwise at a month-end observation: for each entity, the average of the current and immediately preceding month-end ratios must be at least 0.07 (not less than 7%), and the current month-end ratio must be at least 0.05. The preceding month-end's own 5% test is covered at its own observation. Ratios are assumed to be expressed as decimal fractions. The covenant applies only while commitments or obligations are outstanding and no written Required Lenders waiver applies. Net Capital Ratio is kept as an atomic input because the source does not define it."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter.\n; credit_obligations_not_paid_in_full: true iff the Credit Obligations have not yet all been paid in full at the observation time.\n; lenders_commitments_not_terminated: true iff the Lenders' commitments to extend credit under this Agreement and any other Credit Document have not yet all been irrevocably terminated at the observation time.\n; total_funded_debt: Total Funded Debt of the Parent as of the observation date (the last day of the fiscal quarter).\n; adjusted_ebitda_four_quarters: Adjusted EBITDA of the Parent for the four consecutive fiscal quarters ended as of the observation date.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (credit_obligations_not_paid_in_full Bool) (lenders_commitments_not_terminated Bool) (total_funded_debt Real) (adjusted_ebitda_four_quarters Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end (or credit_obligations_not_paid_in_full lenders_commitments_not_terminated))\n      (<= (/ total_funded_debt adjusted_ebitda_four_quarters) 3.0)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter.",
      "source_quote": "last day of each fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "credit_obligations_not_paid_in_full",
      "meaning": "True iff the Credit Obligations have not all been paid in full at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "until all of the Credit Obligations have been paid in full"
    },
    {
      "name": "lenders_commitments_not_terminated",
      "meaning": "True iff the Lenders' commitments to extend credit under this Agreement and any other Credit Document have not yet been irrevocably terminated at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "the Lenders' commitments to extend credit under this Agreement and any other Credit Document have been irrevocably terminated"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_funded_debt",
      "meaning": "Total Funded Debt as of the observation date (last day of the fiscal quarter); numerator of the leverage ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Total Funded Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "adjusted_ebitda_four_quarters",
      "meaning": "Adjusted EBITDA for the four consecutive fiscal quarters ended as of the observation date; denominator of the leverage ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Adjusted EBITDA for the four consecutive fiscal quarters ended as of such day"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Only Section 9.6 is a numeric financial covenant; 9.1.1 and 9.1.2 are qualitative compliance and business-conduct covenants and are not encoded. The covenant applies at quarter-end observations while either the Credit Obligations remain unpaid or the commitments remain unterminated (it ends only when both conditions are satisfied). The ratio is computed as a division, so QF_NRA is used. A zero Adjusted EBITDA is reported by the evaluator as unresolved, and no positivity assumption is made. The bound is non-strict (<= 3.00) per 'not more than 3.00 to 1.00'."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; letters_of_credit_outstanding: True if any Letters of Credit are outstanding at the observation time.\n; revolving_note_unpaid: True if the Revolving Note remains unpaid at the observation time.\n; commitment_in_effect: True if the Commitment has not expired or been terminated at the observation time.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: True if the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter.\n; funded_debt_ratio: Funded Debt Ratio as of the observation date, expressed as a number X meaning X to 1.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((letters_of_credit_outstanding Bool) (revolving_note_unpaid Bool) (commitment_in_effect Bool) (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (funded_debt_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and (or letters_of_credit_outstanding revolving_note_unpaid commitment_in_effect) is_fiscal_quarter_end)\n      (<= funded_debt_ratio 2.0)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "letters_of_credit_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True if any Letters of Credit are outstanding at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "any Letters of Credit are outstanding"
    },
    {
      "name": "revolving_note_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True if the Revolving Note remains unpaid at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "the Revolving Note shall remain unpaid"
    },
    {
      "name": "commitment_in_effect",
      "meaning": "True if the Commitment has not expired or been terminated at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "the Commitment has not expired or been terminated"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True if the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter.",
      "source_quote": "as of the last day of any Fiscal Quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "funded_debt_ratio",
      "meaning": "Funded Debt Ratio as of the observation date, expressed as a number X meaning X to 1 (atomic input; definition not supplied).",
      "source_quote": "Funded Debt Ratio"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The Borrower must not permit the Funded Debt Ratio to exceed 2.0 to 1, so compliance is ratio <= 2.0 (a ratio of exactly 2.0 complies). The covenant applies only at Fiscal Quarter end. The 'so long as' lead-in is encoded as the disjunction of three conditions (any LC outstanding, Revolving Note unpaid, or Commitment not expired or terminated), since the covenant lasts while any of them holds. The Funded Debt Ratio's definition is not supplied, so it remains an atomic Real."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_last_day_of_month: true iff the observation date is the last day of a calendar month (the date as of which the ratio is tested).\n; consolidated_debt: Debt of the Borrowers on a consolidated basis as of the observation date (currency units).\n; consolidated_effective_tangible_net_worth: Effective Tangible Net Worth of the Borrowers on a consolidated basis as of the observation date (currency units).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_last_day_of_month Bool) (consolidated_debt Real) (consolidated_effective_tangible_net_worth Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_last_day_of_month\n      (<= (/ consolidated_debt consolidated_effective_tangible_net_worth) 2.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_last_day_of_month",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a calendar month, i.e. the date as of which the ratio is tested.",
      "source_quote": "as of the last day of each month"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_debt",
      "meaning": "Debt of the Borrowers on a consolidated basis as of the observation date (currency units); the numerator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "a ratio of Debt to Effective Tangible Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_effective_tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Effective Tangible Net Worth of the Borrowers on a consolidated basis as of the observation date (currency units); the denominator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Effective Tangible Net Worth"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Covenant tested pointwise at month-end: the ratio Debt / Effective Tangible Net Worth must be at most 2.50 (non-strict, 'not more than 2.50:1.00'). The ratio is computed as an explicit division, so a zero Effective Tangible Net Worth is reported unresolved by the evaluator. No sign or positivity assumptions are made, so a negative denominator is evaluated arithmetically as written. The definitions of Debt and Effective Tangible Net Worth are not supplied in the source context, so each is an atomic Real input. QF_NRA is used because the division has a variable denominator."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; first_lien_net_leverage_ratio: First Lien Net Leverage Ratio of the Borrower as of the last day of the Test Period, expressed as a number (4.50:1.00 = 4.5).\n; is_test_period_end_sep2014_to_jun2015: True iff this observation is the last day of a Test Period ended September 30, 2014, December 31, 2014, March 31, 2015 or June 30, 2015.\n; is_test_period_end_sep2015_or_later: True iff this observation is the last day of a Test Period ended September 30, 2015 or any later date.\n; lender_has_commitment: True iff any Lender has any Commitment under the agreement at this observation.\n; accrued_payable_obligation_unpaid: True iff any Loan or other Obligation that is accrued and payable remains unpaid or unsatisfied at this observation.\n; letter_of_credit_outstanding: True iff any Letter of Credit remains outstanding at this observation.\n; required_revolving_lenders_written_consent: True iff the Required Revolving Credit Lenders have given written consent covering this financial covenant at this observation.\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n  (first_lien_net_leverage_ratio Real)\n  (is_test_period_end_sep2014_to_jun2015 Bool)\n  (is_test_period_end_sep2015_or_later Bool)\n  (lender_has_commitment Bool)\n  (accrued_payable_obligation_unpaid Bool)\n  (letter_of_credit_outstanding Bool)\n  (required_revolving_lenders_written_consent Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and (or lender_has_commitment accrued_payable_obligation_unpaid letter_of_credit_outstanding)\n           (not required_revolving_lenders_written_consent))\n      (and (=> is_test_period_end_sep2014_to_jun2015 (<= first_lien_net_leverage_ratio 4.5))\n           (=> is_test_period_end_sep2015_or_later (<= first_lien_net_leverage_ratio 4.25)))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "first_lien_net_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "First Lien Net Leverage Ratio of the Borrower as of the last day of the Test Period, as a number (4.50:1.00 = 4.5). Atomic input because no arithmetic definition is supplied.",
      "source_quote": "First Lien Net Leverage Ratio"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_test_period_end_sep2014_to_jun2015",
      "meaning": "True iff this observation is the last day of a Test Period ended September 30, 2014, December 31, 2014, March 31, 2015 or June 30, 2015.",
      "source_quote": "September 30, 2014 4.50:1.00 December 31, 2014 4.50:1.00 March 31, 2015 4.50:1.00 June 30, 2015 4.50:1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_test_period_end_sep2015_or_later",
      "meaning": "True iff this observation is the last day of a Test Period ended September 30, 2015 or any later date.",
      "source_quote": "September 30, 2015 and thereafter 4.25:1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "lender_has_commitment",
      "meaning": "True iff any Lender has any Commitment under the agreement at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "So long as any Lender shall have any Commitment hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "accrued_payable_obligation_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True iff any Loan or other Obligation that is accrued and payable remains unpaid or unsatisfied at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "any Loan or other Obligation hereunder which is accrued and payable shall remain unpaid or unsatisfied"
    },
    {
      "name": "letter_of_credit_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True iff any Letter of Credit remains outstanding at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "any Letter of Credit shall remain outstanding"
    },
    {
      "name": "required_revolving_lenders_written_consent",
      "meaning": "True iff the Required Revolving Credit Lenders have given written consent covering this financial covenant at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "Except with the written consent of the Required Revolving Credit Lenders"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is a prohibition on permitting the ratio to be greater than the cap, so compliance is ratio <= cap. The cap is 4.50 for the four Test Periods ended Sep 30, 2014 to Jun 30, 2015, and 4.25 for Sep 30, 2015 and thereafter. The covenant applies only while a Commitment, an unpaid accrued and payable Obligation, or an outstanding Letter of Credit exists; these three conditions are joined by OR. The covenant does not apply when written consent is given. The two test-period flags are calendar inputs supplied by the evaluator. If neither is true, the observation is not a covered Test Period end and is vacuously compliant. No division is performed."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the last day of a quarterly financial reporting period (the covenant tests apply only then).\n; consolidated_ebitda: Consolidated EBITDA for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on the last day of the quarterly financial reporting period.\n; consolidated_interest_expense: Consolidated Interest Expense for the same four-consecutive-fiscal-quarter period ending on the last day of the quarterly financial reporting period.\n; consolidated_total_debt: Consolidated Total Debt as of the last day of the quarterly financial reporting period.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_quarter_end Bool) (consolidated_ebitda Real) (consolidated_interest_expense Real) (consolidated_total_debt Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_quarter_end\n      (and\n        ; (c)(i) Interest coverage must not be less than 3.00 to 1.00\n        (>= (/ consolidated_ebitda consolidated_interest_expense) 3.0)\n        ; (c)(ii) Total debt to EBITDA must not exceed 3.00 to 1.00\n        (<= (/ consolidated_total_debt consolidated_ebitda) 3.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a quarterly financial reporting period, when both financial covenant tests apply.",
      "source_quote": "at the end of any quarterly financial reporting period"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_ebitda",
      "meaning": "Consolidated EBITDA for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on the last day of the quarterly financial reporting period.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated EBITDA for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on the last day of such quarterly financial reporting period"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Expense for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on the last day of the quarterly financial reporting period.",
      "source_quote": "the ratio of Consolidated EBITDA to Consolidated Interest Expense for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on the last day of such quarterly financial reporting period"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_total_debt",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Total Debt as of the last day of the quarterly financial reporting period.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Total Debt as of the last day of such quarterly financial reporting period"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Formalizes only the two financial covenants in Section 5.02(c). Sections 5.02(a) and (b) are event-based negative covenants on liens and fundamental changes, and they are not modeled here. 'Not less than 3.00 to 1.00' becomes (>= ratio 3.0), and 'not exceed 3.00 to 1.00' becomes (<= ratio 3.0). Both ratios divide by input variables, so the logic is QF_NRA. Division by zero is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved, with no positivity assumptions added. Both tests apply only when is_quarter_end is true."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; fixed_charge_coverage: Fixed Charge Coverage (ratio, in x) as of the observation date, calculated as illustrated on Exhibit 4.6(D); the exhibit is not supplied, so it is an atomic input.\n; is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter: true iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter.\n; quarter_ends_closing_date_through_12_31_99: true iff the fiscal quarter ends in the period from the Closing Date through 12/31/99.\n; quarter_ends_after_12_31_99: true iff the fiscal quarter ends in the 'Thereafter' period, i.e. after 12/31/99.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((fixed_charge_coverage Real) (is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter Bool) (quarter_ends_closing_date_through_12_31_99 Bool) (quarter_ends_after_12_31_99 Bool)) Bool\n  (and\n    (=> (and is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter quarter_ends_closing_date_through_12_31_99)\n        (>= fixed_charge_coverage 1.05))\n    (=> (and is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter quarter_ends_after_12_31_99)\n        (>= fixed_charge_coverage 1.10))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "fixed_charge_coverage",
      "meaning": "Fixed Charge Coverage (ratio, in x) on the observation date, calculated as illustrated on Exhibit 4.6(D). Exhibit not supplied, so it is an atomic input.",
      "source_quote": "\"Fixed Charge Coverage\" will be calculated as illustrated on Exhibit 4.6(D)."
    },
    {
      "name": "is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter.",
      "source_quote": "on the last day of any fiscal quarter ending during any of the periods set forth below"
    },
    {
      "name": "quarter_ends_closing_date_through_12_31_99",
      "meaning": "True iff the fiscal quarter ends in the period from the Closing Date through 12/31/99, where the minimum is 1.05x.",
      "source_quote": "Closing Date through 1.05x 12/31/99"
    },
    {
      "name": "quarter_ends_after_12_31_99",
      "meaning": "True iff the fiscal quarter ends in the 'Thereafter' period, i.e. after 12/31/99, where the minimum is 1.10x.",
      "source_quote": "Thereafter 1.10x"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is checked pointwise at fiscal quarter-end dates. 'Not less than' is encoded as >= (1.05 for the first period, 1.10 thereafter). Fixed Charge Coverage is atomic because Exhibit 4.6(D) is not supplied. The lead-in survival clause (Revolving Loan Commitment in effect, Requisite Lender consent) is not modeled as a separate input; the evaluator is assumed to supply observations only while the covenants are in force."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the last date of a fiscal quarter of Borrower (the date of determination).\n; consolidated_cogs_four_quarters: Consolidated Cost of Goods Sold of Borrower for the four fiscal quarters ending on the date of determination.\n; inventory_current_quarter: Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of the most recent fiscal quarter.\n; inventory_prior_quarter_1: Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of the first (most recent) of the three prior fiscal quarters.\n; inventory_prior_quarter_2: Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of the second of the three prior fiscal quarters.\n; inventory_prior_quarter_3: Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of the third (earliest) of the three prior fiscal quarters.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (consolidated_cogs_four_quarters Real) (inventory_current_quarter Real) (inventory_prior_quarter_1 Real) (inventory_prior_quarter_2 Real) (inventory_prior_quarter_3 Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n      (>= (/ consolidated_cogs_four_quarters\n             (/ (+ inventory_current_quarter inventory_prior_quarter_1 inventory_prior_quarter_2 inventory_prior_quarter_3) 4.0))\n          1.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last date of a fiscal quarter of Borrower (the date of determination).",
      "source_quote": "as of the last date of each fiscal quarter of Borrower"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_cogs_four_quarters",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Cost of Goods Sold for the four fiscal quarters ending on the date of determination.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Cost of Goods Sold"
    },
    {
      "name": "inventory_current_quarter",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of the most recent fiscal quarter.",
      "source_quote": "the amount of Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of the most recent fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "inventory_prior_quarter_1",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of the first (most recent) of the three prior fiscal quarters.",
      "source_quote": "the amount of Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of each of the three (3) prior fiscal quarters"
    },
    {
      "name": "inventory_prior_quarter_2",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of the second of the three prior fiscal quarters.",
      "source_quote": "the amount of Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of each of the three (3) prior fiscal quarters"
    },
    {
      "name": "inventory_prior_quarter_3",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of the third (earliest) of the three prior fiscal quarters.",
      "source_quote": "the amount of Consolidated Inventory as of the last date of each of the three (3) prior fiscal quarters"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "At each fiscal quarter-end, the ratio of four-quarter Consolidated COGS to Average Consolidated Inventory must not be less than 1.5 (so >= 1.5). Average Consolidated Inventory is the sum of the five-point... specifically the current quarter-end inventory plus the three prior quarter-end inventories, divided by four, as the source defines it. Division is kept explicit, so a zero average is reported as unresolved by the evaluator. QF_NRA is used because the divisor is a non-constant term. The stray '32' in the source text is treated as an artifact. The lender-consent exception is not modeled because it is not an observable input."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; debt_service_coverage_ratio: Debt Service Coverage Ratio of the Gaming Enterprise Borrower, as of the observation date (atomic Real; no arithmetic definition supplied).\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: True iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter.\n; is_quarter_on_or_after_dec_31_2003: True iff the fiscal quarter ending on the observation date is the quarter ending December 31, 2003 or a later quarter.\n; loan_not_paid_in_full: True iff the principal of and interest on the Loan have not yet been paid in full at the observation date.\n; lender_written_consent: True iff Lender has consented in writing to the Borrower not complying with this covenant at the observation date.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((debt_service_coverage_ratio Real) (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (is_quarter_on_or_after_dec_31_2003 Bool) (loan_not_paid_in_full Bool) (lender_written_consent Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end\n           is_quarter_on_or_after_dec_31_2003\n           loan_not_paid_in_full\n           (not lender_written_consent))\n      (not (< debt_service_coverage_ratio 1.35))))",
