  "notes": "Section 7.09 requires the Interest Coverage Ratio at each fiscal quarter-end to be at least a minimum that depends on the fiscal year. In the supplied text the year column of the schedule is missing. Only the ratio column survives: '2.50 to 1.00 2.50 to 1.00 2.75 to 1.00 2.75 to 1.00'. There are four thresholds, but the covenant does not say which fiscal years they belong to. It does not say whether the first 2.50 applies to the first or the second year, or where the step to 2.75 happens. A single fixed threshold would therefore be unfaithful. Passing the 'applicable minimum' in as an input would hide the schedule, which is the core numerical content of the covenant. The definition of 'Interest Coverage Ratio' is also not supplied, though it could stay an atomic Real. Needed: the fiscal-year-to-ratio mapping, i.e. the years paired with each of the four 2.50/2.50/2.75/2.75 values. The comparison itself would be (>= interest_coverage_ratio threshold), applied only when the observation is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter ending after the Agreement date and the Loan or other Obligations remain unpaid (excluding unasserted contingent indemnification obligations with no known claim)."
}

