{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; consolidated_indebtedness: Consolidated Indebtedness of the Company at the observation time (numerator of the ratio), in the same currency units as consolidated_tangible_net_worth.\n; consolidated_tangible_net_worth: Consolidated Tangible Net Worth of the Company at the observation time (denominator of the ratio), in the same currency units as consolidated_indebtedness.\n; is_last_day_of_fiscal_year: true iff the observation time is the last day of a fiscal year of the Company; false at any other time.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((consolidated_indebtedness Real) (consolidated_tangible_net_worth Real) (is_last_day_of_fiscal_year Bool)) Bool\n  ; ratio must not exceed 600% (6.00) on the last day of a fiscal year, and 650% (6.50) at any other time\n  (ite is_last_day_of_fiscal_year\n       (<= (/ consolidated_indebtedness consolidated_tangible_net_worth) 6.0)\n       (<= (/ consolidated_indebtedness consolidated_tangible_net_worth) 6.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "consolidated_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Indebtedness of the Company at the observation time (numerator of the ratio), in the same currency units as consolidated_tangible_net_worth.",
      "source_quote": "ratio of Consolidated Indebtedness to Consolidated Tangible Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Tangible Net Worth of the Company at the observation time (denominator of the ratio), in the same currency units as consolidated_indebtedness.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Indebtedness to Consolidated Tangible Net Worth"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_last_day_of_fiscal_year",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation time is the last day of a fiscal year of the Company; false at any other time.",
      "source_quote": "on and as of the last day of any fiscal year"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio is Consolidated Indebtedness divided by Consolidated Tangible Net Worth. The cap is 600% (6.0) on the last day of any fiscal year and 650% (6.5) at any other time, and 'exceed' makes both bounds non-strict (<=). Division is kept as a real division so a zero or negative denominator is not silently treated as compliant; a zero denominator is reported as unresolved by the evaluator. The logic is QF_NRA because dividing one variable by another is nonlinear. The 'at any other time' clause is the else branch of the fiscal-year-end flag. The Required Banks' written-consent exception is not modeled as an input, since consent is not an observable financial state in the source."
}

