{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; debt_ratio: the Debt Ratio at the observation time, as an atomic Real (for example 2.50 means 2.50 to 1).\n; collateral_released_after_upgrade: true iff a Rating Upgrade Event has occurred and Collateral has been released pursuant to Section 6.10(a) at or before the observation time.\n; sp_below_bbb_minus: true iff the Index Debt is rated less than \"BBB-\" by Standard & Poor's at the observation time.\n; moody_below_baa3: true iff the Index Debt is rated less than \"Baa3\" by Moody's at the observation time.\n; moody_below_ba2: true iff the Index Debt is rated less than \"Ba2\" by Moody's at the observation time.\n; sp_below_bb_plus: true iff the Index Debt is rated less than \"BB+\" by Standard & Poor's at the observation time.\n; either_agency_no_rating: true iff either Moody's or Standard & Poor's does not have in effect a rating for the Index Debt at the observation time.\n; new_pledge_agreements_delivered: true iff the Borrower, its Subsidiaries (subject to the Excluded Entity limitations) and the Administrative Agent have executed and delivered a new U.S. Equity Pledge Agreement and, as applicable, new Foreign Equity Pledge Agreements, with the concurrent perfection actions and documents required by Section 6.10(b)(ii).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((debt_ratio Real) (collateral_released_after_upgrade Bool) (sp_below_bbb_minus Bool) (moody_below_baa3 Bool) (moody_below_ba2 Bool) (sp_below_bb_plus Bool) (either_agency_no_rating Bool) (new_pledge_agreements_delivered Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and collateral_released_after_upgrade\n           (or (and (>= debt_ratio 2.5)\n                    (or sp_below_bbb_minus moody_below_baa3))\n               (and (< debt_ratio 2.5)\n                    (or (or sp_below_bbb_minus moody_below_ba2)\n                        (or sp_below_bb_plus moody_below_baa3)))\n               either_agency_no_rating))\n      new_pledge_agreements_delivered))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "debt_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Debt Ratio at the observation time, as an atomic Real (2.50 means 2.50 to 1).",
      "source_quote": "the Debt Ratio shall be greater than or equal to 2.50 to 1"
    },
    {
      "name": "collateral_released_after_upgrade",
      "meaning": "True iff a Rating Upgrade Event has occurred and Collateral has been released pursuant to Section 6.10(a) at or before the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "Collateral shall have been released pursuant to paragraph (a) above"
    },
    {
      "name": "sp_below_bbb_minus",
      "meaning": "True iff the Index Debt is rated less than \"BBB-\" by Standard & Poor's at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "the Index Debt shall be rated less than \"BBB-\" by Standard & Poor's"
    },
    {
      "name": "moody_below_baa3",
      "meaning": "True iff the Index Debt is rated less than \"Baa3\" by Moody's at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "less than \"Baa3\" by Moody's"
    },
    {
      "name": "moody_below_ba2",
      "meaning": "True iff the Index Debt is rated less than \"Ba2\" by Moody's at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "less than \"Ba2\" by Moody's"
    },
    {
      "name": "sp_below_bb_plus",
      "meaning": "True iff the Index Debt is rated less than \"BB+\" by Standard & Poor's at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "less than \"BB+\" by Standard & Poor's"
    },
    {
      "name": "either_agency_no_rating",
      "meaning": "True iff either Moody's or Standard & Poor's does not have in effect a rating for the Index Debt at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "either Moody's or Standard & Poor's shall not have in effect a rating for the Index Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "new_pledge_agreements_delivered",
      "meaning": "True iff the Borrower, its Subsidiaries (subject to the Excluded Entity limitations) and the Administrative Agent have executed and delivered a new U.S. Equity Pledge Agreement and, as applicable, new Foreign Equity Pledge Agreements, with the concurrent perfection actions and documents required by Section 6.10(b)(ii).",
      "source_quote": "shall promptly execute and deliver a new U.S. Equity Pledge Agreement and, as applicable, new Foreign Equity Pledge Agreements"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The formalized obligation is the Section 6.10(b) re-pledge requirement. It applies once Collateral has been released after a Rating Upgrade Event and any one of the triggers holds: (i) Debt Ratio >= 2.50 with S&P below BBB- or Moody's below Baa3; (ii) Debt Ratio < 2.50 with either (x) S&P below BBB- or Moody's below Ba2, or (y) S&P below BB+ or Moody's below Baa3; or (iii) either agency has no rating. The boundary at exactly 2.50 follows the source: >= in (i), < in (ii). Section 6.10(a) and (c) set the conditions for release and for a Rating Upgrade Event. They are not separate obligations, and their effect enters through the collateral_released_after_upgrade input. 'Promptly' is handled pointwise: the evaluator supplies whether the new Pledge Agreements have been delivered at each observation. The 'as evidenced by a confirmation or notice' language is treated as how the rating facts are established, not as a separate input. No division is used."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; leverage_ratio: The Borrower's Leverage Ratio at the observation date, as a decimal fraction (175% = 1.75, 50% = 0.5). The source does not define the ratio's arithmetic, so it is an atomic input.\n; is_on_or_after_effective_date: True iff the observation date is from and after the Effective Date.\n; any_bank_has_commitment: True iff any Bank has any Commitment under the agreement at the observation date.\n; any_note_amount_unpaid: True iff any amount payable under any Note remains unpaid at the observation date.\n; is_on_or_after_july_31_1995: True iff the observation date is on or after July 31, 1995. False means the date is prior to July 31, 1995.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((leverage_ratio Real) (is_on_or_after_effective_date Bool) (any_bank_has_commitment Bool) (any_note_amount_unpaid Bool) (is_on_or_after_july_31_1995 Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and is_on_or_after_effective_date (or any_bank_has_commitment any_note_amount_unpaid))\n      (ite is_on_or_after_july_31_1995\n           (<= leverage_ratio 0.5)\n           (<= leverage_ratio 1.75))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Borrower's Leverage Ratio at the observation date, as a decimal fraction (175% = 1.75, 50% = 0.5). Atomic input because the source gives no arithmetic definition.",
      "source_quote": "The Leverage Ratio will not exceed"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_on_or_after_effective_date",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is from and after the Effective Date.",
      "source_quote": "from and after the Effective Date"
    },
    {
      "name": "any_bank_has_commitment",
      "meaning": "True iff any Bank has any Commitment under the agreement at the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "any Bank has any Commitment hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "any_note_amount_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True iff any amount payable under any Note remains unpaid at the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "any amount payable under any Note remains unpaid"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_on_or_after_july_31_1995",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is on or after July 31, 1995. False means the date is prior to July 31, 1995.",
      "source_quote": "at any date on or after July 31, 1995"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies from the Effective Date for so long as any Commitment exists or any Note amount is unpaid. The maximum is 175% before July 31, 1995 and 50% on or after that date. Both limits are non-strict (<=), matching 'will not exceed'. Percentages are encoded as decimal fractions, and leverage_ratio must be supplied in the same units."
