  ],
  "notes": "Applicability is at each fiscal-quarter-end observation (Computation Period end) while any Commitment or Credit Exposure exists. Interest Expense = gross interest expense minus insurance-policy interest expense minus interest income, and is used both as the ratio denominator and as the EBITDA add-back. EBITDA follows clauses (a), (b)(i)-(v) and (c)(i)-(iii). The threshold 'not less than 3.25:1.00' is encoded as ratio >= 3.25. The ratio is a division by a non-constant, so QF_NRA is used. A zero denominator is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. No sign assumptions are made. The 'to the extent included in Consolidated Net Income' and 'without duplication' qualifiers are carried in the input meanings, because the formula cannot enforce them."
