{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; commitments_in_effect: true iff any of the Commitments are in effect at the observation time.\n; payment_obligations_unpaid: true iff, at the observation time, payment in full has not yet occurred of the Loans, all interest thereon, and all other amounts payable by the Borrower under the agreement.\n; total_debt: total Debt of the Borrower and its Consolidated Subsidiaries at the observation time.\n; tangible_net_worth: Tangible Net Worth at the observation time.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((commitments_in_effect Bool) (payment_obligations_unpaid Bool) (total_debt Real) (tangible_net_worth Real)) Bool\n  (=> (or commitments_in_effect payment_obligations_unpaid)\n      (<= (/ total_debt (+ tangible_net_worth total_debt)) 0.45)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "commitments_in_effect",
      "meaning": "True iff any of the Commitments are in effect at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "so long as any of the Commitments are in effect"
    },
    {
      "name": "payment_obligations_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True iff, at the observation time, payment in full has not yet occurred of the Loans, all interest thereon, and all other amounts payable by the Borrower under the agreement.",
      "source_quote": "until payment in full of Loans hereunder, all interest thereon and all other amounts payable by the Borrower hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_debt",
      "meaning": "Total Debt of the Borrower and its Consolidated Subsidiaries at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "total Debt of the Borrower and its Consolidated Subsidiaries"
    },
    {
      "name": "tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Tangible Net Worth at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "Tangible Net Worth"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies while the Commitments are in effect or until payment in full of the Loans, interest and other amounts, so applicability is the disjunction of the two Boolean inputs. The ratio is total_debt / (tangible_net_worth + total_debt) and must not be greater than 0.45 (stated as 0.45 to 1.00), so the test is <= 0.45. 'At any time' is translated pointwise at each observation. Division is kept literal, so QF_NRA is used. A zero denominator is reported as unresolved by the evaluator, and no sign or positivity assumptions are made."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; revolving_credit_commitment_in_effect: True if the Revolving Credit Commitment is in effect under the Agreement at the observation time.\n; amounts_payable_remain_unpaid: True if any amount payable under the Agreement or any other Loan Document remains unpaid at the observation time.\n; senior_debt_to_ebitda_ratio: The Loan Parties' combined Consolidated Senior Indebtedness/Consolidated EBITDA Ratio at the observation time, expressed as a multiple (x to 1.0).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((revolving_credit_commitment_in_effect Bool) (amounts_payable_remain_unpaid Bool) (senior_debt_to_ebitda_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> (or revolving_credit_commitment_in_effect amounts_payable_remain_unpaid)\n      (<= senior_debt_to_ebitda_ratio 2.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "revolving_credit_commitment_in_effect",
      "meaning": "True if the Revolving Credit Commitment is in effect under the Agreement at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "so long as the Revolving Credit Commitment is in effect hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "amounts_payable_remain_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True if any amount payable under the Agreement or any other Loan Document remains unpaid at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "any amount payable under this Agreement or any other Loan Document remains unpaid"
    },
    {
      "name": "senior_debt_to_ebitda_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Loan Parties' combined Consolidated Senior Indebtedness/Consolidated EBITDA Ratio at the observation time, expressed as a multiple (x to 1.0).",
      "source_quote": "combined Consolidated Senior Indebtedness/Consolidated EBITDA Ratio to exceed 2.5 to 1:0"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies while the commitment is in effect OR any amount is unpaid, so the two applicability flags are joined with OR. The 'at no time' clause is applied pointwise at each observation. The limit is 'shall not exceed 2.5 to 1.0', so a ratio of exactly 2.5 complies (<=). The definitions of Consolidated Senior Indebtedness and Consolidated EBITDA are not supplied, so the ratio is kept as an atomic Real input. No division is performed in the formula."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; total_funded_debt: XL Capital's Total Funded Debt at the observation time, as defined in the agreement (currency units).\n; consolidated_net_worth: XL Capital's Consolidated Net Worth at the observation time, as defined in the agreement (same currency units).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((total_funded_debt Real) (consolidated_net_worth Real)) Bool\n  (<= (/ total_funded_debt (+ total_funded_debt consolidated_net_worth)) 0.35))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "total_funded_debt",
      "meaning": "XL Capital's Total Funded Debt at the observation time, as defined in the agreement (currency units). It is the numerator of the ratio and the first term of the denominator.",
      "source_quote": "Total Funded Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_net_worth",
      "meaning": "XL Capital's Consolidated Net Worth at the observation time, as defined in the agreement (same currency units as total_funded_debt). It is added to Total Funded Debt in the denominator.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Net Worth"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is a negative covenant that applies at any time, so it is translated pointwise with no calendar flag. The ratio is Total Funded Debt / (Total Funded Debt + Consolidated Net Worth). Compliance requires it to be not greater than 0.35, which is written as <= 0.35 (0.35:1.00 is read as 0.35). The ratio is kept as a division so a zero denominator is reported as unresolved by the evaluator, and no sign assumptions are made. QF_NRA is used because the denominator is non-constant. The definitions of Total Funded Debt and Consolidated Net Worth are not supplied, so they are atomic inputs."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Company (applicability flag for 6.1(a) and 6.1(b)).\n; total_leverage_ratio: the Total Leverage Ratio of the Company as of the observation date, as a multiple (x to 1.0).\n; interest_coverage_ratio_4q: the Interest Coverage Ratio for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on the observation date, as a multiple (x to 1).\n; priority_debt: the amount of Priority Debt at the observation time.\n; consolidated_capitalization: the amount of Consolidated Capitalization at the observation time, in the same currency units as priority_debt.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (total_leverage_ratio Real) (interest_coverage_ratio_4q Real) (priority_debt Real) (consolidated_capitalization Real)) Bool\n  (and\n    ; 6.1(a): at fiscal quarter end, leverage must not be greater than 3.50\n    (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (<= total_leverage_ratio 3.5))\n    ; 6.1(b): at fiscal quarter end, four-quarter interest coverage must not be less than 2.50\n    (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (>= interest_coverage_ratio_4q 2.5))\n    ; 6.1(c): at any time, Priority Debt must not exceed 25% of Consolidated Capitalization\n    (<= priority_debt (* 0.25 consolidated_capitalization))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Company; it gates the Total Leverage Ratio and Interest Coverage Ratio tests.",
      "source_quote": "As of the last day of any fiscal quarter of the Company"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Total Leverage Ratio as of the observation date, as a multiple (x to 1.0). Its definition is not supplied, so it is an atomic input.",
      "source_quote": "permit the Total Leverage Ratio to be greater than 3.50 to 1.0"
    },
    {
      "name": "interest_coverage_ratio_4q",
      "meaning": "Interest Coverage Ratio for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on the observation date, as a multiple (x to 1). Its definition is not supplied, so it is an atomic input.",
      "source_quote": "permit the Interest Coverage Ratio for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on such date to be less than 2.50 to 1"
    },
    {
      "name": "priority_debt",
      "meaning": "Amount of Priority Debt at the observation time, in currency units.",
      "source_quote": "Priority Debt to exceed 25% of Consolidated Capitalization"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_capitalization",
      "meaning": "Amount of Consolidated Capitalization at the observation time, in the same currency units as priority_debt.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Capitalization"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is a negative covenant, so each test is compliant when the prohibited condition is absent. (a) The prohibited condition is leverage greater than 3.50, so the compliant condition is <= 3.5 (non-strict). (b) The prohibited condition is coverage less than 2.50, so the compliant condition is >= 2.5. (c) The prohibited condition is Priority Debt exceeding 25% of Consolidated Capitalization, so the compliant condition is priority_debt <= 0.25 * consolidated_capitalization. (c) applies at any time, so it is not gated by the quarter-end flag. The 25% test is written as multiplication by a constant, so no division occurs and no domain assumptions are added. The definitions of the ratios and of Priority Debt are not in the supplied text, so they are kept as atomic inputs."
}

