{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is a fiscal quarter end of the Borrower, the date at which the Total Leverage Ratio is measured under Section 4.1.\n; total_leverage_ratio: the Borrower's Total Leverage Ratio at the observation date, expressed as a multiple (X in X:1.0), calculated on a consolidated basis for the Borrower and its Subsidiaries. The definition is not supplied, so it is an atomic Real.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (total_leverage_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (<= total_leverage_ratio 4.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is a fiscal quarter end of the Borrower, the date at which the Total Leverage Ratio is measured under Section 4.1.",
      "source_quote": "measured at each fiscal quarter end"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Borrower's Total Leverage Ratio at the observation date, expressed as a multiple (X in X:1.0), calculated on a consolidated basis for the Borrower and its Subsidiaries. Its definition is not supplied, so it is an atomic Real.",
      "source_quote": "Total Leverage Ratio less than or equal to 4.5:1.0"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Pointwise translation: at each observation that is a fiscal quarter end, the Total Leverage Ratio must be <= 4.5 (non-strict, per 'less than or equal to'). The 'at all times' language is read as applying at the measurement dates, as the clause itself says 'measured at each fiscal quarter end'. The proviso is not encoded. It deems the Agreement to include any additional or more restrictive financial covenants the Borrower gives other holders of Indebtedness after the Closing Date. Those covenants' content is unknown and external to the supplied text, so no numeric constraint can be formalized from them. The Requisite Lenders' written-consent waiver and the termination condition on payment in full of Obligations are likewise not modeled. The 'Total Leverage Ratio' definition is not provided, so it is kept as an atomic Real input."
