  "notes": "The covenant is clear: (a) the Total Leverage Ratio must not exceed the scheduled maximum, and (b) the Interest Coverage Ratio must not fall below the scheduled minimum, each at the end of a Test Period beginning with the period ending June 30, 2007. The step-down schedules cannot be tied to test-period dates faithfully, though. The fiscal-year row labels were stripped from both tables, so the threshold values are only a flat list with no year attached. The Interest Coverage table is also broken by an elision marker ('* * *') and a repeated header, so it is unclear whether the repeated '2.25:1 2.25:1' values are duplicates or continuations. The fiscal-year definition is not supplied either. Mapping the thresholds to dates would mean guessing both the alignment and the fiscal calendar, and a wrong guess would produce an unfaithful formula. A reliable version needs the schedule with its fiscal-year and quarter labels intact, including the portion hidden by the elision."
