  "notes": "The Borrower must not permit the ratio to be greater than 3.50 to 1.0, so compliance is ratio <= 3.5, with the comparison non-strict at the threshold. The ratio is computed as Consolidated Indebtedness divided by EBITDA. Division by non-constant EBITDA is nonlinear, so the logic is QF_NRA. A zero EBITDA is reported by the evaluator as unresolved, and no positivity assumption is added. Cross-multiplying was deliberately avoided because it would give wrong results for negative EBITDA. The covenant applies only at Fiscal Quarter ends, so the body is conditioned on is_fiscal_quarter_end. The lead-in condition (Commitments expired or terminated, and Loans and fees paid in full) defines how long the covenant lasts. It is not modeled as an input, since the evaluator supplies observations only while the covenant is in force. Consolidated Indebtedness and EBITDA are not defined in the supplied text, so they remain atomic Real inputs."
}

{
