  "notes": "The three financial covenants in 7.1(a)-(c) are conjoined. Leverage covenants use 'exceed' so the test is <=, and the interest coverage covenant uses 'less than' so the test is >=. The six period flags are meant to be mutually exclusive and are supplied by the evaluator. Where the senior secured and interest coverage schedules merge or split the periods, the FQ4 2005-FQ2 2006 and FQ3 2006 flags are combined (3.00x and 2.00x) and the FQ4 2006-FQ3 2007 and FQ4 2007+ flags are combined (1.75x). When no flag is true, the observation is outside the scheduled periods, so no limit applies. The temporal lead-in (so long as Commitments remain in effect, etc.) is treated as observation-scope context and not encoded as a separate input."
