    }
  ],
  "notes": "Both financial covenants (a) and (b) apply at each fiscal quarter end, so they are conjoined under the quarter-end flag. (a) prohibits Total Funded Debt / EBITDA from being more than 3.25 to 1.00, so the compliant condition is <= 3.25. (b) prohibits the Interest Coverage Ratio from being less than 2.50 to 1.00, so the compliant condition is >= 2.5. The leverage ratio is computed as an explicit division, because the source defines it as the ratio of Total Funded Debt to EBITDA. Zero EBITDA is left to the evaluator's unresolved-division policy, and no sign or positivity assumptions are added. The Interest Coverage Ratio is an atomic input because no definition is supplied. QF_NRA is used because the division has a variable denominator. The 'so long as any Commitments are outstanding' preamble is treated as the overall duration of the covenant, so each observation supplied is assumed to fall within that period."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; credit_available: true iff credit is available under the Agreement at this observation.\n; bank_repaid_in_full: true iff the Bank has been repaid in full at this observation.\n; is_quarterly_test_date: true iff this observation is a quarterly testing point for the covenant.\n; current_liabilities: consolidated current liabilities of the Borrower.\n; long_term_liabilities: consolidated long term liabilities of the Borrower.\n; tangible_net_worth: consolidated tangible net worth of the Borrower.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((credit_available Bool) (bank_repaid_in_full Bool) (is_quarterly_test_date Bool) (current_liabilities Real) (long_term_liabilities Real) (tangible_net_worth Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and credit_available (not bank_repaid_in_full) is_quarterly_test_date)\n      (<= (/ (+ current_liabilities long_term_liabilities) tangible_net_worth) 0.75)))",
