{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Company (end of that fiscal quarter), when Sections 6.3 and 6.4 are tested.\n; consolidated_total_indebtedness: Consolidated Total Indebtedness as at the observation date (numerator of the Section 6.3 ratio).\n; annualized_consolidated_cash_flow: Annualized Consolidated Cash Flow as at the end of the fiscal quarter (denominator of the 6.3 ratio, numerator of the 6.4 ratio).\n; annualized_consolidated_interest_expense: Annualized Consolidated Interest Expense as at the end of the same fiscal quarter (denominator of the 6.4 ratio).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (consolidated_total_indebtedness Real) (annualized_consolidated_cash_flow Real) (annualized_consolidated_interest_expense Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n      (and\n        ; 6.3: the debt-to-cash-flow ratio must not exceed 2.50 to 1.00\n        (<= (/ consolidated_total_indebtedness annualized_consolidated_cash_flow) 2.5)\n        ; 6.4: the cash-flow-to-interest-expense ratio must not be less than 2.0 to 1\n        (>= (/ annualized_consolidated_cash_flow annualized_consolidated_interest_expense) 2.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day or end of a fiscal quarter of the Company, the date on which the Section 6.3 and 6.4 ratios are tested.",
      "source_quote": "as at the last day of any fiscal quarter of the Company"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_total_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Total Indebtedness as at the last day of the fiscal quarter. It is the numerator of the Section 6.3 ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Total Indebtedness"
    },
    {
      "name": "annualized_consolidated_cash_flow",
      "meaning": "Annualized Consolidated Cash Flow as at the end of the fiscal quarter. It is the denominator of the Section 6.3 ratio and the numerator of the Section 6.4 ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Annualized Consolidated Cash Flow"
    },
    {
      "name": "annualized_consolidated_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Annualized Consolidated Interest Expense as at the end of the same fiscal quarter. It is the denominator of the Section 6.4 ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Annualized Consolidated Interest Expense"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Formalized the two financial maintenance covenants, Sections 6.3 and 6.4, as one conjunction gated by the fiscal-quarter-end flag. Section 6.3 requires debt / cash flow <= 2.50 (the ratio must not exceed 2.50 to 1.00). Section 6.4 requires cash flow / interest expense >= 2.0 (the ratio must not be less than 2.0 to 1). Both thresholds are non-strict, matching 'exceed' and 'less than'. Division is kept as written in the ratio definitions, so a zero denominator is reported as unresolved by the evaluator. No positivity assumptions are made. Sections 6.1 and 6.2(b) are non-financial negative covenants. The 6.1 lien exceptions are truncated in the source and the 6.2(b) text is only a fragment, so both are omitted. QF_NRA is used because the ratios divide one variable by another."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; ebitda: EBITDA of the Borrower for the period of four (4) consecutive Fiscal Quarters ending at this observation.\n; consolidated_interest_expense: Consolidated Interest Expense for that same four-Fiscal-Quarter period.\n; commitments_expired_or_terminated: true iff the Commitments have expired or terminated at this observation.\n; loans_and_fees_paid_in_full: true iff the principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees payable under the agreement have been paid in full at this observation.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((ebitda Real) (consolidated_interest_expense Real) (commitments_expired_or_terminated Bool) (loans_and_fees_paid_in_full Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (not (and commitments_expired_or_terminated loans_and_fees_paid_in_full))\n      (>= (/ ebitda consolidated_interest_expense) 3.5)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "ebitda",
      "meaning": "EBITDA of the Borrower for the period of four consecutive Fiscal Quarters ending at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "the ratio of EBITDA for any period of four (4) consecutive Fiscal Quarters to Consolidated Interest Expense for such period"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Expense for the same four-consecutive-Fiscal-Quarter period as ebitda. It is the denominator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "the ratio of EBITDA for any period of four (4) consecutive Fiscal Quarters to Consolidated Interest Expense for such period"
    },
    {
      "name": "commitments_expired_or_terminated",
      "meaning": "True iff the Commitments have expired or terminated at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "Until the Commitments have expired or terminated"
    },
    {
      "name": "loans_and_fees_paid_in_full",
      "meaning": "True iff the principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees payable under the agreement have been paid in full at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "the principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees payable hereunder have been paid in full"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies until both the Commitments have expired or terminated and all Loan principal, interest and fees are paid in full. It is therefore active unless both Boolean flags are true. When active, the ratio EBITDA / Consolidated Interest Expense must be at least 3.5, because the covenant prohibits a ratio below 3.50 to 1.0. The ratio is computed by division, so a zero interest expense is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the divisor is a variable. The trailing four-quarter period is supplied through the inputs, and the pointwise convention applies the check at each observation."
}

