    }
  ],
  "notes": "Section 5.01 is an information covenant with many deliverables. This formalization covers only the clauses with concrete numeric deadlines and clear conditions: (a) annual statements within 113 days, (b) quarterly statements within 53 days for the first three quarters, and (f) the default certificate within five days if the Default is continuing. All three apply only while a Lender has Credit Exposure. Each deadline is checked pointwise: once the elapsed days exceed the limit, the matching timely-delivery flag must be true. Not encoded: the 'promptly' clauses (d, g, h), because they have no numeric limit; the ERISA notices in (i), the on-request information in (j), and the electronic-delivery deemed-date mechanics. Clause (c), the compliance certificate, is also omitted. Section 5.05 and the definitions of Default and Responsible Officer are not supplied, so 'Default' and 'Responsible Officer' knowledge are taken as externally supplied inputs."
