{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; consolidated_total_debt: Consolidated Total Debt at the observation time, the numerator (a) of the Section 5.14 ratio.\n; consolidated_total_capitalization: Consolidated Total Capitalization at the observation time, the denominator (b) of the Section 5.14 ratio.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((consolidated_total_debt Real) (consolidated_total_capitalization Real)) Bool\n  (not (> (/ consolidated_total_debt consolidated_total_capitalization) 0.40)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "consolidated_total_debt",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Total Debt at the observation time, the numerator (a) of the Section 5.14 ratio. The source supplies no further definition, so it is an atomic Real input.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Total Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Total Capitalization at the observation time, the denominator (b) of the Section 5.14 ratio. The source supplies no further definition, so it is an atomic Real input.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Total Capitalization"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant forbids the ratio of Consolidated Total Debt to Consolidated Total Capitalization from being greater than 0.40 to 1. Compliance is therefore ratio <= 0.40, with the threshold inclusive. It is encoded as (not (> ratio 0.40)), which is equivalent to (<= ratio 0.40). The covenant applies at all times while the Agreement is in effect, so under pointwise semantics it needs no calendar flag. The evaluator supplies observations only for times the Agreement is in effect. Division by a zero capitalization is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved, and no positivity assumption is made. Division by a variable makes the formula nonlinear, so the logic is QF_NRA."
}

