{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; net_worth: Borrower's Net Worth as at that fiscal quarter end, in dollars.\n; net_income: net income of the Borrower and its consolidated Subsidiaries for the four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on or most recently ended prior to the observation day.\n; income_taxes: income taxes of the Borrower and its consolidated Subsidiaries for that same four-quarter period.\n; noncash_provisions_writeoffs: non-cash provisions for, or actual write-offs of, assets (without duplication in respect of any prior period) for the Borrower and its consolidated Subsidiaries for that same four-quarter period.\n; interest_on_indebtedness: all interest in respect of Indebtedness (including the interest component of Capital Lease Obligation payments) accrued or capitalized during that same four-quarter period, whether or not paid.\n; net_hedging_interest_payable: net amount payable under interest-related Hedging Agreements during that same four-quarter period, signed negative if there is a net amount receivable.\n; lease_interest_factor_estimate: estimate of the portion of minimum rents under operating leases representing the interest factor, for that same four-quarter period.\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n    (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool)\n    (net_worth Real)\n    (net_income Real)\n    (income_taxes Real)\n    (noncash_provisions_writeoffs Real)\n    (interest_on_indebtedness Real)\n    (net_hedging_interest_payable Real)\n    (lease_interest_factor_estimate Real)\n  ) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n    (and\n      ; 5.03(a): Net Worth must not be less than $1,100,000,000\n      (>= net_worth 1100000000.0)\n      ; 5.03(b): Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio = Cash Flow / Fixed Charges must not be less than 1.30\n      ; Fixed Charges = interest_on_indebtedness + net_hedging_interest_payable + lease_interest_factor_estimate\n      ; Cash Flow = net_income + income_taxes + noncash_provisions_writeoffs + Fixed Charges\n      (>= (/ (+ net_income income_taxes noncash_provisions_writeoffs\n                (+ interest_on_indebtedness net_hedging_interest_payable lease_interest_factor_estimate))\n             (+ interest_on_indebtedness net_hedging_interest_payable lease_interest_factor_estimate))\n          1.30))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower; both tests apply only then.",
      "source_quote": "as at the end of any fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_worth",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Net Worth, in dollars, as at the fiscal quarter end (atomic; no definition supplied).",
      "source_quote": "The Borrower will not permit its Net Worth to be, as at the end of any fiscal quarter, less than $1,100,000,000"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_income",
      "meaning": "Net income of the Borrower and its consolidated Subsidiaries for the four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on or most recently ended prior to the observation day.",
      "source_quote": "net income"
    },
    {
      "name": "income_taxes",
      "meaning": "Income taxes of the Borrower and its consolidated Subsidiaries for the same four-quarter period.",
      "source_quote": "income taxes"
    },
    {
      "name": "noncash_provisions_writeoffs",
      "meaning": "Non-cash provisions for, or actual write-offs of, assets (without duplication in respect of any prior period) for the Borrower and its consolidated Subsidiaries for the same four-quarter period.",
      "source_quote": "non-cash provisions for, or actual write-offs of, assets"
    },
    {
      "name": "interest_on_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "All interest in respect of Indebtedness (including the interest component of Capital Lease Obligation payments) accrued or capitalized during the same four-quarter period, whether or not paid.",
      "source_quote": "all interest in respect of Indebtedness (including the interest component of any payments in respect of Capital Lease Obligations) accrued or capitalized during such period"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_hedging_interest_payable",
      "meaning": "Net amount payable under interest-related Hedging Agreements during the same four-quarter period, whether or not actually paid or received; negative if there is a net amount receivable.",
      "source_quote": "the net amount payable (or minus the net amount receivable) under Hedging Agreements relating to interest during such period"
    },
    {
      "name": "lease_interest_factor_estimate",
      "meaning": "Estimate of the portion of minimum rents under operating leases representing the interest factor, for the same four-quarter period.",
      "source_quote": "estimate of that portion of minimum rents under operating leases representing the interest factor"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Pointwise at fiscal quarter ends. Fixed Charges = Interest Expense + lease interest factor, where Interest Expense = interest_on_indebtedness + net_hedging_interest_payable. Cash Flow = net income + income taxes + non-cash provisions/write-offs + Fixed Charges. The ratio is computed by division, so a zero Fixed Charges value is reported as unresolved by the evaluator. No positivity assumptions are made. Net Worth is atomic because its definition is not supplied. The 'Until the Commitments ... paid in full' duration clause is treated as the period over which observations are supplied. The 1.30 to 1 ratio threshold is non-strict: a ratio below 1.30 breaches the covenant, and exactly 1.30 complies."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true exactly when the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; consolidated_adjusted_net_income: Consolidated Adjusted Net Income, calculated for the four fiscal quarters then ending (trailing four fiscal quarters ending on the observation date).\n; consolidated_interest_expense: Consolidated Interest Expense, calculated for the same four fiscal quarters then ending.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (consolidated_adjusted_net_income Real) (consolidated_interest_expense Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n      (>= (/ consolidated_adjusted_net_income consolidated_interest_expense) 3.0)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.",
      "source_quote": "as at the last day of each fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_adjusted_net_income",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Adjusted Net Income, calculated for the four fiscal quarters ending on the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Adjusted Net Income"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Expense, calculated for the same four fiscal quarters ending on the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Interest Expense"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant requires the ratio of Consolidated Adjusted Net Income to Consolidated Interest Expense to be not less than 3.0 to 1.0, so the comparison is non-strict (>=). It applies only at fiscal quarter-end, via the implication on is_fiscal_quarter_end. The ratio is kept as an explicit division because the source defines it that way. A zero interest expense is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the division is by a variable. The defined terms are kept as atomic Real inputs because their definitions are not supplied. The 'unless the Required Lenders shall otherwise consent in writing' waiver is not modelled because no consent-state input is needed for the pointwise check."
}

