  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; consolidated_ebitda: Consolidated EBITDA, as calculated for the period of the four prior consecutive fiscal quarters ending at the observation time (numerator (a) of the ratio).\n; consolidated_interest_expense: Consolidated Interest Expense, as calculated for the same four-prior-consecutive-fiscal-quarter period (denominator (b) of the ratio).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((consolidated_ebitda Real) (consolidated_interest_expense Real)) Bool\n  (not (< (/ consolidated_ebitda consolidated_interest_expense) 3.75)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "consolidated_ebitda",
      "meaning": "Consolidated EBITDA, as calculated for the period of the four prior consecutive fiscal quarters ending at the observation time (numerator (a) of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "(a) Consolidated EBITDA"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Expense, as calculated for the same four-prior-consecutive-fiscal-quarter period (denominator (b) of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "(b) Consolidated Interest Expense"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant prohibits permitting the ratio of Consolidated EBITDA to Consolidated Interest Expense to be less than 3.75 to 1.0. The formula is therefore the negation of ratio < 3.75, which is ratio >= 3.75 (exactly 3.75 complies). The covenant applies throughout the agreement's term, so there is no calendar flag and it is evaluated pointwise at each observation. The ratio is defined in the source as EBITDA divided by interest expense, so it is encoded as a division. A zero denominator is reported as unresolved by the evaluator, and no positivity is assumed. QF_NRA is used because the division has a variable denominator. The definitions of Consolidated EBITDA and Consolidated Interest Expense are not supplied, so they remain atomic Real inputs."
}

{"status":"formalized","smt2":"(set-logic QF_LRA)
(define-fun covenant_holds (
  (is_test_period_end_on_or_after_2004_12_31 Bool) ; true iff the observation is the last day of a Test Period that ends on or after December 31, 2004
  (fixed_charges_ratio Real) ; the Fixed Charges Ratio of MDC Partners as at the last day of the Test Period, expressed as a number x for x to 1.0
  ) Bool
  (=> is_test_period_end_on_or_after_2004_12_31 (>= fixed_charges_ratio 1.25)))","symbols":[{"name":"is_test_period_end_on_or_after_2004_12_31","meaning":"True iff the observation date is the last day of a Test Period ending on or after December 31, 2004.","source_quote":"as at the last day of any Test Period ending on or after December 31, 2004"},{"name":"fixed_charges_ratio","meaning":"The Fixed Charges Ratio of MDC Partners as at the last day of the Test Period, expressed as x in 'x to 1.0'.","source_quote":"MDC Partners will not permit the Fixed Charges Ratio to be less than 1.25 to 1.0"}],"notes":"The ratio is an atomic Real since its definition is not supplied. The covenant prohibits the ratio from being less than 1.25, so the requirement is >= 1.25 (non-strict). The lead-in condition (Advances unpaid, Commitments, or Letters of Credit or Bankers' Acceptances outstanding) is the covenant's duration, and it is not modeled as a separate input; the evaluator supplies observations within that period."}

