{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter: true iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Company\n; total_cash_balances: Company's Total Cash Balances as of the observation date\n; accounts_receivable: Company's Accounts Receivable as of the observation date\n; revolving_loans_principal: aggregate outstanding principal balance of Revolving Loans as of the observation date\n; letter_of_credit_outstandings: aggregate amount of Letter of Credit Outstandings as of the observation date\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter Bool) (total_cash_balances Real) (accounts_receivable Real) (revolving_loans_principal Real) (letter_of_credit_outstandings Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter\n      (>= (/ (+ total_cash_balances accounts_receivable)\n             (+ revolving_loans_principal letter_of_credit_outstandings))\n          1.25)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Company.",
      "source_quote": "as of the last day of any fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_cash_balances",
      "meaning": "The Company's Total Cash Balances as of the observation date (numerator component (i)).",
      "source_quote": "Total Cash Balances"
    },
    {
      "name": "accounts_receivable",
      "meaning": "The Company's Accounts Receivable as of the observation date (numerator component (i)).",
      "source_quote": "Accounts Receivable"
    },
    {
      "name": "revolving_loans_principal",
      "meaning": "Aggregate outstanding principal balance of Revolving Loans as of the observation date (denominator component (ii)).",
      "source_quote": "the aggregate outstanding principal balance of Revolving Loans"
    },
    {
      "name": "letter_of_credit_outstandings",
      "meaning": "Aggregate amount of Letter of Credit Outstandings as of the observation date (denominator component (ii)).",
      "source_quote": "the aggregate amount of Letter of Credit Outstandings"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant prohibits the ratio from being less than 1.25 to 1.0, so compliance is ratio >= 1.25 (non-strict), applied only when the observation is the last day of a fiscal quarter. The ratio is computed as (cash + AR) / (revolving loans + LC outstandings), as defined in the clause. A zero denominator is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved, with no positivity assumption. QF_NRA is used because the division is by a non-constant term. The waiver and commitment/obligation-outstanding preamble is not modeled as a separate input: the Majority Banks' waiver is a written event with no defined input, and the preamble is a standing condition of the Article rather than a numeric test."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; commitment_or_obligation_outstanding: true iff, at the observation, any Lender has a Commitment under the agreement or any Obligation remains unpaid or outstanding.\n; is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter: true iff the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter.\n; is_on_or_after_commencement_quarter: true iff the Fiscal Quarter ending on the observation date is the Fiscal Quarter ending June 30, 2003 or a later Fiscal Quarter.\n; fixed_charge_coverage_ratio: the Borrower's Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio as of the observation date, expressed as a number X for X:1.0 (1.25:1.0 is 1.25).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((commitment_or_obligation_outstanding Bool) (is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter Bool) (is_on_or_after_commencement_quarter Bool) (fixed_charge_coverage_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and commitment_or_obligation_outstanding\n           is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter\n           is_on_or_after_commencement_quarter)\n      (>= fixed_charge_coverage_ratio 1.25)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "commitment_or_obligation_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True iff, at the observation, any Lender has a Commitment under the agreement or any Obligation remains unpaid or outstanding.",
      "source_quote": "so long as any Lender has a Commitment hereunder or any Obligation remains unpaid or outstanding"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter.",
      "source_quote": "as of the last day of each Fiscal Quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_on_or_after_commencement_quarter",
      "meaning": "True iff the Fiscal Quarter ending on the observation date is the Fiscal Quarter ending June 30, 2003 or a later Fiscal Quarter.",
      "source_quote": "commencing with the Fiscal Quarter ending June 30, 2003"
    },
    {
      "name": "fixed_charge_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Borrower's Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio as of the observation date, as a number X for X:1.0 (1.25:1.0 is 1.25).",
      "source_quote": "a Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio of not less than 1.25:1.0"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies only when the Commitment/Obligation condition, the fiscal-quarter-end condition and the commencement condition all hold. When it applies, the ratio must be at least 1.25, so exactly 1.25 complies (non-strict inequality). Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio is kept as an atomic Real because its definition is not supplied. The evaluator supplies the calendar and event-state flags at each observation."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Company.\n; annualized_consolidated_cash_flow: Annualized Consolidated Cash Flow as at the end of the fiscal quarter, the numerator of the ratio (a).\n; annualized_consolidated_interest_expense: Annualized Consolidated Interest Expense as at the end of the same fiscal quarter, the denominator of the ratio (b).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (annualized_consolidated_cash_flow Real) (annualized_consolidated_interest_expense Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n      (not (< (/ annualized_consolidated_cash_flow annualized_consolidated_interest_expense) 2.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Company; the covenant is tested only then.",
      "source_quote": "as at the end of any fiscal quarter of the Company"
    },
    {
      "name": "annualized_consolidated_cash_flow",
      "meaning": "Annualized Consolidated Cash Flow as at the end of the fiscal quarter, the numerator (a) of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Annualized Consolidated Cash Flow as at the end of any fiscal quarter of the Company"
    },
    {
      "name": "annualized_consolidated_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Annualized Consolidated Interest Expense as at the end of the same fiscal quarter, the denominator (b) of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Annualized Consolidated Interest Expense as at the end of such fiscal quarter"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant forbids the ratio from being less than 2.0 to 1, so the compliant condition is ratio >= 2.0. The threshold is non-strict: a ratio of exactly 2.0 complies. The body states this as (not (< ratio 2.0)). The ratio is computed by direct division, so the logic is QF_NRA. A zero denominator is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. No positivity assumptions are added. The definitions of Annualized Consolidated Cash Flow and Annualized Consolidated Interest Expense are not supplied, so each is an atomic Real input. The opening lead-in about commitments and loans outstanding is the standing condition for all negative covenants. It is treated as part of the observation context and is not modeled as a separate input."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; lender_commitment_outstanding: true exactly when any Lender has any Commitment under the agreement at the observation time.\n; loan_or_obligation_unpaid: true exactly when any Loan or other Obligation remains unpaid or unsatisfied at the observation time, excluding contingent indemnification obligations.\n; debt_to_cap_ratio: the Consolidated Total Debt to Capitalization Ratio as of the observation date, as a Real (1.00 means 1 to 1).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (lender_commitment_outstanding Bool) (loan_or_obligation_unpaid Bool) (debt_to_cap_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end\n           (or lender_commitment_outstanding loan_or_obligation_unpaid))\n      (<= debt_to_cap_ratio 0.75)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True exactly when the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.",
      "source_quote": "as of the end of any fiscal quarter of the Borrower"
    },
    {
      "name": "lender_commitment_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True exactly when any Lender has any Commitment under the agreement at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "so long as any Lender shall have any Commitment hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "loan_or_obligation_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True exactly when any Loan or other Obligation remains unpaid or unsatisfied at the observation time, excluding contingent indemnification obligations.",
      "source_quote": "any Loan or other Obligation (other than contingent indemnification obligations) hereunder shall remain unpaid or unsatisfied"
    },
    {
      "name": "debt_to_cap_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Consolidated Total Debt to Capitalization Ratio as of the observation date, as an atomic Real (1.00 means 1 to 1).",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Total Debt to Capitalization Ratio"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies only at a fiscal quarter end while either a Commitment is outstanding or a non-excluded Loan or Obligation is unpaid. The ratio must not be greater than 0.75 to 1.00, so the check is <= 0.75, and exactly 0.75 complies. No definition of the ratio is supplied, so it stays an atomic Real input. No division occurs in the formula."
}

{
