{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; leverage_ratio: The Leverage Ratio of the Company as of the observation date (to be read as x to 1.0, so 3.5 means 3.5 to 1.0).\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: True iff the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter of the Company.\n; acquisition_closing_occurred: True iff the observation date is on or after the Acquisition Closing Date. False means the date is before it, so the pre-Acquisition limits apply.\n; pre_first_quarter_reached: True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the first Fiscal Quarter after the Effective Date (pre-Acquisition clause (i)).\n; pre_fifth_quarter_reached: True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the fifth full Fiscal Quarter following December 18, 2013 (pre-Acquisition clause (ii)).\n; qualified_acquisition_window: True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is one of the four Fiscal Quarters after a Fiscal Quarter in which a Qualified Acquisition has occurred.\n; post_first_quarter_reached: True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the first full Fiscal Quarter after the Acquisition Closing Date (post-Acquisition clause (i)).\n; post_sep2015_reached: True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the Fiscal Quarter ended on or about September 30, 2015 (post-Acquisition clause (ii)).\n; post_mar2016_reached: True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the Fiscal Quarter ended on or about March 31, 2016 (post-Acquisition clause (iii)).\n; post_sep2016_reached: True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the Fiscal Quarter ended on or about September 30, 2016 (post-Acquisition clause (iv)).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((leverage_ratio Real)\n                            (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool)\n                            (acquisition_closing_occurred Bool)\n                            (pre_first_quarter_reached Bool)\n                            (pre_fifth_quarter_reached Bool)\n                            (qualified_acquisition_window Bool)\n                            (post_first_quarter_reached Bool)\n                            (post_sep2015_reached Bool)\n                            (post_mar2016_reached Bool)\n                            (post_sep2016_reached Bool)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n    (ite (not acquisition_closing_occurred)\n      (and\n        (=> pre_first_quarter_reached (<= leverage_ratio 3.5))\n        (=> pre_fifth_quarter_reached\n            (<= leverage_ratio (ite qualified_acquisition_window 3.5 3.25))))\n      (and\n        (=> post_first_quarter_reached (<= leverage_ratio 5.25))\n        (=> post_sep2015_reached (<= leverage_ratio 4.5))\n        (=> post_mar2016_reached\n            (<= leverage_ratio (ite qualified_acquisition_window 4.0 3.75)))\n        (=> post_sep2016_reached\n            (<= leverage_ratio (ite qualified_acquisition_window 4.0 3.5)))))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Leverage Ratio of the Company as of the observation date, expressed as x to 1.0.",
      "source_quote": "the Company will not permit the Leverage Ratio to exceed 3.5 to 1.0"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of a Fiscal Quarter of the Company.",
      "source_quote": "as of the last day of any such Fiscal Quarter of the Company"
    },
    {
      "name": "acquisition_closing_occurred",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is on or after the Acquisition Closing Date. False means the pre-Acquisition limits apply.",
      "source_quote": "The following will apply on and after the Acquisition Closing Date"
    },
    {
      "name": "pre_first_quarter_reached",
      "meaning": "True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the first Fiscal Quarter after the Effective Date (pre-Acquisition clause (i)).",
      "source_quote": "beginning with the first Fiscal Quarter after the Effective Date"
    },
    {
      "name": "pre_fifth_quarter_reached",
      "meaning": "True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the fifth full Fiscal Quarter following December 18, 2013 (pre-Acquisition clause (ii)).",
      "source_quote": "beginning with the fifth full Fiscal Quarter following December 18, 2013"
    },
    {
      "name": "qualified_acquisition_window",
      "meaning": "True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is one of the four Fiscal Quarters after a Fiscal Quarter in which a Qualified Acquisition has occurred.",
      "source_quote": "during the four Fiscal Quarters after a Fiscal Quarter in which a Qualified Acquisition has occurred"
    },
    {
      "name": "post_first_quarter_reached",
      "meaning": "True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the first full Fiscal Quarter after the Acquisition Closing Date (post-Acquisition clause (i)).",
      "source_quote": "beginning with the first full Fiscal Quarter after the Acquisition Closing Date"
    },
    {
      "name": "post_sep2015_reached",
      "meaning": "True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the Fiscal Quarter ended on or about September 30, 2015 (post-Acquisition clause (ii)).",
      "source_quote": "beginning with the Fiscal Quarter ended on or about September 30, 2015"
    },
    {
      "name": "post_mar2016_reached",
      "meaning": "True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the Fiscal Quarter ended on or about March 31, 2016 (post-Acquisition clause (iii)).",
      "source_quote": "beginning with the Fiscal Quarter ended on or about March 31, 2016"
    },
    {
      "name": "post_sep2016_reached",
      "meaning": "True iff the observed Fiscal Quarter is on or after the Fiscal Quarter ended on or about September 30, 2016 (post-Acquisition clause (iv)).",
      "source_quote": "beginning with the Fiscal Quarter ended on or about September 30, 2016"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The clauses within each regime are cumulative, so each active clause is enforced separately. Pre-Acquisition clause (ii) uses 3.5 instead of 3.25 during a Qualified Acquisition window. Post-Acquisition clauses (iii) and (iv) use 4.0 during a Qualified Acquisition window; clauses (i) and (ii) have no such increase. Compliance is checked only at fiscal quarter ends, which are the dates the covenant tests. The temporal flags are evaluator-supplied calendar inputs. The Effective Date and Acquisition Closing Date are not given as dates, so they are represented through those flags."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; commitments_not_terminated: True at this observation if the Commitments have not yet terminated.\n; letters_of_credit_outstanding: True at this observation if any Letter of Credit has not yet terminated or expired.\n; loans_and_amounts_unpaid: True at this observation if principal and interest on the Loans, Reimbursement Obligations, or fees, expenses and other amounts then due and owing have not been paid in full in cash.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: True if this observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter.\n; consolidated_indebtedness: Consolidated Indebtedness of the Borrower as of the observation date (currency units).\n; total_capitalization: Total Capitalization of the Borrower as of the observation date (same currency units).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((commitments_not_terminated Bool) (letters_of_credit_outstanding Bool) (loans_and_amounts_unpaid Bool) (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (consolidated_indebtedness Real) (total_capitalization Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and (or commitments_not_terminated letters_of_credit_outstanding loans_and_amounts_unpaid) is_fiscal_quarter_end)\n      (<= (/ consolidated_indebtedness total_capitalization) 0.30)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "commitments_not_terminated",
      "meaning": "True at this observation if the Commitments have not yet terminated.",
      "source_quote": "Until the termination of the Commitments"
    },
    {
      "name": "letters_of_credit_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True at this observation if any Letter of Credit has not yet terminated or expired.",
      "source_quote": "the termination or expiration of all Letters of Credit"
    },
    {
      "name": "loans_and_amounts_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True at this observation if principal and interest on the Loans, Reimbursement Obligations, or fees, expenses and other amounts then due and owing have not been paid in full in cash.",
      "source_quote": "the payment in full in cash of all principal and interest with respect to the Loans and all Reimbursement Obligations together with all fees, expenses and other amounts then due and owing hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True if the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter.",
      "source_quote": "as of the last day of any fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_indebtedness",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Indebtedness of the Borrower as of the observation date (currency units); the numerator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "The ratio of Consolidated Indebtedness to Total Capitalization"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "Total Capitalization of the Borrower as of the observation date (same currency units); the denominator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "The ratio of Consolidated Indebtedness to Total Capitalization"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies while any of the three termination or payment conditions remains unsatisfied. This is an OR of the 'not yet' states, because the covenant ends only once all conditions are met. At a fiscal quarter end during that period, the ratio must be at most 0.30 (0.30 to 1.0). 'Not greater than' is encoded as <=. The ratio is computed as a division, so a zero Total Capitalization is left for the evaluator to report as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the divisor is a variable. Consolidated Indebtedness and Total Capitalization are kept as atomic inputs because their definitions are not supplied."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; is_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter, when the ratio is calculated.\n; commitment_in_effect: true iff the Commitment is in effect at the observation time.\n; note_outstanding: true iff the Note is outstanding at the observation time.\n; cash_flow_to_total_borrowed_funds_ratio: ratio of Cash Flow to Total Borrowed Funds, calculated at the observation quarter end on a trailing four quarter basis (the four consecutive quarters ending then), as a pure number (e.g. 0.30).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_quarter_end Bool) (commitment_in_effect Bool) (note_outstanding Bool) (cash_flow_to_total_borrowed_funds_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and is_quarter_end (or commitment_in_effect note_outstanding))\n      (>= cash_flow_to_total_borrowed_funds_ratio 0.30)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the end of a fiscal quarter, when the ratio is calculated.",
      "source_quote": "such ratio to be calculated at the end of each quarter on a trailing four quarter basis"
    },
    {
      "name": "commitment_in_effect",
      "meaning": "True iff the Commitment is in effect at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "So long as the Commitment shall be in effect or the Note is outstanding"
    },
    {
      "name": "note_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True iff the Note is outstanding at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "So long as the Commitment shall be in effect or the Note is outstanding"
    },
    {
      "name": "cash_flow_to_total_borrowed_funds_ratio",
      "meaning": "Ratio of Cash Flow to Total Borrowed Funds, calculated at the observation quarter end on a trailing four quarter basis, as a pure number.",
      "source_quote": "The ratio of Cash Flow to Total Borrowed Funds shall not be less than .30"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies while the Commitment is in effect OR the Note is outstanding, and the ratio is tested at each quarter end. 'Not less than .30' is encoded as >= 0.30. The ratio is kept atomic because the source does not define Cash Flow or Total Borrowed Funds, so no division is needed. The trailing four quarter basis is part of how the evaluator computes the input, so the formula only compares the supplied ratio with 0.30."
}

{
