  "notes": "Both tests are applied only at Fiscal Quarter end. The leverage maximum is 4.25 by default, 4.00 from the quarter ending June 30, 2014, and 3.50 from the quarter ending June 30, 2015. The leverage test is non-strict (<=) because the Company may not permit the ratio to 'exceed' the limit. The interest coverage test is non-strict (>=) because the ratio may not be 'less than' 3.00. Ratios are atomic inputs because their definitions are not supplied. The lead-in conditions about Commitments, Letters of Credit and payment in full are the period during which the covenant applies. They are not modelled as inputs, since the evaluator supplies observations only within that period."
