{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; required_lenders_written_consent: True if the Required Lenders have consented in writing to otherwise than the covenants applying at this observation.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: True if the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Company.\n; is_on_or_after_2012_02_29: True if the fiscal quarter ending on the observation date ends on or after February 29, 2012.\n; indebtedness_for_borrowed_money: Indebtedness For Borrowed Money of the Company and its consolidated Subsidiaries as of the last day of the fiscal quarter, in currency units, excluding undrawn amounts in respect of Facility LCs.\n; ebitda_ttm: EBITDA actual amount for the four-quarter period ending on the observation date, in currency units, pro forma for Permitted Acquisitions as the source requires.\n; ebit_ttm: EBIT actual amount for the four-quarter period ending on the observation date, in currency units, pro forma for Permitted Acquisitions as the source requires.\n; interest_expense_ttm: Interest Expense actual amount for the four-quarter period ending on the observation date, in currency units, pro forma for Permitted Acquisitions as the source requires.\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n  (required_lenders_written_consent Bool)\n  (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool)\n  (is_on_or_after_2012_02_29 Bool)\n  (indebtedness_for_borrowed_money Real)\n  (ebitda_ttm Real)\n  (ebit_ttm Real)\n  (interest_expense_ttm Real)) Bool\n  (or required_lenders_written_consent\n      (=> (and is_fiscal_quarter_end is_on_or_after_2012_02_29)\n          (and (<= (/ indebtedness_for_borrowed_money ebitda_ttm) 3.5)\n               (>= (/ ebit_ttm interest_expense_ttm) 2.5)))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "required_lenders_written_consent",
      "meaning": "True if the Required Lenders have consented in writing to otherwise than the covenants applying at this observation.",
      "source_quote": "unless the Required Lenders shall otherwise consent in writing"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True if the observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Company.",
      "source_quote": "as of the end of each fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_on_or_after_2012_02_29",
      "meaning": "True if the fiscal quarter ending on the observation date ends on or after February 29, 2012.",
      "source_quote": "ending on or after February 29, 2012"
    },
    {
      "name": "indebtedness_for_borrowed_money",
      "meaning": "Indebtedness For Borrowed Money of the Company and its consolidated Subsidiaries as of the last day of the fiscal quarter, in currency units, excluding undrawn amounts in respect of Facility LCs.",
      "source_quote": "Indebtedness For Borrowed Money of the Company and its consolidated Subsidiaries (excluding any undrawn amounts in respect of Facility LCs)"
    },
    {
      "name": "ebitda_ttm",
      "meaning": "EBITDA actual amount for the four-quarter period ending on the observation date, in currency units, pro forma for Permitted Acquisitions as the source requires.",
      "source_quote": "the actual amount for the four-quarter period ending on such day"
    },
    {
      "name": "ebit_ttm",
      "meaning": "EBIT actual amount for the four-quarter period ending on the observation date, in currency units, pro forma for Permitted Acquisitions as the source requires.",
      "source_quote": "EBIT to (ii) Interest Expense"
    },
    {
      "name": "interest_expense_ttm",
      "meaning": "Interest Expense actual amount for the four-quarter period ending on the observation date, in currency units, pro forma for Permitted Acquisitions as the source requires.",
      "source_quote": "actual amount of EBIT and Interest Expense for the four-quarter period ending on such day"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Both ratios are tested only at fiscal quarter ends ending on or after February 29, 2012. The Leverage Ratio (debt / EBITDA) must not be greater than 3.50, so it is encoded as <= 3.5. The Interest Expense Coverage Ratio (EBIT / Interest Expense) must be at least 2.50, so it is encoded as >= 2.5. Division by a zero denominator is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the denominators are variables. The Required Lenders' written consent is modeled as a Boolean exception. The pro forma treatment of Permitted Acquisitions is part of how the input figures are defined and is not enforced in the formula."
