{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; commitment_or_loan_outstanding: true if, at the observation time, any Commitment or Loan is outstanding and amounts payable by the Company hereunder have not been paid in full.\n; period_ends_on_or_after_2011_04_02: true if the four-consecutive-fiscal-quarter period being tested ends on or after April 2, 2011.\n; ebitda: EBITDA of the Company for the four-consecutive-fiscal-quarter period ending at the observation (numerator of the ratio, as defined in the agreement).\n; net_interest_expense: Net Interest Expense of the Company for the same four-fiscal-quarter period (denominator of the ratio, as defined in the agreement).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((commitment_or_loan_outstanding Bool) (period_ends_on_or_after_2011_04_02 Bool) (ebitda Real) (net_interest_expense Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and commitment_or_loan_outstanding period_ends_on_or_after_2011_04_02)\n      (>= (/ ebitda net_interest_expense) 3.0)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "commitment_or_loan_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True if, at the observation time, any Commitment or Loan is outstanding and amounts payable by the Company hereunder have not been paid in full.",
      "source_quote": "so long as any Commitment or Loan is outstanding and until payment in full of all amounts payable by the Company hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "period_ends_on_or_after_2011_04_02",
      "meaning": "True if the four-consecutive-fiscal-quarter period being tested ends on or after April 2, 2011.",
      "source_quote": "for any period for four consecutive fiscal quarters ending on or after April 2, 2011"
    },
    {
      "name": "ebitda",
      "meaning": "EBITDA of the Company for the four-consecutive-fiscal-quarter period ending at the observation (numerator of the ratio, as defined in the agreement).",
      "source_quote": "EBITDA"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_interest_expense",
      "meaning": "Net Interest Expense of the Company for the same four-fiscal-quarter period (denominator of the ratio, as defined in the agreement).",
      "source_quote": "Net Interest Expense"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant requires the ratio of EBITDA to Net Interest Expense not to be less than 3.0 to 1.0, so the compliant condition is ratio >= 3.0 (non-strict). The ratio is written as division, which requires QF_NRA because the denominator is a variable. If Net Interest Expense is zero, the evaluator reports the result as unresolved, per the stated policy. No sign or positivity assumptions are added. The two Boolean applicability flags are supplied by the evaluator and appear separately in the antecedent of the implication. EBITDA and Net Interest Expense remain atomic inputs because their definitions are not supplied."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; total_debt: Total Debt of the Company at the observation time, as defined in the Agreement (definition not supplied), in the same currency units as total_capital.\n; total_capital: Total Capital of the Company at the observation time, as defined in the Agreement (definition not supplied), in the same currency units as total_debt.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((total_debt Real) (total_capital Real)) Bool\n  (<= (/ total_debt total_capital) 0.6))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "total_debt",
      "meaning": "Total Debt of the Company at the observation time, as defined in the Agreement (definition not supplied), in the same currency units as total_capital. It is the numerator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Total Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_capital",
      "meaning": "Total Capital of the Company at the observation time, as defined in the Agreement (definition not supplied), in the same currency units as total_debt. It is the denominator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Total Capital"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Section 6.08 says 'at any time', so it is encoded pointwise with no calendar applicability flag: the ratio of Total Debt to Total Capital must be at most 0.60 to 1 at every observation. 'Not exceed' makes the bound non-strict (<= 0.6). The ratio is computed as total_debt / total_capital. Because the denominator is a variable, the logic is QF_NRA. A zero Total Capital is reported by the evaluator as unresolved, and no positivity assumption is made. The definitions of Total Debt and Total Capital are not in the supplied context, so they stay as atomic Real inputs. The covenant's lead-in (Commitments in effect and Loans unpaid) is the standing period of the agreement, and the evaluator supplies observations only within it."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; tangible_net_worth: Borrower's Tangible Net Worth on a stand-alone basis at the observation time, in US dollars.\n; ebitda_coverage_ratio: Borrower's EBITDA Coverage Ratio on a stand-alone basis, calculated on a rolling four fiscal quarter basis as of the observation date (a ratio, where 1.0 means 1.0 to 1.0).\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the last day of one of Borrower's fiscal quarters.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((tangible_net_worth Real) (ebitda_coverage_ratio Real) (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool)) Bool\n  (and\n    (>= tangible_net_worth 2000000.0)\n    (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (>= ebitda_coverage_ratio 1.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Tangible Net Worth on a stand-alone basis at the observation time, in US dollars.",
      "source_quote": "a Tangible Net Worth of not less than $2,000,000"
    },
    {
      "name": "ebitda_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Borrower's EBITDA Coverage Ratio on a stand-alone basis, calculated on a rolling four fiscal quarter basis as of the observation date (1.0 means 1.0 to 1.0).",
      "source_quote": "calculated on a rolling four (4) fiscal quarter basis"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last day of one of Borrower's fiscal quarters.",
      "source_quote": "as of the last day of each of its fiscal quarters"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Clause (a) applies at every observation (pointwise 'at all times'), so the Tangible Net Worth minimum is unconditional. Clause (b) applies only when is_fiscal_quarter_end is true. Both thresholds are 'not less than', so the comparisons are non-strict (>=). The EBITDA Coverage Ratio is an atomic input because its arithmetic definition is not supplied; it is understood to be computed on a rolling four fiscal quarter basis. The 'tested quarterly' sentence is covered by the quarter-end flag. The lender-consent exception and the term of the covenant are not modeled as inputs, since the covenant is evaluated only at observations within the covenant period."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; interest_coverage_ratio: Interest Coverage Ratio of the Borrowers and their respective subsidiaries on a combined basis, for the four consecutive fiscal quarter periods ending on the observation date (three consecutive fiscal quarters if the observation date is 6/30/2000). Atomic Real; its definition is not supplied.\n; is_test_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is a fiscal quarter ending date on which the covenant's ratio determination is made.\n; is_on_or_after_2000_06_30: true iff the observation date is on or after 6/30/2000 (the first listed Quarter Ending).\n; is_on_or_before_final_maturity_date: true iff the observation date is on or before the Final Maturity Date (inclusive).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((interest_coverage_ratio Real) (is_test_quarter_end Bool) (is_on_or_after_2000_06_30 Bool) (is_on_or_before_final_maturity_date Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and is_test_quarter_end is_on_or_after_2000_06_30 is_on_or_before_final_maturity_date)\n      (>= interest_coverage_ratio 2.5)))",
