      "meaning": "True iff Borrower has received prior written consent to the contrary from Administrative Agent as authorized by Determining Lenders, covering this covenant at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "UNLESS Borrower receives a prior written consent to the contrary by Administrative Agent as authorized by Determining Lenders"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_debt",
      "meaning": "Total Debt of the Restricted Companies, calculated on a consolidated basis, at the date of determination, in currency units. Its definition is not supplied, so it is an atomic input.",
      "source_quote": "As calculated on a consolidated basis for the Restricted Companies"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "Total Capitalization of the Restricted Companies, calculated on a consolidated basis, at the date of determination, in the same currency units. Its definition is not supplied, so it is an atomic input.",
      "source_quote": "the ratio of Total Debt to Total Capitalization"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant is applied pointwise at each date of determination (\"on any date of determination\"). The ratio is Total Debt / Total Capitalization, and the limit is non-strict (<= 0.68, since the ratio must not exceed 0.68 to 1.00). A zero Total Capitalization makes the division unresolved under the evaluator policy, and no positivity assumption is added. The covenant period and the consent exception come from the lead-in of Section 7. The covenant is enforced only when the observation is on or after the Closing Date, Lenders are still committed or amounts remain unpaid, and no consent has been received."
}

{
