    },
    {
      "name": "total_liabilities",
      "meaning": "Total Liabilities as of the observation date (numerator of the leverage ratio).",
      "source_quote": "Total Liabilities"
    },
    {
      "name": "tangible_net_worth",
      "meaning": "Tangible Net Worth as of the observation date (denominator of the leverage ratio).",
      "source_quote": "Tangible Net Worth"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio Total Liabilities / Tangible Net Worth must be at most 0.60 to 1.0 (non-strict, since the breach condition is 'more than 0.60 to 1.0'). It is tested only at fiscal quarter-ends. The division is kept literally, so a zero Tangible Net Worth is reported by the evaluator as unresolved. No sign assumptions are made. Because division by a variable is nonlinear, the logic is QF_NRA. Total Liabilities and Tangible Net Worth are left as atomic inputs because the source gives no definitions for them."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; credit_exposure_outstanding: true iff at this observation any Lender has any Credit Exposure under the agreement.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff this observation date is the last day of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; consolidated_total_indebtedness: Consolidated Total Indebtedness of the Borrower as of this observation date (numerator of the ratio).\n; consolidated_capitalization: Consolidated Capitalization of the Borrower as of this observation date (denominator of the ratio).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((credit_exposure_outstanding Bool) (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (consolidated_total_indebtedness Real) (consolidated_capitalization Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and credit_exposure_outstanding is_fiscal_quarter_end)\n      (<= (/ consolidated_total_indebtedness consolidated_capitalization) 0.65)))",
