{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; in_restriction_period: true at observations during the period commencing on the Closing Date and continuing through Bank Facility Termination.\n; cumulative_share_repurchases: cumulative aggregate dollar amount of Share Repurchases made by MCRI from the Closing Date through the observation time.\n; has_quarter_end_since_closing: true if at least one Fiscal Quarter end following the Closing Date has occurred at or before the observation time, so a Leverage Ratio has been determined.\n; min_quarter_end_leverage_ratio: lowest Leverage Ratio (Borrower, ratio to 1.00) determined as of any Fiscal Quarter end following the Closing Date, up to the observation time. Ignored if has_quarter_end_since_closing is false.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((in_restriction_period Bool) (cumulative_share_repurchases Real) (has_quarter_end_since_closing Bool) (min_quarter_end_leverage_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> in_restriction_period\n      (or (and has_quarter_end_since_closing (< min_quarter_end_leverage_ratio 1.75))\n          (<= cumulative_share_repurchases 5000000.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "in_restriction_period",
      "meaning": "True at observations during the period commencing on the Closing Date and continuing through Bank Facility Termination.",
      "source_quote": "during the period commencing on the Closing Date and continuing through Bank Facility Termination"
    },
    {
      "name": "cumulative_share_repurchases",
      "meaning": "Cumulative aggregate dollar amount of Share Repurchases made by MCRI from the Closing Date through the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "the MCRI shall not make Share Repurchases in excess of the cumulative aggregate amount of Five Million Dollars ($5,000,000.00)"
    },
    {
      "name": "has_quarter_end_since_closing",
      "meaning": "True if at least one Fiscal Quarter end following the Closing Date has occurred at or before the observation time, so a Leverage Ratio has been determined.",
      "source_quote": "determined as of any Fiscal Quarter end following the Closing Date"
    },
    {
      "name": "min_quarter_end_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Lowest Leverage Ratio (to 1.00) of Borrower determined as of any Fiscal Quarter end following the Closing Date, up to the observation time. Ignored if there has been no such quarter end.",
      "source_quote": "Borrower achieves a Leverage Ratio determined as of any Fiscal Quarter end following the Closing Date, less than 1.75 to 1.00"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Pointwise reading: during the restriction period, cumulative repurchases must be at most $5,000,000, unless the Stock Repurchase Limitation Release has occurred. The release means some Fiscal Quarter end after the Closing Date had a Leverage Ratio strictly below 1.75. Because the release is permanent ('no further force or effect'), the history-dependent minimum leverage ratio is supplied as an input and compared with the strict 1.75 threshold in the formula. 'In excess of' makes the $5,000,000 cap inclusive (<=). The Leverage Ratio is treated as an atomic Real because its definition is not supplied."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; reserve_report_delivered: true at an observation where a Reserve Report is delivered pursuant to Section 4.9(b), so Section 7.2(j) applies.\n; schedule_delivered_with_report: true if a schedule is delivered together with that Reserve Report. The schedule sets forth the location and filing information of the recorded Mortgages and the PV-10 Value of the Borrowing Base Properties, and demonstrates the Collateral Coverage Ratio.\n; collateral_coverage_ratio: the Collateral Coverage Ratio at this observation, as x in 'x to 1.0'. It is an atomic Real because no arithmetic definition is supplied.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((reserve_report_delivered Bool) (schedule_delivered_with_report Bool) (collateral_coverage_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> reserve_report_delivered\n      (and schedule_delivered_with_report\n           (>= collateral_coverage_ratio 1.5))))",
  "symbols": [
