{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; consolidated_total_funded_debt: US Borrower's Consolidated Total Funded Debt at the observation date (end of the Fiscal Quarter), in currency units.\n; total_capitalization: US Borrower's Total Capitalization at the same observation date, in the same currency units.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the end of a Fiscal Quarter.\n; fiscal_quarter_ends_on_or_before_2002_06_30: true iff the Fiscal Quarter ending at this observation ends on or before June 30, 2002; false if it ends after June 30, 2002.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((consolidated_total_funded_debt Real) (total_capitalization Real) (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (fiscal_quarter_ends_on_or_before_2002_06_30 Bool)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n      (ite fiscal_quarter_ends_on_or_before_2002_06_30\n           (<= (/ consolidated_total_funded_debt total_capitalization) 0.70)\n           (<= (/ consolidated_total_funded_debt total_capitalization) 0.65))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "consolidated_total_funded_debt",
      "meaning": "US Borrower's Consolidated Total Funded Debt at the observation date (end of the Fiscal Quarter), in currency units; the numerator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Total Funded Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "US Borrower's Total Capitalization at the same observation date, in the same currency units; the denominator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Total Capitalization"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the end of a Fiscal Quarter, so the ratio test applies.",
      "source_quote": "at the end of any Fiscal Quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "fiscal_quarter_ends_on_or_before_2002_06_30",
      "meaning": "True iff the Fiscal Quarter ending at this observation ends on or before June 30, 2002 (70% limit applies); false if it ends after June 30, 2002 (65% limit applies).",
      "source_quote": "at the end of any Fiscal Quarter ending on or before June 30, 2002"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio is computed as debt divided by capitalization, so a zero denominator is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. The limits are non-strict (<=), matching 'will not exceed': 0.70 for quarters ending on or before June 30, 2002 and 0.65 for later quarters. The test applies only at Fiscal Quarter ends. QF_NRA is used because the division by a variable is nonlinear."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_quarter_end: true iff the observation date is the end of a quarter of a fiscal year of the relevant Borrower\n; is_energy_borrower: true iff the Borrower tested at this observation is Energy\n; is_oncor_borrower: true iff the Borrower tested at this observation is Oncor\n; consolidated_senior_debt: the Borrower's Consolidated Senior Debt at the observation date (as defined in the agreement)\n; consolidated_total_capitalization: the Borrower's Consolidated Total Capitalization at the observation date (as defined in the agreement)\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_quarter_end Bool) (is_energy_borrower Bool) (is_oncor_borrower Bool) (consolidated_senior_debt Real) (consolidated_total_capitalization Real)) Bool\n  (and\n    (=> (and is_quarter_end is_energy_borrower)\n        (<= (/ consolidated_senior_debt consolidated_total_capitalization) 0.60))\n    (=> (and is_quarter_end is_oncor_borrower)\n        (<= (/ consolidated_senior_debt consolidated_total_capitalization) 0.65))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the end of a quarter of a fiscal year of the Borrower being tested.",
      "source_quote": "as of the end of each quarter of each fiscal year of such Borrower"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_energy_borrower",
      "meaning": "True iff the Borrower tested at this observation is Energy, so the 0.60 to 1.00 limit applies.",
      "source_quote": "in the case of Energy"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_oncor_borrower",
      "meaning": "True iff the Borrower tested at this observation is Oncor, so the 0.65 to 1.00 limit applies.",
      "source_quote": "in the case of Oncor"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_senior_debt",
      "meaning": "The tested Borrower's Consolidated Senior Debt as of the observation date, the numerator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Senior Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "The tested Borrower's Consolidated Total Capitalization as of the observation date, the denominator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Total Capitalization"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The ratio is Consolidated Senior Debt divided by Consolidated Total Capitalization. It must not be greater than the limit, so the test is <=: 0.60 for Energy and 0.65 for Oncor. Each limit applies only at quarter-end observations for the matching Borrower. Division by zero is left to the evaluator to report as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the denominator is a variable. The Article V preamble (commitments outstanding and similar conditions) is treated as the general period in which the covenants apply and is not modeled as a separate input."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; adjusted_ebitda: Borrower's Adjusted EBITDA for the fiscal quarter being tested (numerator of the ratio of Adjusted EBITDA to Fixed Charges), in the same currency units as fixed_charges. The source does not define it further.\n; fixed_charges: Borrower's Fixed Charges for the same fiscal quarter (denominator of the ratio), in the same currency units. The source does not define it further.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((adjusted_ebitda Real) (fixed_charges Real)) Bool\n  (>= (/ adjusted_ebitda fixed_charges) 1.75))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "adjusted_ebitda",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Adjusted EBITDA for the fiscal quarter being tested; the numerator of the Adjusted EBITDA to Fixed Charges ratio, in the same currency units as fixed_charges. The source does not define it further.",
      "source_quote": "Adjusted EBITDA to Fixed Charges"
    },
    {
      "name": "fixed_charges",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Fixed Charges for the same fiscal quarter; the denominator of the ratio, in the same currency units as adjusted_ebitda. The source does not define it further.",
      "source_quote": "Fixed Charges"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant prohibits a ratio of Adjusted EBITDA to Fixed Charges below 1.75 to 1.0, so compliance means ratio >= 1.75 (the threshold itself is compliant). The ratio is computed as adjusted_ebitda / fixed_charges. Because the denominator is a variable, the logic is QF_NRA. Division by zero is reported by the evaluator as unresolved, per the stated policy. The 'at any time ... for any fiscal quarter' wording is handled pointwise: each observation supplies the figures for the fiscal quarter tested. No calendar flag is added because the source gives no separate applicability condition. Definitions of Adjusted EBITDA and Fixed Charges are not supplied, so both remain atomic Real inputs."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; obligations_outstanding: true at the observation time if any Lender has any Commitment, or any Loan, Committed Loan Note, Competitive Bid Loan Note or other Borrower obligation under the Agreement/Loan Documents remains unpaid or unperformed (the period during which Article VI applies).\n; agent_written_consent: true at the observation time if the Agent, with the consent of the Majority Lenders, has otherwise consented in writing to non-compliance with Section 6.14.\n; total_debt: Total Debt on a consolidated basis for the Borrower and its Subsidiaries: all Indebtedness for borrowed money (including subordinated and convertible debt and commercial paper), plus Indebtedness or liability for borrowed money or the deferred purchase price of property or services for which the Borrower or any Subsidiary is contingently or directly liable, or against which it assures a creditor against loss. Currency units.\n; shareholders_equity: the Borrower's shareholders' equity on a consolidated basis, in the same currency units. Capitalization = total_debt + shareholders_equity.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((obligations_outstanding Bool) (agent_written_consent Bool) (total_debt Real) (shareholders_equity Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and obligations_outstanding (not agent_written_consent))\n      (<= (/ total_debt (+ total_debt shareholders_equity)) 0.55)))",
