{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; bank_has_commitment: true iff, at the observation time, any Bank has any Commitment under the agreement.\n; note_amount_unpaid: true iff, at the observation time, any amount payable under any Note remains unpaid.\n; leverage_ratio: the Company's Leverage Ratio at the observation time, as a number (3.50 means 3.50 to 1.00).\n; interest_coverage_ratio: the Company's Interest Coverage Ratio at the observation time, as a number (3.00 means 3.00 to 1.00).\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n  (bank_has_commitment Bool)\n  (note_amount_unpaid Bool)\n  (leverage_ratio Real)\n  (interest_coverage_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> (or bank_has_commitment note_amount_unpaid)\n      (and (<= leverage_ratio 3.5)\n           (>= interest_coverage_ratio 3.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "bank_has_commitment",
      "meaning": "True iff, at the observation time, any Bank has any Commitment under the agreement.",
      "source_quote": "any Bank has any Commitment hereunder"
    },
    {
      "name": "note_amount_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True iff, at the observation time, any amount payable under any Note remains unpaid.",
      "source_quote": "any amount payable under any Note remains unpaid"
    },
    {
      "name": "leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Company's Leverage Ratio at the observation time, as a number (3.50 means 3.50 to 1.00). It is an atomic input because the source gives no definition.",
      "source_quote": "the Leverage Ratio at any time to exceed 3.50 to 1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "interest_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Company's Interest Coverage Ratio at the observation time, as a number (3.00 means 3.00 to 1.00). It is an atomic input because the source gives no definition.",
      "source_quote": "the Interest Coverage Ratio at any time to be less than 3.00 to 1.00"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenants apply so long as any Bank has any Commitment OR any Note amount remains unpaid, so the two conditions are joined with OR. Section 5.07(a) prohibits the Leverage Ratio exceeding 3.50, so the compliant condition is <= 3.5. Section 5.07(b) prohibits the Interest Coverage Ratio being less than 3.00, so the compliant condition is >= 3.0. Both ratios are atomic inputs because the source gives no formulas. 'At any time' is handled pointwise: each observation is checked, and the evaluator conjoins the results. Both clauses are conjoined under the same applicability condition."
}

