{"status":"formalized","smt2":"(set-logic QF_LRA)
(define-fun covenant_holds (
  (is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) ; True if the observation date is a fiscal quarter end of the Borrower (Section 8.2: "as of any fiscal quarter end")
  (balance_sheet_leverage_ratio Real) ; Balance Sheet Leverage Ratio as of the observation date, expressed as a number X meaning X to 1.00 (e.g. 0.30 means 0.30 to 1.00)
) Bool
  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end (<= balance_sheet_leverage_ratio 0.30)))","symbols":[{"name":"is_fiscal_quarter_end","meaning":"True if the observation date is a fiscal quarter end of the Borrower, the only time at which the ratio test applies.","source_quote":"as of any fiscal quarter end"},{"name":"balance_sheet_leverage_ratio","meaning":"The Balance Sheet Leverage Ratio as of the observation date, expressed as a number X meaning X to 1.00 (0.30 means 0.30 to 1.00). Treated as an atomic input since its definition is not supplied.","source_quote":"the Balance Sheet Leverage Ratio to exceed 0.30 to 1.00"}],"notes":"The covenant prohibits permitting the ratio to exceed 0.30:1.00 at a fiscal quarter end, so compliance is ratio <= 0.30 (non-strict) when the quarter-end flag is true. The 'until payment in full' preamble is the covenant's duration; it is treated as the period over which observations are supplied, not as a separate input. The ratio's definition is not provided, so it is kept atomic."}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; cash_flow: Borrower's Cash Flow for the most recently completed four fiscal quarters as of the date of determination (numerator of the ratio).\n; fixed_charges: Borrower's Fixed Charges for the same most recently completed four fiscal quarters (denominator of the ratio).\n; any_lender_committed: true iff, at the observation date, any Lender is committed to lend or issue LCs under this agreement.\n; obligation_not_fully_paid: true iff, at the observation date, the Obligation has not yet been fully paid and performed.\n; consent_obtained: true iff Administrative Agent has given written notice of Determining Lenders' consent to the contrary for this covenant at the observation date.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((cash_flow Real) (fixed_charges Real) (any_lender_committed Bool) (obligation_not_fully_paid Bool) (consent_obtained Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and (or any_lender_committed obligation_not_fully_paid)\n           (not consent_obtained))\n      (>= (/ cash_flow fixed_charges) 1.25)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "cash_flow",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Cash Flow for the most recently completed four fiscal quarters as of the date of determination (numerator of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "of Cash Flow to Fixed Charges"
    },
    {
      "name": "fixed_charges",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Fixed Charges for the same most recently completed four fiscal quarters (denominator of the ratio).",
      "source_quote": "of Cash Flow to Fixed Charges"
    },
    {
      "name": "any_lender_committed",
      "meaning": "True iff, at the observation date, any Lender is committed to lend or issue LCs under this agreement.",
      "source_quote": "any Lender is committed to lend or issue LCs under this agreement"
    },
    {
      "name": "obligation_not_fully_paid",
      "meaning": "True iff, at the observation date, the Obligation has not yet been fully paid and performed.",
      "source_quote": "until the Obligation has been fully paid and performed"
    },
    {
      "name": "consent_obtained",
      "meaning": "True iff Administrative Agent has given written notice of Determining Lenders' consent to the contrary for this covenant at the observation date.",
      "source_quote": "written notice of Determining Lenders' consent to the contrary"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant forbids the ratio of Cash Flow to Fixed Charges from ever being less than 1.25 to 1.00, so compliance is ratio >= 1.25 (a ratio exactly equal to 1.25 complies). It is applied pointwise at each date of determination, with no calendar flag since it applies as of any date. The covenant period is modeled as active while any Lender is committed OR the Obligation is unpaid, because it ends only once both conditions have ceased. The consent exception disables the requirement. Division is left as (/ cash_flow fixed_charges), so QF_NRA is used; a zero Fixed Charges value is reported as unresolved by the evaluator, and no positivity assumptions are made. The definitions of Cash Flow and Fixed Charges are not supplied, so they remain atomic inputs."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; debt_to_capitalization_ratio: The Debt to Capitalization Ratio of the Borrower at the observation time, as an atomic Real (definition not supplied), expressed as a ratio to 1.00.\n; aggregate_commitment_expired_or_terminated: True iff the Aggregate Commitment has expired or been terminated at the observation time.\n; all_loans_and_fees_paid_in_full: True iff the principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees payable hereunder have been paid in full at the observation time. Indemnities and other contingent obligations not then due and payable and as to which no claim has been made are excluded.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((debt_to_capitalization_ratio Real) (aggregate_commitment_expired_or_terminated Bool) (all_loans_and_fees_paid_in_full Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (not (and aggregate_commitment_expired_or_terminated all_loans_and_fees_paid_in_full))\n      (<= debt_to_capitalization_ratio 0.6)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "debt_to_capitalization_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Debt to Capitalization Ratio of the Borrower at the observation time, as an atomic Real (definition not supplied), expressed as a ratio to 1.00.",
      "source_quote": "The Borrower will not permit the Debt to Capitalization Ratio at any time to exceed 0.60 to 1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "aggregate_commitment_expired_or_terminated",
      "meaning": "True iff the Aggregate Commitment has expired or been terminated at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "Until the Aggregate Commitment has expired or been terminated"
    },
    {
      "name": "all_loans_and_fees_paid_in_full",
      "meaning": "True iff the principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees payable hereunder have been paid in full at the observation time. Indemnities and other contingent obligations not then due and payable and as to which no claim has been made are excluded.",
      "source_quote": "the principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees payable hereunder have been paid in full (other than indemnities and other contingent obligations not then due and payable and as to which no claim has been made)"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies until BOTH the Aggregate Commitment has expired or been terminated AND the Loans and fees have been paid in full, so it is active whenever either condition is not yet met. While active, the ratio must not exceed 0.60 (0.60 to 1.00 = 0.6), so the check is non-strict (<=). The 'at any time' clause is translated pointwise over the supplied observations. The ratio is kept atomic because its definition is not supplied, so there is no division in the formula."
