  "notes": "The covenant is applicable at fiscal quarter-end observations on or after April 30, 2000. When applicable, the Interest Coverage Ratio (EBITDDA divided by combined interest expense) must be at least 2.75 (the 'not less than 2.75 to 1.0' threshold, non-strict). EBITDDA is kept as its stated arithmetic definition: net income excluding extraordinary items plus the five add-backs. The add-back interest expense and the denominator's combined interest expense (which includes capitalized interest and the capital lease interest portion) are separate inputs because the source defines them differently. A zero denominator is left for the evaluator to report as unresolved, so QF_NRA is used. The Article 7 lead-in (so long as Commitments, Loans or Letters of Credit remain, unless the Majority Banks waive in writing) is not modeled. Waivers and the outstanding-obligation status are not given as inputs, and the evaluator is assumed to supply observations only while the covenant is in force."
