  "notes": "The Leverage Ratio is an atomic input because its definition is not supplied. The maximum is inclusive, because the covenant prohibits a ratio 'greater than' the limit. Borrowing dates require both the before and after ratios to meet the limit. The covenant applies only while commitments or obligations are outstanding and no written waiver from the Majority Banks exists. The period flags are supplied by the evaluator and are expected to be mutually exclusive."
