{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; event_of_default_8_2_for_6_9: true iff an Event of Default under Section 8.2 has occurred as a result of the Borrowers' failure to comply with Section 6.9.\n; agent_appraisal_obtained: true iff the Agent has obtained an Appraisal with respect to each Facility included in the Collateral.\n; appraisal_ltv_ratio: LTV Ratio (as a plain number, 0.667:1.00 = 0.667) based on that Appraisal.\n; five_business_days_elapsed: true iff at this observation five Business Days have elapsed since any Borrower obtained knowledge of the Appraisal-based LTV Ratio.\n; post_cure_ltv_ratio: LTV Ratio at this observation after giving effect to any prepayment of Credit Loans or grant of additional or substituted Eligible Healthcare Assets liens.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((event_of_default_8_2_for_6_9 Bool) (agent_appraisal_obtained Bool) (appraisal_ltv_ratio Real) (five_business_days_elapsed Bool) (post_cure_ltv_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (=> (and event_of_default_8_2_for_6_9\n           agent_appraisal_obtained\n           (> appraisal_ltv_ratio 0.667)\n           five_business_days_elapsed)\n      (<= post_cure_ltv_ratio 0.667)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "event_of_default_8_2_for_6_9",
      "meaning": "True iff an Event of Default under Section 8.2 has occurred as a result of the Borrowers' failure to comply with Section 6.9.",
      "source_quote": "Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default arising under Section 8.2 as a result of the Borrowers' failure to comply with Section 6.9"
    },
    {
      "name": "agent_appraisal_obtained",
      "meaning": "True iff the Agent has obtained an Appraisal with respect to each Facility included in the Collateral.",
      "source_quote": "obtain an Appraisal with respect to each Facility included in the Collateral"
    },
    {
      "name": "appraisal_ltv_ratio",
      "meaning": "LTV Ratio based on the Agent-obtained Appraisal, as a plain number (0.667:1.00 = 0.667).",
      "source_quote": "the LTV Ratio is greater than 0.667:1.00"
    },
    {
      "name": "five_business_days_elapsed",
      "meaning": "True iff at this observation five Business Days have elapsed since any Borrower obtained knowledge of the Appraisal-based LTV Ratio exceeding 0.667.",
      "source_quote": "within five (5) Business Days of any of the Borrowers obtaining knowledge thereof"
    },
    {
      "name": "post_cure_ltv_ratio",
      "meaning": "LTV Ratio at this observation after giving effect to any prepayment of Credit Loans or grant of a first Lien on additional or substituted Eligible Healthcare Assets, as a plain number.",
      "source_quote": "such that after giving effect to such prepayment or such grant, the LTV Ratio shall again be equal to or less than 0.667:1.000"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Formalizes the quantitative obligation of Section 6.2(b). Once the Section 8.2/6.9 Event of Default has occurred, an Appraisal is obtained, and the Appraisal LTV exceeds 0.667 (strict), the Borrowers must restore the LTV to at most 0.667 (non-strict) by the end of the five-Business-Day period. The pointwise reading applies this requirement at observations on or after that deadline. Prepayment and lien-grant mechanics are captured through the post-cure LTV input, since either route yields the same required outcome. Section 6.2(a) (access, inspection and audit rights, and who bears expense) is a non-numeric access covenant and is not encoded. The lead-in about outstanding Commitments is treated as the general duration of the covenant."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end: true iff this observation is as of the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower.\n; pv10: PV10 of the Borrower's and its Subsidiaries' proved Oil and Gas Properties as of the end of the fiscal quarter, based on the most recent Reserve Report delivered pursuant to Section 8.07.\n; consolidated_net_debt: Consolidated Net Debt as of the end of the fiscal quarter.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_fiscal_quarter_end Bool) (pv10 Real) (consolidated_net_debt Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_fiscal_quarter_end\n      (>= (/ pv10 consolidated_net_debt) 2.0)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation is as of the end of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower (the quarterly test date).",
      "source_quote": "as of the end of any fiscal quarter of the Borrower"
    },
    {
      "name": "pv10",
      "meaning": "PV10 of the Borrower's and its Subsidiaries' proved Oil and Gas Properties as of the end of the fiscal quarter, based on the most recent Reserve Report delivered pursuant to Section 8.07. This is the numerator of the PV10 Ratio.",
      "source_quote": "PV10 for the Borrower and its Subsidiaries proved Oil and Gas Properties as of the end of such fiscal quarter based on the most recent Reserve Report delivered pursuant to Section 8.07"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_net_debt",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Net Debt as of the end of the fiscal quarter. This is the denominator of the PV10 Ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Net Debt as of the end of such fiscal quarter"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The PV10 Ratio is defined in the source as PV10 divided by Consolidated Net Debt, so the formula keeps the division. If consolidated_net_debt is zero, the evaluator reports the result as unresolved. The covenant forbids a ratio 'less than 2.00 to 1.00', so compliance is ratio >= 2.0 (non-strict). The test applies only at fiscal quarter end, via the is_fiscal_quarter_end flag. QF_NRA is used because the division is by a variable. The source's lead-in about the Commitments being in effect and the Required Lenders' consent is not modeled as an input. Under pointwise semantics, the evaluator supplies observations only while the covenant is in force."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; is_month_end: true iff the observation date is a month-end, the test date for the ratio (\"at any prior month-end\").\n; consolidated_total_debt: Consolidated Total Debt of the Borrower and its Subsidiaries at this month-end, in currency units (numerator of the ratio).\n; consolidated_total_capitalization: Consolidated Total Capitalization at this month-end, in the same currency units (denominator of the ratio).\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_month_end Bool) (consolidated_total_debt Real) (consolidated_total_capitalization Real)) Bool\n  (=> is_month_end (<= (/ consolidated_total_debt consolidated_total_capitalization) 0.45)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_month_end",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is a month-end, which is when the ratio is tested.",
      "source_quote": "month-end"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_total_debt",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Total Debt at the observed month-end, in currency units. It is the numerator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Total Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_total_capitalization",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Total Capitalization at the observed month-end, in the same currency units. It is the denominator of the ratio.",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Total Capitalization"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant forbids the ratio from exceeding 0.45:1, so the compliant condition is ratio <= 0.45, and exactly 0.45 complies. The test applies only at month-end observations, so the body is an implication on is_month_end. The ratio is written as an explicit division, so a zero capitalization is reported as unresolved by the evaluator, and no positivity is assumed. The 'So long as any Lender shall have any Commitment...' lead-in is treated as the standing condition under which the covenant applies at every observation, and no separate input is added for it. The word 'prior' in 'at any prior month-end' is treated as referring to the month-end observation points in the supplied history."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; interest_coverage_ratio: Borrower's Interest Coverage Ratio at the observation time, measured on a rolling four (4) quarter basis, expressed as a multiple X in 'X to 1.00'. Taken as an atomic input because the source gives no arithmetic definition.\n; rlc_note_unpaid: true iff the RLC Note remains unpaid at the observation time.\n; rlc_outstanding: true iff the RLC is outstanding at the observation time.\n; lender_written_consent: true iff the Lender has otherwise consented in writing, at the observation time, to the Borrower not complying with the Interest Coverage Ratio requirement.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((interest_coverage_ratio Real) (rlc_note_unpaid Bool) (rlc_outstanding Bool) (lender_written_consent Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and (or rlc_note_unpaid rlc_outstanding) (not lender_written_consent))\n      (>= interest_coverage_ratio 5.0)))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "interest_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Borrower's Interest Coverage Ratio at the observation time, measured on a rolling four (4) quarter basis, expressed as X in 'X to 1.00'. Atomic input because no arithmetic definition is supplied.",
      "source_quote": "Interest Coverage Ratio of not less than 5.00 to 1.00 measured on a rolling four(4) quarter basis"
    },
    {
      "name": "rlc_note_unpaid",
      "meaning": "True iff the RLC Note remains unpaid at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "So long as the RLC Note shall remain unpaid or the RLC shall be outstanding"
    },
    {
      "name": "rlc_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True iff the RLC is outstanding at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "So long as the RLC Note shall remain unpaid or the RLC shall be outstanding"
    },
    {
      "name": "lender_written_consent",
      "meaning": "True iff the Lender has otherwise consented in writing, at the observation time, to the Borrower not complying with the Interest Coverage Ratio requirement.",
      "source_quote": "unless the Lender shall otherwise consent in writing"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenant applies while the RLC Note is unpaid OR the RLC is outstanding, unless the Lender has consented in writing. The ratio must be at least 5.00 (not less than, so >=). 'At all times' is evaluated pointwise at each observation. The rolling four-quarter measurement is reflected in the meaning of the ratio input, since its arithmetic definition is not given."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; on_or_after_closing_date: true iff the observation time is on or after the Closing Date.\n; total_commitment_terminated: true iff the Total Commitment has been terminated at the observation time.\n; notes_outstanding: true iff any Notes remain outstanding at the observation time.\n; obligations_paid_in_full: true iff the Loans and Swingline Loans, together with interest, Fees and all other Obligations under the Agreement and the other Credit Documents, have been paid in full.\n; total_funded_debt_to_ebitda_ratio: the Total Funded Debt to EBITDA Ratio at the observation time (x to 1.0).\n; senior_funded_debt_to_ebitda_ratio: the Senior Funded Debt to EBITDA Ratio at the observation time (x to 1.0).\n; interest_coverage_ratio: the Interest Coverage Ratio at the observation time (x to 1.0).\n; net_worth: the Borrowers' Net Worth in US dollars at the observation time.\n; cumulative_net_income: Cumulative Net Income in US dollars before the $0 floor. It is the consolidated net income of the Borrowers and their Subsidiaries from December 31, 2004 through the end of the fiscal quarter for which Net Worth is calculated.\n; is_fiscal_quarter_end_on_or_after_2005_03_31: true iff the observation is the last day of a fiscal quarter that is March 31, 2005 or later.\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n    (on_or_after_closing_date Bool)\n    (total_commitment_terminated Bool)\n    (notes_outstanding Bool)\n    (obligations_paid_in_full Bool)\n    (total_funded_debt_to_ebitda_ratio Real)\n    (senior_funded_debt_to_ebitda_ratio Real)\n    (interest_coverage_ratio Real)\n    (net_worth Real)\n    (cumulative_net_income Real)\n    (is_fiscal_quarter_end_on_or_after_2005_03_31 Bool)) Bool\n  (=> (and on_or_after_closing_date\n           (not (and total_commitment_terminated\n                     (not notes_outstanding)\n                     obligations_paid_in_full)))\n      (and (<= total_funded_debt_to_ebitda_ratio 3.75)\n           (<= senior_funded_debt_to_ebitda_ratio 3.25)\n           (>= interest_coverage_ratio 3.0)\n           (>= net_worth\n               (+ 200000000.0\n                  (ite is_fiscal_quarter_end_on_or_after_2005_03_31\n                       (* 0.4 (ite (< cumulative_net_income 0.0) 0.0 cumulative_net_income))\n                       0.0))))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "on_or_after_closing_date",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation time is on or after the Closing Date, when the covenants begin to apply.",
      "source_quote": "on the Closing Date and thereafter"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_commitment_terminated",
      "meaning": "True iff the Total Commitment has been terminated at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "the Total Commitment has been terminated"
    },
    {
      "name": "notes_outstanding",
      "meaning": "True iff any Notes remain outstanding at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "no Notes remain outstanding"
    },
    {
      "name": "obligations_paid_in_full",
      "meaning": "True iff the Loans and Swingline Loans, together with interest, Fees and all other Obligations under the Agreement and the other Credit Documents, have been paid in full.",
      "source_quote": "the Loans and Swingline Loans, together with interest, Fees and all other Obligations incurred hereunder and under the other Credit Documents, have been paid in full"
    },
    {
      "name": "total_funded_debt_to_ebitda_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Total Funded Debt to EBITDA Ratio at the observation time, as x in 'x to 1.0'. Its definition is not supplied, so it is an atomic input.",
      "source_quote": "Total Funded Debt to EBITDA Ratio to exceed 3.75 to 1.0"
    },
    {
      "name": "senior_funded_debt_to_ebitda_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Senior Funded Debt to EBITDA Ratio at the observation time, as x in 'x to 1.0'. Its definition is not supplied, so it is an atomic input.",
      "source_quote": "Senior Funded Debt to EBITDA Ratio to exceed 3.25 to 1.0"
    },
    {
      "name": "interest_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Interest Coverage Ratio at the observation time, as x in 'x to 1.0'. Its definition is not supplied, so it is an atomic input.",
      "source_quote": "Interest Coverage Ratio to be less than 3.0 to 1.0"
    },
    {
      "name": "net_worth",
      "meaning": "The Borrowers' Net Worth in US dollars at the observation time.",
      "source_quote": "The Borrowers will not permit the Net Worth to be less than $200,000,000"
    },
    {
      "name": "cumulative_net_income",
      "meaning": "Cumulative Net Income in US dollars before the $0 floor. It is the consolidated net income of the Borrowers and their Subsidiaries from December 31, 2004 through the end of the fiscal quarter for which Net Worth is calculated. The formula applies the floor.",
      "source_quote": "from December 31, 2004 through the end of the fiscal quarter for which the calculation of Net Worth is being made"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_fiscal_quarter_end_on_or_after_2005_03_31",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation is the last day of a fiscal quarter that is March 31, 2005 or later. The 40% Cumulative Net Income addition to the Net Worth floor applies only then.",
      "source_quote": "commencing March 31, 2005 and as of the end of each fiscal quarter thereafter"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The covenants apply from the Closing Date until the Total Commitment is terminated, no Notes remain outstanding, and all Obligations are paid in full. The termination period is therefore decomposed into separate Boolean inputs. The ratio tests are evaluated pointwise, matching 'at any time': Total Funded Debt ratio <= 3.75, Senior Funded Debt ratio <= 3.25, and Interest Coverage ratio >= 3.0 (violated only if strictly less than 3.0). The Net Worth floor is $200,000,000 plus 40% of Cumulative Net Income, with Cumulative Net Income floored at $0. The addition applies only at fiscal quarter-ends on or after March 31, 2005. At other times, the floor is read as $200,000,000 alone. The source is ambiguous about the floor between quarter-ends and before March 31, 2005, and this is the literal reading. The ratios are atomic inputs because their definitions are not supplied. No division is performed."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter: true iff the observation date is the last date of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower\n; consolidated_leverage_ratio: Consolidated Leverage Ratio as at the last day of the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Borrower ending on the observation date\n; maximum_leverage_ratio: the Maximum Leverage Ratio (defined term, applicable level) in effect for the observation date\n; consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio: Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio for the period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Borrower ending on the observation date (3.0 to 1.0 is encoded as 3.0)\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter Bool) (consolidated_leverage_ratio Real) (maximum_leverage_ratio Real) (consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio Real)) Bool\n  (and\n    ; 6.1(g): leverage ratio must not exceed the Maximum Leverage Ratio\n    (=> is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter (<= consolidated_leverage_ratio maximum_leverage_ratio))\n    ; 6.1(h): interest coverage ratio must not be less than 3.0\n    (=> is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter (>= consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio 3.0))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "is_last_day_of_fiscal_quarter",
      "meaning": "True iff the observation date is the last date of a fiscal quarter of the Borrower; both tests apply only then.",
      "source_quote": "As of the last date of each fiscal quarter"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Leverage Ratio as at the last day of the four-consecutive-fiscal-quarter period of the Borrower ending on the observation date (atomic Real; definition not supplied).",
      "source_quote": "the Consolidated Leverage Ratio as at the last day of any period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Borrower ending on such date"
    },
    {
      "name": "maximum_leverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "The Maximum Leverage Ratio (defined term whose level is not given in the source) applicable on the observation date, supplied by the evaluator.",
      "source_quote": "to exceed the Maximum Leverage Ratio"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_interest_coverage_ratio",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio for the four-consecutive-fiscal-quarter period of the Borrower ending on the observation date, expressed as a number (3.0 means 3.0 to 1.0); atomic Real.",
      "source_quote": "the Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio for any period of four consecutive fiscal quarters of the Borrower ending on such date to be less than 3.0 to 1.0"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Both covenants are prohibitions on permitting a breach, so compliance is leverage <= Maximum Leverage Ratio (exceeding is the breach, so equality complies) and interest coverage >= 3.0 (below 3.0 is the breach, so equality complies). Each applies only at fiscal quarter end, and the two are conjoined. The Maximum Leverage Ratio is a defined term whose level is not in the source, so it is an externally supplied Real input. The ratios are atomic inputs because their definitions are not supplied. No division occurs in the formula."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_LRA)\n; commitments_expired_or_terminated: True iff the Commitments have expired or been terminated at this observation.\n; obligations_paid_in_full: True iff principal of and interest on each Loan and all fees, expenses and other amounts payable under this Agreement or any other Loan Document have been paid in full at this observation; contingent amounts not yet due are excluded.\n; letters_of_credit_resolved_and_disbursements_reimbursed: True iff all Letters of Credit have expired, terminated, or been backstopped or cash collateralized in a manner reasonably satisfactory to the applicable Issuing Bank, and all LC Disbursements have been reimbursed, at this observation.\n; is_spin_off_consummation: True iff this observation is the consummation of the Spin-Off, when the Spin-Off must have been consummated lawfully and consistently with the Form 10.\n; spin_off_lawful_and_consistent_with_form10: True iff the Spin-Off is consummated in accordance with applicable law in all material respects and consistent with the information in the Form 10 (as in effect three Business Days prior to the Effective Date).\n; is_immediately_after_spin_off: True iff this observation is immediately after giving effect to the Spin-Off.\n; cash_and_cash_equivalents_usd: Cash and Cash Equivalents (as defined in the Separation Agreement) held by the Borrower and the Restricted Subsidiaries, in US dollars, after applying the adjustment procedures in the Separation Agreement.\n; is_spin_off_date: True iff this observation is at the Spin-Off Date, by which the Spin-Off Documents must already have been delivered.\n; true_complete_spin_off_documents_provided: True iff the Borrower has provided the Administrative Agent with true and complete copies of the Spin-Off Documents prior to the Spin-Off Date.\n; has_material_adverse_form10_modification: True iff the Spin-Off Documents contain a modification from the Form 10 information that is material and adverse to the Lenders, excluding placeholder information such as the distribution ratio, the date of any DuPont Distribution and record dates.\n; form10_modification_has_admin_agent_prior_written_consent: True iff the Administrative Agent gave prior written consent to the material and adverse modification from the Form 10.\n; has_material_adverse_waiver_or_amendment: True iff any term or condition of the Spin-Off Documents has been waived, amended or otherwise modified in a manner material and adverse to the rights or interests of the Lenders.\n; waiver_or_amendment_has_admin_agent_prior_written_consent: True iff the Administrative Agent gave prior written consent (not to be unreasonably withheld, conditioned or delayed) to that material and adverse waiver, amendment or modification.\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n    (commitments_expired_or_terminated Bool)\n    (obligations_paid_in_full Bool)\n    (letters_of_credit_resolved_and_disbursements_reimbursed Bool)\n    (is_spin_off_consummation Bool)\n    (spin_off_lawful_and_consistent_with_form10 Bool)\n    (is_immediately_after_spin_off Bool)\n    (cash_and_cash_equivalents_usd Real)\n    (is_spin_off_date Bool)\n    (true_complete_spin_off_documents_provided Bool)\n    (has_material_adverse_form10_modification Bool)\n    (form10_modification_has_admin_agent_prior_written_consent Bool)\n    (has_material_adverse_waiver_or_amendment Bool)\n    (waiver_or_amendment_has_admin_agent_prior_written_consent Bool)\n  ) Bool\n  (let ((covenant_period_over\n          (and commitments_expired_or_terminated\n               obligations_paid_in_full\n               letters_of_credit_resolved_and_disbursements_reimbursed)))\n    (or covenant_period_over\n        (and\n          (=> is_spin_off_consummation spin_off_lawful_and_consistent_with_form10)\n          (=> is_immediately_after_spin_off (>= cash_and_cash_equivalents_usd 200000000.0))\n          (=> is_spin_off_date true_complete_spin_off_documents_provided)\n          (=> has_material_adverse_form10_modification form10_modification_has_admin_agent_prior_written_consent)\n          (=> has_material_adverse_waiver_or_amendment waiver_or_amendment_has_admin_agent_prior_written_consent)))))",
