{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; total_senior_funded_debt: Total Senior Funded Debt at the date of determination, in dollars, as used in clauses (x) and (y) of the ratio.\n; subordinated_debt: Subordinated Debt (total, before any exclusion) at the date of determination, in dollars.\n; kti_series_b_subordinated_debt: Aggregate principal amount, in dollars, of Subordinated Debt issued by KTI in redemption or conversion of its Series B Preferred Stock. The formula caps the amount excluded from the numerator at 24,100,000.\n; consolidated_equity: Consolidated Equity at the date of determination, in dollars, used in the denominator (y).\n; is_period_through_june_30_1999: True iff the four-fiscal-quarter period preceding the date of determination is a period through June 30, 1999, so the .60 limit applies.\n; is_period_ending_on_or_after_july_1_1999: True iff the four-fiscal-quarter period preceding the date of determination ends on or after July 1, 1999, so the .55 limit applies.\n(define-fun covenant_holds (\n  (total_senior_funded_debt Real)\n  (subordinated_debt Real)\n  (kti_series_b_subordinated_debt Real)\n  (consolidated_equity Real)\n  (is_period_through_june_30_1999 Bool)\n  (is_period_ending_on_or_after_july_1_1999 Bool)) Bool\n  (and\n    (=> is_period_through_june_30_1999\n        (<= (/ (- (+ total_senior_funded_debt subordinated_debt)\n                  (ite (<= kti_series_b_subordinated_debt 24100000.0) kti_series_b_subordinated_debt 24100000.0))\n               (+ consolidated_equity total_senior_funded_debt subordinated_debt))\n            0.60))\n    (=> is_period_ending_on_or_after_july_1_1999\n        (<= (/ (- (+ total_senior_funded_debt subordinated_debt)\n                  (ite (<= kti_series_b_subordinated_debt 24100000.0) kti_series_b_subordinated_debt 24100000.0))\n               (+ consolidated_equity total_senior_funded_debt subordinated_debt))\n            0.55))))",
  "symbols": [
    {
      "name": "total_senior_funded_debt",
      "meaning": "Total Senior Funded Debt at the date of determination, in dollars, used in both the numerator (x) and the denominator (y).",
      "source_quote": "Total Senior Funded Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "subordinated_debt",
      "meaning": "Total Subordinated Debt at the date of determination, in dollars, before any exclusion. It is used in both the numerator (x) and the denominator (y).",
      "source_quote": "Subordinated Debt"
    },
    {
      "name": "kti_series_b_subordinated_debt",
      "meaning": "Aggregate principal amount, in dollars, of Subordinated Debt issued by KTI in redemption or conversion of its Series B Preferred Stock. Up to $24,100,000 of it is excluded from the numerator (x) only.",
      "source_quote": "Subordinated Debt issued by KTI in redemption or conversion of its Series B Preferred Stock"
    },
    {
      "name": "consolidated_equity",
      "meaning": "Consolidated Equity at the date of determination, in dollars, used in the denominator (y).",
      "source_quote": "Consolidated Equity"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_period_through_june_30_1999",
      "meaning": "True iff the four-fiscal-quarter period preceding the date of determination is a period through June 30, 1999, so the .60 maximum applies.",
      "source_quote": ".60 for the period through June 30, 1999"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_period_ending_on_or_after_july_1_1999",
      "meaning": "True iff the four-fiscal-quarter period preceding the date of determination ends on or after July 1, 1999, so the .55 maximum applies.",
      "source_quote": ".55 for periods ending on or after July 1, 1999"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Ratio = (Total Senior Funded Debt + Subordinated Debt - min(KTI Series B subordinated debt, 24,100,000)) / (Consolidated Equity + Total Senior Funded Debt + Subordinated Debt). The KTI exclusion applies only to the numerator, as the source states 'only for purposes of the calculation in this clause (x)'. The covenant forbids a ratio greater than the limit, so compliance is ratio <= limit, with non-strict comparisons. Each limit is guarded by its own period flag. A zero denominator is left for the evaluator to report as unresolved. QF_NRA is used because the division has a non-constant denominator. The Article 6 lead-in about Subsidiary Borrowers is not modeled, since it needs entity-level context that the source does not supply."
}

{
  "status": "formalized",
  "smt2": "(set-logic QF_NRA)\n; total_liabilities: The REIT's Total Liabilities at the observation time (numerator of the ratio).\n; gross_asset_value: The REIT's Gross Asset Value at the observation time (denominator of the ratio).\n; is_quarterly_measurement_observation: True iff this observation is a quarterly measurement of compliance, based on the financial statements delivered to Agent pursuant to Section 7.1.\n; is_prior_to_april_1_1997: True iff the observation date is prior to April 1, 1997.\n; is_april_1_1997_to_march_31_1998: True iff the observation date is in the period from April 1, 1997 to March 31, 1998.\n; is_after_march_31_1998: True iff the observation date is after March 31, 1998.\n(define-fun covenant_holds ((total_liabilities Real) (gross_asset_value Real) (is_quarterly_measurement_observation Bool) (is_prior_to_april_1_1997 Bool) (is_april_1_1997_to_march_31_1998 Bool) (is_after_march_31_1998 Bool)) Bool\n  (=> is_quarterly_measurement_observation\n    (and\n      (=> is_prior_to_april_1_1997 (<= (/ total_liabilities gross_asset_value) 0.70))\n      (=> is_april_1_1997_to_march_31_1998 (<= (/ total_liabilities gross_asset_value) 0.67))\n      (=> is_after_march_31_1998 (<= (/ total_liabilities gross_asset_value) 0.65)))))",
